PVD("philippines_ndp_2011-2016",{"docs":["","PDP 2011 2016"],"s":{"1":[[1,"220","11","National Cyber Security Plan","Formulating a National Cyber Security Plan; strengthening enforcement mechanisms for cybercrime detection, investigation and prosecution; and forging multilateral and bilateral agreements on cyber security;",""],[1,"220","11","Cybercrime Enforcement Mechanism Strengthening","strengthening enforcement mechanisms for cybercrime detection, investigation and prosecution;",""],[1,"220","11","Cyber Security Cooperation Agreements","forging multilateral and bilateral agreements on cyber security;",""],[1,"284","9","Cybersecurity Law Enactment","Enactment of law strengthening security and capability against cyberattacks, cybercrimes, cyberterrorism, and cyberwarfare",""],[1,"289","5","National Cybersecurity Program","the government will formulate a National Cybersecurity Program, which will include, among others, the development of a National Cybersecurity Plan and implementation of a government-wide systems and networks security management program.",""],[1,"289","10","National Cybersecurity Program","the government will formulate a National Cybersecurity Program, which will include, among others, the development of a National Cybersecurity Plan.",""]],"2":[[1,"186","6","Government ICT Systems Harmonization","Harmonize government information and communications technology (ICT) systems;",""],[1,"188","2","Government Human Resource Information System Completion","the government will complete its Government Human Resource Information System (GHRIS)",""],[1,"188","2","National Payroll System Development","develop a National Payroll System (NPS)",""],[1,"188","4","Medium-Term Information and Communication Technology Harmonization Initiative","The government will continue to implement the Medium-Term Information and Communication Technology Harmonization Initiative (MITHI).",""]],"3":[[1,"67","12","Local Government Revenue Mobilization and Fiscal Administration Reform","To this end, the DOF, through the BLGF and in partnership with LGUs, will strive to increase locally sourced revenues.","DOF | BLGF | LGUs"],[1,"68","1","Strengthening of LGU Debt Monitoring Systems","LGUs including the strengthening of LGU debt monitoring systems.",""],[1,"68","1","LGU Income Re-classification System Bill","The DOF will also pursue the passage of important legislative proposals, such as the LGU Income Re-classification System Bill and the proposed Valuation Reform Act.","DOF"],[1,"68","1","Valuation Reform Act","The DOF will also pursue the passage of important legislative proposals, such as the LGU Income Re-classification System Bill and the proposed Valuation Reform Act.","DOF"],[1,"68","2","GOCC Dividend Collection and Government Asset Disposition","With the passage of RA 10149 or the GOCC Governance Act of 2011,12 the Governance Commission on GOCCs (GCG) will help ensure the sustained dividend collection from GOCCs.","Governance Commission on GOCCs (GCG)"],[1,"329","11","Local Government Income Reclassification Reform","A legislative proposal that seeks to establish updated, rationalized and transparent processes for the income re-classification of provinces, cities and municipalities by amending EO 249, issued on July 25, 1987.",""],[1,"339","2","Local Government Decentralization and Autonomy Reform","An act providing for a local government code which seeks to promote genuine and meaningful local autonomy for territorial and political subdivisions of the State to enable them to attain their fullest development as self-reliant communities and make them more effective partners in the attainment of national goals.",""]],"4":[[1,"50","4","Citizen Access to Information and Participation Mechanism","The Plan aims for effective and efficient governance by empowering citizens with access to information and venues for participation",""],[1,"50","4","Public Service Accountability Improvement","as well as by providing high-quality public services where service providers are held accountable for the quality and efficiency of services delivered",""],[1,"50","4","Anti-Corruption Efforts","Intensifying anti-corruption efforts will continue to be a key strategy",""],[1,"50","5","Participatory Planning, Budgeting, and Civic Participation Support","strategies will aim to deepen participatory planning and budgeting, monitoring and evaluation (M&E), support community and civil society organization participation, and enhance voter's education.",""],[1,"50","5","Anti-Corruption Internal Control and Enforcement Measures","Anti-corruption efforts will be further intensified by strengthening internal control systems in relation to the generation and allocation of government funds, and the enforcement of penalties against those found guilty of corrupt practices.",""],[1,"183","2","Citizen and CSO Participation Mechanism Strengthening","existing mechanisms where citizens and CSOs can actively engage and participate will be enhanced and strengthened by making them more inclusive and free from political influence.",""],[1,"183","3","Participatory Planning, Budgeting, and M&E Strengthening","Deepen participatory planning and budgeting, monitoring and evaluation (M&E);",""],[1,"183","4","Community and CSO Participation Support","Support community and CSO participation;",""],[1,"184","1","Local Poverty Reduction Action Plans","The government will push for stronger collaboration among NGAs, LGUs and community organizations in localizing poverty reduction through the formulation of Local Poverty Reduction Action Plans (LPRAPs).",""],[1,"184","1","Bottom-Up Participatory Planning and Budgeting Process","For 2014 to 2015, 90 percent of the total number of cities and municipalities are targeted to undertake the bottom-up participatory planning and budgeting process and continuously come up with LPRAPs.",""],[1,"184","1","Nationwide Bottom-Up Planning and Budgeting Coverage","By 2016, it is envisioned that the bottom-up planning and budgeting will cover all cities and municipalities.",""],[1,"184","2","Grassroots Participatory Budgeting Process","The Grassroots Participatory Budgeting Process (GPBP) will see to it that the planning and budgeting processes, both at the local and national government, are more participatory and responsive to local needs.",""],[1,"184","3","Grassroots Participatory Budgeting Process","The Grassroots Participatory Budgeting Process will see to it that the planning and budgeting processes, both at the local and national government, are more participatory and responsive to local needs.",""],[1,"184","4","Regional Participatory Planning and Budgeting Mechanism","At the regional level, the Regional Development Councils (RDCs), whose memberships comprise regional line agencies, LGUs and CSOs, will also be used as a mechanism for participatory planning and budgeting.",""],[1,"184","5","Citizens' Satisfaction Index System Survey","At the local level, the DILG, with the help of local resource institutes, will continue carrying out the Citizens' Satisfaction Index System (CSIS) survey to cover all cities from 2014 to 2016.","DILG"],[1,"184","6","CSO Representation in Local Special Bodies","the DILG will also ensure that CSOs are represented in local special bodies (LSBs) as stipulated in the Local Government Code of 1991 (RA 7160).","DILG"],[1,"184","7","CSO Capacity-Building for Governance Participation","the DILG will conduct capacity-building activities for CSOs on identified competencies, including community organizing, mobilization and support for advocacy work, networking and participation in local governance.","DILG"],[1,"184","8","Local Governance Policy Development and Replication Support","the Union of Local Authorities in the Philippines (ULAP) and its member leagues will support LGUs in policy development and in replicating good and inclusive local governance practices in the areas of education, health, and migration development.",""],[1,"189","4","Citizens' Participatory Audit Project Expansion and Institutionalization","The Citizens' Participatory Audit (CPA) Project, launched in 2012, will be expanded and eventually institutionalized.",""],[1,"192","3","CPA Project Strengthening for Public Audit","Strengthening the CPA Project of the Commission on Audit (COA) to enhance transparency, accountability and citizen participation in the public audit process;","Commission on Audit (COA)"],[1,"309","3","Civil Society Participation in Budget Monitoring and Evaluation Agreement","A formal agreement entered into by a national government agency (NGA) or a government-owned and controlled corporation (GOCC) and a partner civil society organization (CSO) defining the roles, duties, responsibilities, schedules and expectations with regard to implementing the CSO's participation in monitoring and evaluating budget programs/ activities/ projects (PAPs) of the counterpart NGA GOCC for preparation of the annual budget.",""],[1,"312","4","Participatory Audit Institutionalization","Conduct of joint audits by the Commission on Audit (COA) and civil society organizations (CSOs) of select infrastructure projects, including the setting up of systems, tools, and processes to institutionalize participatory audit.","Commission on Audit (COA) | civil society organizations (CSOs)"],[1,"312","6","Citizen Feedback System for Local Government Service Delivery","A system designed to collect and generate citizens' feedback on local government units' (LGUs) service delivery performance.",""],[1,"322","2","Local Government Financial Disclosure Program","The FDP mandates LGUs to post plans, budgets, and full utilization reports in a designated web portal, print media, and in conspicuous places.",""],[1,"322","2","Public Access to Local Government Financial Documents","Enables the public to view, download, and print local government units (LGUs) financial documents to allow their constituents to understand how their local governments budget and spend for public services.",""],[1,"322","2","Constituent Sharing Requirement for Provincial and Municipal Financial Documents","It also obliges provinces, cities, and municipalities (PCMs) share their financial documents with their constituents.",""],[1,"323","8","Participatory Budget and Planning for Priority Poverty Reduction Projects","The enhancement of budget and planning process to involve grassroots organizations and local government units (LGUs) in the identification of - priority poverty reduction projects that will be funded by national government agencies (NGAs).",""]],"5":[[1,"179","11","Public Service Delivery Improvement","government needs to ensure high-quality, efficient, accountable, and accessible delivery of public services.",""],[1,"179","11","Simplification of Public Service Access Procedures","Citizens, especially those already in dire situations, need to be spared from burdensome requirements and processes in accessing public services.",""],[1,"185","2","Public Sector Service Delivery and Accountability Measures","the government has been able to implement several measures to make public institutions deliver services more efficiently and effectively and to make NGAs accountable for their level of performance.",""],[1,"185","3","Citizen's Charter and Anti-Red Tape Service Streamlining","With the Anti-Red Tape Act or ARTA (RA 9485), NGAs, GOCCs, SUCs and LGUs are required to set up Citizen's Charter where service standards are made known to the public.",""],[1,"186","8","Public Service Efficiency and Competence Improvement","Improve efficiency and competence of public service provided;",""],[1,"186","9","Business Process and Frontline Service Streamlining","Streamline business processes and frontline services;",""],[1,"190","3","Anti-Red Tape Program Implementation Enhancement","The Civil Service Commission will enhance the implementation of the Anti-Red Tape Program to ensure the delivery of quality frontline services to the people.","Civil Service Commission"],[1,"190","6","Anti-Red Tape Program Implementation Enhancement","The CSC will enhance the implementation of the Anti-Red Tape Program to ensure the delivery of quality frontline services to the people.","CSC"],[1,"190","6","Service Delivery Excellence Program Strengthening","Its Service Delivery Excellence Program (SDEP) will be strengthened to increase the likelihood of government offices' passing the ARTA-Report Card Survey (RCS).","CSC"],[1,"190","6","Citizen's Charter Review and Enhancement System","A system for reviewing and enhancing Citizen's Charters will also be developed to ensure that Charters are products of (a) streamlining through time and motion studies and other business process improvements; and (b) genuine consultation and agreement between government bodies and citizens.",""],[1,"190","6","Citizen's Satisfaction Center Seal of Excellence Awards","the CSC will continue conferring the Citizen's Satisfaction Center Seal of Excellence to government offices epitomizing exemplary public service.","CSC"],[1,"307","5","Anti-Red Tape Act Compliance Monitoring Program","An initiative of the government to monitor compliance of government agencies with the Anti-Red Tape Act (ARTA).",""],[1,"309","7","Business Permits and Licensing Streamlining Reform","Efforts to streamline the BPLS include adopting a unified form, reducing the number of signatories, limiting the number of steps in securing permits and licenses, and reducing processing time through automation.",""]],"6":[[1,"194","9","Jail Decongestion Program","Detainees under the jail decongestion program increased (under E-JOW, Judgment Day, and newly- issued SC Guidelines on Jail decongestion)",""],[1,"220","8","Modern Criminal Code Reform","Formulating a modern Criminal Code responsive to new laws, current social conditions and emerging crime trends;",""],[1,"220","9","Justice System Reform to Reduce Case Congestion and Backlogs","Implementing reforms in the justice system to address case congestion and backlogs;",""],[1,"220","10","Detention and Corrections Facilities Upgrade","Upgrading detention and corrections facilities and equipment to improve security, living conditions and rehabilitation of inmates;",""]],"7":[[1,"151","4","Health Facility Infrastructure and Quality of Care Improvement","Ensure quality of service by not only investing in facility infrastructure and equipment, but also improving clinical and management processes, and regulating the quality of care provided.",""],[1,"151","6","Health Access and Quality Improvement Efforts","The government continues to undertake efforts as well as investments to address the twin challenge of health access and quality.",""],[1,"153","1","Health Facility Upgrading and Construction Programme","Gaps in the quality of basic facility infrastructure and equipment will be addressed through the upgrading and construction of 10,596 government health facilities from 2014 through 2016, including the rehabilitation of health facilities in areas affected by Super Typhoon Yolanda.",""],[1,"153","1","Health Technology Assessment System","Regular technology assessments will ensure that infrastructure and procedures are both adequate and cost-effective.",""],[1,"153","1","Clinical Practice Guidelines Development and Implementation","Clinical quality will be improved through the development and implementation of better clinical practice guidelines.",""],[1,"153","1","PhilHealth Facility Accreditation System","The Department of Health (DOH), through PhilHealth, will implement an accreditation system in both public and private facilities to ensure that PhilHealth beneficiaries are served in facilities that meet minimum healthcare standards.","Department of Health (DOH) | PhilHealth"],[1,"285","2","Basic Health Care Facility Construction, Rehabilitation, and Upgrading Programme","the government will construct, rehabilitate and upgrade 10,596 basic health care hospitals and facilities within the Updated Plan period, including the installation of basic and comprehensive emergency obstetric facilities with modern and new equipment.",""],[1,"286","15","Philippine Orthopedic Center Modernization","Modernization of the Philippine Orthopedic Center",""]],"8":[[1,"37","6","Agriculture and Fisheries Productivity and Resilience Strategy","For the remaining Plan period, the PDP strategies for agriculture and fisheries sector (Chapter 4) will aim to (a) increase productivity in the sector; (b) increase forward linkage with the industry and services sectors; and (c) improve sector resilience to risks, including climate change.",""],[1,"37","7","Key Commodity Productivity Enhancement Programme","Interventions will be directed towards increasing the productivity of key commodities, such as palay, corn, sugarcane, pineapple, coconut, coffee, banana, mango, livestock and poultry and fisheries, among others.",""],[1,"37","7","Agricultural Research and Extension Investment Expansion","Investments in R&D and extension will be increased to generate appropriate technologies",""],[1,"38","2","Agribusiness and Value Chain Training for Farmers and Fisherfolk","farmers and fisherfolk will be trained in value-adding, agri-business development and value chain management activities.",""],[1,"38","2","Strengthening of Farmers and Fisherfolk Groups and Cooperatives","Farmers and fisherfolk groups and cooperatives will be strengthened and, where possible, transformed into MSMEs that can transact with other MSMEs in industry and services.",""],[1,"117","1","Food Staples Sufficiency Program","The DA has launched the Food Staples Sufficiency Program (FSSP), which aims to provide sufficient, locally-sourced food staples to every Filipino.","DA | NFA"],[1,"117","8","Irrigation Services and Small-Scale Irrigation Development","Provide irrigation services and facilities; maintain existing systems and establish small-scale irrigation systems; enhance cost-sharing/counterpart mechanisms for financing with LGUs;",""],[1,"118","3","Post-Harvest Facilities Development","Establish post-harvest facilities in strategic agricultural production areas.",""],[1,"126","1","Agricultural Support Services and Rural Infrastructure Programme","These involve the provision of support services, such as credit and financing, insurance, rural infrastructure, post- harvest facilities, training and extension, research and development.",""],[1,"339","11","Agriculture and Fisheries Modernization Act","An act modernizing the agriculture and fishing industries of the Philippines.",""],[1,"344","9","NAPAAD Agricultural and Agroindustrial Development Support","The areas within the Network of Protected Areas for Agricultural and Agroindustrial Development (NAPAAD) identified for production, agro processing and marketing activities to help develop and modernize, either the support of government, the agriculture and fisheries sectors in an environmentally and socioculturally sound manner (RA 8435).",""]],"9":[[1,"116","8","High-Value Commodity Production Promotion","Promote the production of high value commodities with comparative advantage, including industrial crops;",""],[1,"116","9","Market Expansion and Value Chain Linkage Initiative","Expand existing markets, explore new markets, and link farmers and fisherfolk to these value chains and commodity/industry clusters;",""],[1,"116","18","Timely Market Information Service for Farmers and SMEs","Provide timely market information to farmers, fishfolk, farmers' and fisherfolk groups, and small and medium enterprises (SMEs) through the use of ICT and other appropriate technologies;",""],[1,"119","6","Industrial Crops Production Expansion","the volume and productivity of industrial crops will be increased for abaca, cacao, coffee, oil palm, rubber, sugarcane and tobacco",""],[1,"119","7","Value-Adding and Agribusiness Development for Small-Holder Farmers","The following strategies will be implemented to promote value-adding of A&F products and agribusiness development among small-holder farmers, including ARBs and indigenous peoples:",""],[1,"119","8","Market Expansion and Value Chain Linkage Strategy","Expand existing markets, explore new markets, and link farmers and fisherfolk to these value chains and commodity/industry clusters",""],[1,"120","3","Timely Market Information Service for Farmers, Fisherfolk, and SMEs","Provide timely market information to farmers, fisherfolk, farmers' and fisherfolk groups, and small and medium enterprises (SMEs) through the use of ICT and other appropriate technologies",""]],"10":[[1,"114","11","Sustainable Productivity-Enhancing Technology Adoption for Farmers and Fisherfolk","Farmers, fisherfolk and their oganizations adopt sustainable, productivity- enhancing technologies and innovations",""],[1,"115","3","Sustainable Productivity-Enhancing Technology Adoption for Farmers and Fisherfolk","Farmers, fisherfolk and their oganizations adopt sustainable, productivity-enhancing technologies and innovations",""],[1,"116","11","Farmer and Fisherfolk Capacity Building Programme","Strengthen and build the capacities of farmers and fisherfolk through the provision of extension and conduct of trainings on appropriate technologies and innovations on production, farming systems and fishery practices.",""],[1,"116","12","Stakeholder Extension and Training Capacity-Building Programme","Strengthen and build the capacities of stakeholders through extension and training (value-adding, agribusiness development, value-chain management)",""],[1,"116","14","Agribusiness Extension and Value-Chain Training Programme","Strengthen and build the capacities of stakeholders by providing extension services and conducting training on value-adding agribusiness development and value-chain management",""],[1,"117","4","Agricultural Extension Services Strengthening and Coordination","Rationalize and strengthen the provision of extension services through improved complementation of national, local and private sector entities;",""],[1,"117","5","Farmer and Fisherfolk Participation in Research and Promotion","Encourage the participation of farmers, fisherfolk and their organizations in research and promotion activities;",""],[1,"117","6","Farmer and Fisherfolk Capacity-Building through Extension and Training","Strengthen and build the capacities of farmers and fisherfolk through the provision of extension and conduct of trainings on appropriate technologies and innovations on production, farming systems and fishery practices",""],[1,"120","1","Stakeholder Capacity-Building through Extension Services and Training","Strengthen and build the capacities of stakeholders by providing extension services and conducting training on value-adding, agribusiness development and value-chain management",""],[1,"121","12","Climate-Sensitive Agricultural Extension and Support Services","Strengthen agricultural extension and support services on the adoption of climate-sensitive farming and fishing technologies;",""],[1,"320","3","Agriculture and Fisheries Training and Support Services","The provision of training, information, and support services by the government and non-government organizations to the agriculture and fisheries sectors to improve the technical, business, and social capabilities of farmers and fisherfolk (RA 8435).",""]],"11":[[1,"38","4","Agricultural and Fisheries Livelihood Diversification Support","households engaged in agriculture and fisheries will be encouraged to diversify production and livelihood sources.",""],[1,"38","4","Sector Insurance System Strengthening","The insurance system for the sector will also be strengthened.",""],[1,"38","4","Community-Based Employment Program Redesign","the Community- based Employment Program (CBEP) will be re-designed to function as a social protection mechanism.",""],[1,"116","19","Access to Credit and Financial Packages Improvement","Improve access to credit and other financial packages",""],[1,"119","2","Strengthening of the AFMA-Mandated AMCFP","· Strengthen the Agriculture and Fisheries Modernization Act (AFMA)- mandated AMCFP;",""],[1,"119","3","Farmer and Fisherfolk Creditworthiness Capacity Building Program","Implement capacity building programs to improve the credit-worthiness of farmers, fisherfolk and their organizations;",""],[1,"119","4","Innovative Agricultural Financing and Risk-Reduction Scheme","Develop and promote innovative financing schemes and risk-reducing mechanisms (i.e., guarantee and insurance) to encourage more banks and other lending conduits (i.e., cooperatives, government agencies, LGUs) to lend to farmers' and fisherfolk;",""],[1,"119","5","Credit, Guarantee and Insurance Information Dissemination","Intensify information dissemination of credit, guarantee and insurance program.",""],[1,"121","1","Agricultural and Fisheries Insurance Expansion","The Updated PDP intends to increase insurance protection extended to farmers and fisherfolk against losses in the A&F sector due to natural calamities as well as plant pests and diseases.",""],[1,"121","11","Agriculture and Fisheries Insurance System Strengthening","Strengthen the A&F insurance system;",""],[1,"124","3","Domestic Agriculture Competitiveness and Safety Net Support","the government will strengthen competitiveness of domestic agriculture to take advantage of trade opportunities while ensuring the provision of safety nets.",""]],"12":[[1,"93","2","Inclusive Business and Value Chain Integration","The government will also promote inclusive businesses and include low-income communities in product value chains.",""],[1,"116","10","Agriculture and Fisheries Household Diversification Support","Encourage diversification of production and livelihood options for A&F households.",""],[1,"116","20","Formalization and SME Transformation of Farmers' and Fisherfolk Cooperatives","Support the transformation of farmers' and fisherfolk groups and cooperatives into formal and viable SMEs;",""],[1,"120","4","Transformation of Farmers' and Fisherfolk Groups into Formal SMEs","Strategy 11: Support the transformation of farmers' and fisherfolk groups and cooperatives into formal and viable SMEs",""],[1,"121","4","Off-Farm and Non-Farm Activities Promotion","Promote the development of off-farm and non-farm activities;",""],[1,"121","5","Community-Based Employment Program Income Protection Reform","Revise the design of the Community-Based Employment Program (CBEP) to function as an income protection measure;",""]],"13":[[1,"31","2","Geographically Converged Agrarian Reform Community Support","with the Department of Agrarian Reform's (DAR) program for agrarian reform communities (ARCs), the Departments of Agriculture (DA), Environment and Natural Resources (DENR) and LGUs respectively contribute for the roads and irrigation, watershed protection services, and extension services to make the land productive, while DAR and, subsequently, government financial institutions support the farmers' organizations in financing the requirements for their enterprises.","Department of Agrarian Reform | Department of Agriculture | Department of Environment and Natural Resources | LGUs | government financial institutions | Department of Trade and Industry"],[1,"31","2","ARC Supply Contract Facilitation","the DAR and Department of Trade and Industry (DTI) bring together ARCs, often from contiguous towns, to negotiate supply contracts with businesses downstream, in the process reducing transaction costs and facilitating commerce.","Department of Agrarian Reform | Department of Trade and Industry"],[1,"38","3","Rural Connectivity and Market Access Infrastructure Enhancement","Rural infrastructure will be enhanced by focusing on connectivity between production areas and markets, as well as facilities that provide production and technology choices to farmers and fisherfolk.",""],[1,"38","3","Public-Private Financing for Postharvest and Rural Infrastructure","Public-private sector partnerships will be explored to finance certain postharvest facilities and other rural infrastructure.",""],[1,"46","6","Agricultural Irrigation Expansion","Adequate irrigation facilities will be provided, including small irrigation facilities, to increase crop productivity and enable farmers to have greater control over their production patterns.",""],[1,"46","6","Farm-to-Market Road Construction and Rehabilitation","farm-to-market roads will be constructed or rehabilitated to strategically connect rural and agricultural areas to market towns and destinations.",""],[1,"118","5","Agrarian Reform Support Services Continuation","Alongside the intensified efforts to complete land acquisition and distribution, the government will ensure continued delivery of support services to agrarian reform beneficiaries and communities.",""],[1,"118","6","Support Services for ARBs and ARCs","the government will ensure continued delivery of support services to ARBs and ARCs",""],[1,"118","7","Convergence on Value-Chain Enhancement for Rural Growth and Empowerment Project","An example of such intervention is the newly approved Convergence on Value- Chain Enhancement for Rural Growth & Empowerment (CONVERGE) Project.",""],[1,"119","1","GROWTH Project for Rural Organizations and Smallholder Farmers","Another example is the proposed Gearing Rural Organizations for Wealth Creation Towards Household Income Improvement (GROWTH) Project.",""],[1,"124","6","Continued Delivery of Support Services to Agrarian Reform Beneficiaries","It should include the completion of the LAD component and continued delivery of support services to ARBs.",""]],"14":[[1,"141","9","Social Safety Nets and Risk Protection","The Updated PDP recognizes the role of government in putting in place appropriate safety nets and risk protection for the poor.",""],[1,"146","4","Social Protection and Secure Shelter Expansion","the PDP seeks to (b) reduce people's vulnerability by expanding social protection services and providing more secure shelter",""],[1,"147","13","Targeting System Enhancement for Vulnerable Households","Enhance the targeting system by identifying the \"near poor\"/ vulnerable and knowing their needs",""],[1,"161","7","Social Protection Expansion and Secure Shelter Support","Thus, a strategy to reduce vulnerabilities entails expanding social protection and providing more secure shelter, particularly in Category 3 provinces that are highly vulnerable and prone to multiple hazards.",""],[1,"162","12","Social Protection Mechanisms for Vulnerable Households and Workers","the government has been keen on continuing and putting in place different social protection mechanisms.",""],[1,"164","3","Expansion of Social Insurance for Vulnerable Households","Social insurances that seek to mitigate individual and life cycle risks to vulnerable households (HH) expanded",""],[1,"165","2","Expansion of the NHTS-PR Vulnerability Database","there is a need to revisit and expand the NHTS-PR database to cover those who are vulnerable to different types of risks or shocks",""],[1,"165","2","Development of More Responsive Social Protection Programs","appropriate and more responsive social protection programs may be developed",""],[1,"165","3","Expansion and Responsiveness of Social Protection and Social Insurance Systems","Coverage of social protection programs and social insurance systems will be expanded and made more responsive to different types or sources of vulnerabilities such as the growing number of children in hazardous labor.",""],[1,"165","6","Pantawid Pamilya Graduation Support","These will involve enhancing programs such as the Pantawid Pamilya Program to enable its beneficiaries to be more self-sufficient when they graduate from the program.",""],[1,"166","1","Social Welfare Programs for Vulnerable Groups","effectively design and implement social welfare programs particularly to address violence against women, to provide social pension for indigent senior citizens, and to serve persons with disabilities.",""],[1,"166","2","Multi-Level and Multi-Program Convergence Mechanism","The mechanism will depict the multi-level and multi-program convergence, where various types of convergence will be implemented depending on the social protection needs of target areas or sectors.",""],[1,"166","3","Social Protection Operational Framework Implementation","Implementation of social protection programs will thus be guided by the Social Protection Operational Framework adopted in 2012.",""],[1,"166","3","Social Protection Handbook Development","a Social Protection Handbook will also be developed to serve as primary reference in planning, implementing, monitoring and evaluating social protection interventions.",""],[1,"166","4","Vulnerability and Adaptation Manual for Social Protection","The Vulnerability and Adaptation Manual for Social Protection, which is part of the Handbook focusing on risk and vulnerability assessment, will be formulated as a guide for local development workers from the LGUs, government agencies and NGOs in assessing risks and vulnerabilities and identifying adaptive strategies for social protection in the communities.",""],[1,"166","5","Institutionalization of Social Protection Programs and Projects","Social protection programs and projects will be institutionalized to become part of the regular program and budget of the government at different levels.",""],[1,"166","5","Local Government Social Protection Convergence Planning","LGUs implementing social protection convergent programs will already start including them in their own plans and budgets as this will initially synchronize and harmonize program implementation/operations across sectors and institutions.",""],[1,"166","5","Bottom-Up Budgeting for Social Protection Convergence","The menu on bottom-up budgeting will be the take-off for this convergence.",""],[1,"166","6","Social Protection Monitoring and Evaluation System","A unified and user-friendly monitoring and evaluation system based on agreed common data sets shall be designed and used by agencies implementing social protection programs.",""],[1,"343","12","Stop-gap Relief and Transition Support Measures","Stop-gap mechanisms or urgent responses that address effects of economic shocks, disasters and calamities on specific vulnerable groups.",""]],"15":[[1,"163","4","Local Government Unit Capacity Strengthening for Disaster Risk Reduction and Social Protection Delivery","Need to strengthen capability of LGUs to implement disaster risk reduction strategies and deliver social protection services;",""],[1,"165","5","Local Government Emergency Response Capacity Enhancement","Capacities of LGUs shall be enhanced to provide immediate response in emergency situations to include a menu of tested safety net programs especially during calamities and disasters.",""],[1,"165","5","Funding Support Options for Local Emergency Response","Options for funding support will also be explored.",""]],"16":[[1,"13","10","Major Connectivity Infrastructure Projects","Major infrastructure projects to improve connectivity between urban centers and regional growth hubs",""],[1,"33","4","Typhoon Yolanda Reconstruction and Infrastructure Bottleneck Reduction","government spearheads reconstruction efforts in the areas affected by typhoon Yolanda and further addresses infrastructure bottlenecks elsewhere",""],[1,"36","6","Infrastructure Development Investment","Government will continue to invest in infrastructure development, with government capital outlay increasing to 5 percent of GDP by 2016.",""],[1,"42","3","Physical Infrastructure Improvement for Trade and Labor Mobility","Improving physical infrastructure to enhance trade and labor mobility are critical interventions.",""],[1,"46","4","Accelerated Public Infrastructure Investment and PPP Mobilization","Infrastructure development will be accelerated to support rapid and sustained growth and promote inclusivity (Chapter 10).",""],[1,"46","7","Connectivity Infrastructure Development","In industry and services, infrastructure development will focus on improving the connectivity between urban centers and regional growth hubs, between airport and ports and economic/industrial zones; and between airport and ports and tourism destinations.",""],[1,"47","5","New Bohol (Panglao) Airport Development Project","New Bohol (Panglao) Airport Development Project",""],[1,"47","6","Budget/Low Cost Carrier Terminal Construction at Clark International Airport","Clark International Airport Construction of a Budget/Low Cost Carrier (LCC) Terminal",""],[1,"47","7","Mactan Cebu International Airport New Passenger International Terminal Construction","Mactan Cebu International Airport Construction of the New Passenger International Terminal",""]],"17":[[1,"273","5","Maritime Security Capability and Infrastructure Strengthening","The thrust is to strengthen maritime security capabilities and infrastructure facilities and reinforce security measures from external threats through ICT-based technologies.",""],[1,"276","5","Clark International Airport Service Enhancement Projects","With several projects also lined up to enhance the services of Clark International Airport (CIA), the extension of SCMB corridor farther north and south will be pursued through increased utilization of the Subic and Batangas Ports.",""],[1,"277","1","Central RORO Spine Project","The completion of the Central RORO (Roll-On/Roll-Off) Spine Project will enhance interisland logistics, to facilitate seamless movement of passengers, vehicles and goods along the Luzon-Panay-Negros-Cebu-Bohol-Mindanao route.",""],[1,"277","8","Tourism Port Construction, Upgrading and Improvement","construction/upgrading and improvement of several tourism ports, like Ivana Port in Batanes, Panganngan Port in Bohol, Lawigan Port in Camiguin, and Cagban Jetty Port in Aklan, will be undertaken to expand their capacities.",""],[1,"284","16","Amendment of Port and Civil Aviation Authority Charters","Amendment of the Charters of Philippine Ports Authority and Civil Aviation Authority of the Philippines, to address conflicts in their regulatory and operation/ operator functions",""],[1,"289","4","Sea Navigation Aids Rehabilitation and Maritime Security Capacity Building","the government will continue rehabilitating sea navigation aids, including capability building of PCG personnel on counter terrorism and against other external threats.",""],[1,"289","4","Procurement of Patrol Boats and Multi-role Response Vessels","Along with this is the procurement of patrol boats and multi-role response vessels, as well as the utilization of geographical information system technologies in identifying safe areas for marine navigation.",""],[1,"289","4","Geographic Information System for Marine Navigation Safety","the utilization of geographical information system technologies in identifying safe areas for marine navigation.",""],[1,"290","2","Municipal Port Improvement, Construction, and Rehabilitation","with the DOTC improving, constructing and rehabilitating municipal ports in San Esteban in Ilocos Sur, Tarahib in Catanduanes, Kawayan in Biliran, Galas in Dipolog, Lugus in Sulu, as well as other ports in ARMM.","DOTC"],[1,"305","9","Coastal Security Program","A program designed to secure the country's coasts especially in Mindanao regions.",""]],"19":[[1,"88","1","Logistics Infrastructure Investment Programme","the government will encourage investments in the development of logistics infrastructure to cater to both domestic and international supply chains.",""],[1,"88","1","Customs and Multimodal Transport Policy Reform","the government will review and develop/reform related policies and rules, such as customs practices; trans- shipment of cargoes through various modes (i.e. air-air, sea-air, and air-sea); and foreign shipping services along the entire multimodal transportation chain.",""],[1,"88","1","National Logistics Plan","the government, in coordination with the private sector, will formulate and implement the National Logistics Plan",""],[1,"88","1","Logistics Cost Reduction Target","will target to reduce the share of logistics costs (including shipping) in the cost of goods and services from 23 percent to 15 percent by 2016.",""],[1,"89","1","National Single Window-E2M System Linkage","The linkage of the National Single Window with the Electronic to Mobile (E2M) system will be pursued to facilitate trade and reduce transaction costs for businesses.",""],[1,"116","15","Rural Infrastructure Improvement for Market Connectivity","Improve rural infrastructure to enhance connectivity and integration of production areas to markets",""],[1,"116","23","Public-Private Partnership Promotion for Infrastructure and Value Chain Development","Pursue public-private parnerships (PPPs) especially for infrastructure and value chain development and management",""],[1,"117","9","Logistics Infrastructure Development for Market Connectivity","Establish roads, bridges and other logistics-related infrastructure to link production areas to markets;",""],[1,"118","1","Rural Infrastructure System Improvement","Increase the effectiveness and efficiency of the rural infrastructure system such as FMRs, bridges, post-harvest, information and communications technology (ICT) systems and all other infrastructure",""],[1,"122","2","Public-Private Partnership Infrastructure and Services Delivery for Agriculture and Fisheries","The private sector will be tapped to participate in the government's efforts to immediately deliver the needed infrastructure and services for A&F.",""],[1,"122","2","PPP-Eligible Agriculture and Fisheries Infrastructure Projects","Among the projects that may be eligible under PPP include irrigation infrastructure, food supply chain and postharvest services (i.e., bulk handling facilities, food/ grains terminals and processing, storage, handling and port/transport facilities), production centers for various farm inputs, fish-farming infrastructure, and market and trading centers.",""],[1,"123","2","Public Investment in Access Connectivity and Electricity","Public investments such as access connectivity and electricity will be needed for those without road access to boost market potential.",""],[1,"126","1","Agricultural Support Services and Rural Infrastructure Programme","These involve the provision of support services, such as credit and financing, insurance, rural infrastructure, post- harvest facilities, training and extension, research and development.",""],[1,"332","2","National Transportation Policy Framework","A long-term comprehensive policy which shall guide all elements of the transportation system and all sub-sectors of transportation, including passengers, shippers, service providers, agencies and instrumentalities of government and those involved in the movement of people and goods and in the provision of transportation infrastructure, facilities and services.",""]],"20":[[1,"284","4","Anti-Trust Law Enactment","Enactment of Anti-Trust Law, to combat unfair competition in industries",""],[1,"284","5","Tariff and Customs Code and Domestic Shipping Act Amendment","Amendment of the Tariff and Customs Code and Domestic Shipping Development Act, to foster greater competition and lower transportation cost",""],[1,"315","2","Tariff and Customs Code Harmonization Reform","a legislative proposal that seeks to introduce amendments to the Tariff and Customs Code of the Philippines (TCCP) with a view of aligning its provisions with the International Convention on the Simplification and Harmonization of Customs Procedures (i.e., Revised Kyoto Convention (RKC))",""]],"21":[[1,"271","1","Critical Social Infrastructure and Social Protection Support","These entail the provision of critical infrastructure support related to health, nutrition, education, shelter and other means of social protection.",""],[1,"276","5","High Standard Highway Network Development Master Plan","Under the master plan on High Standard Highway Network Development, additional 234.13 kilometers (km) of toll expressways will provide interconnectivity in Central Luzon, Metro Manila and the CALABARZON.",""],[1,"276","5","SCMB Corridor Multimodal Logistics System","the government will develop a seamless multimodal logistics system along the Subic-Clark-Manila-Batangas (SCMB) corridor to ensure efficient flow of commodities, supplies, and inputs to tourism, agricultural production and economic/industrial zones.",""],[1,"276","6","Long-Distance High-Speed Mass Rail Transit System","the government will explore establishing a long-distance, high-speed mass rail transit system",""],[1,"276","6","Integrated Freight Railway System","the government will explore establishing ... an integrated/full-length railway system for freight-rail services across Luzon",""],[1,"276","6","Rationalization of Mass Transport Agency Roles","Along with this is the rationalization of agency roles on mass transport development.",""],[1,"278","10","Contactless Automatic Fare Collection System","Contactless Automatic Fare Collection System to be implemented in 2015",""],[1,"279","9","Farm-to-Market Road Construction and Rehabilitation","In addition, rural infrastructure and facilities will be improved through the construction/rehabilitation of farm-to-market roads that strategically connect rural and agricultural areas with market towns and destinations, and enable efficient transport of agriculture produce to market towns and distribution centers.",""],[1,"284","1","National Transport Policy Approval","The expected approval of the National Transport Policy will raise the level of accountability in decision making and enhance interaction among institutions regulating international and domestic freight transport, transport operators and intermediaries providing brokerage services.",""],[1,"285","1","Soft and Hard Infrastructure Expansion for Basic and Social Services","Both soft and hard infrastructure strategies will address gaps in the supply-side of basic and social services to help improve human capability, reduce vulnerabilities, and ultimately equalize development opportunities for all.",""],[1,"289","1","Automatic Fare Collection System Installation","In the case of existing mass transport systems, priority interventions include installation of automatic fare collection systems and system rehabilitation to modernize facilities and improve service.",""],[1,"289","1","Mass Transport System Rehabilitation and Modernization","In the case of existing mass transport systems, priority interventions include installation of automatic fare collection systems and system rehabilitation to modernize facilities and improve service.",""],[1,"289","1","Maintenance Fund Provision for Transport Infrastructure","For long-term sustainability, the government will ensure availability and adequacy of maintenance funds.",""],[1,"289","1","Innovative Financing Schemes for Local Transport Networks","For local transport networks management and maintenance, innovative financing schemes will be set up for LGUs.",""],[1,"290","2","Foreign-Assisted Road and Bridge Construction Projects","The government will continue until 2016 to implement ongoing and programmed foreign-assisted projects for road and bridge construction",""]],"22":[[1,"275","11","Safety and Security Measures","10. Provide safety and security measures",""],[1,"283","13","Independent Regulatory Authorities for Transport, Water, and ICT","It is necessary to strengthen institutional and regulatory regimes, particularly in the transport, water, and ICT subsectors, by creating independent regulators to enhance competitiveness and protect consumers.",""],[1,"284","15","National Transport Safety and Security Act","Enactment of National Transport Safety and Security Act, to create a board that investigates transport accidents and provides transport safety recommendations",""],[1,"289","3","Transport Terminal Security Inspection and Plan Evaluation","the DOTC-Office of Transport Security (OTS) will continue thorough inspections and evaluation of security plans of public transport terminals.","DOTC-Office of Transport Security (OTS)"]],"23":[[1,"239","1","Intelligent Transport Systems and Green Mobility Expansion","the Department of Transportation and Communication's (DOTC) implementation of intelligent transport systems and reduction of road vehicle volume through mass transportation systems, alternative modes/green transport and integration of provincial terminals","Department of Transportation and Communication"],[1,"292","10","National Environmentally Sustainable Transport Strategy","The government will pursue the National Environmentally Sustainable Transport (NEST) strategy, which aims to reduce energy consumption and associated greenhouse gases and air pollutant emissions.",""],[1,"292","10","Safe Non-Motorized Transport Facilities Expansion","Further installation of safe, non-motorized transport facilities, such as sidewalks, footbridges, underground walkways and bicycle ways, will be provided to ensure pedestrian safety.",""]],"24":[[1,"89","4","Cabotage Rule Review and Shipping Market Liberalization","Reduce domestic shipping costs through the review of the cabotage rule and leveling of playing field among domestic and foreign shipping lines;",""],[1,"89","12","Maritime Regulatory Harmonization and Central Maritime Administration Reform","Provide uniform rules and regulations governing global maritime professionals in accordance with the Standards for Training, Certification and Watchkeeping (STCW) Convention and establish the Maritime Industry Authority (MARINA) as the single and central maritime administration of government;",""],[1,"124","4","Review of Laws on Inter-Island Shipping by Foreign Vessels","There is a need to review the provisions of relevant laws that tackle inter-island shipping activities of foreign vessels that are perceived to support the development of shipping operations within the country.",""],[1,"124","5","Review of Shipping and Customs Laws","To address this, there is a need to review the provisions of relevant laws that tackle inter-island shipping activities of foreign vessels that are perceived to support the development of shipping operations within the country.",""]],"25":[[1,"36","5","Transparent and Predictable Investment Policy Reform","government will continue to promote transparent and predictable policies and further streamline bureaucratic procedures to encourage investments.",""],[1,"36","5","Local Business Permit Licensing System Streamlining","By 2016, the government aims to have all LGUs adopt and streamline the business permit licensing system.",""],[1,"36","5","Philippine Business Registry and LGU Linkage","The government will likewise continue to undertake measures to link the Philippine Business Registry with LGUs to ensure that businesses in local communities enjoy the benefits of easier registration.",""],[1,"36","5","National Single Window to E2M System Linkage","The linkage of the National Single Window to the Electronic to Mobile (E2M) system will be pursued to facilitate trade and reduce cost of transactions for businesses.",""],[1,"51","2","Unified Competition and Anti-Trust Law","enhancing economic justice entails enacting a unified competition/ anti-trust law",""],[1,"51","2","Competition Law Enforcement Strengthening","intensifying enforcement efforts, in partnership with sector regulators and other stakeholders",""],[1,"51","2","Commercial Dispute Resolution Efficiency Reform","addressing efficiency concerns on commercial dispute resolution",""],[1,"76","3","Business Climate Improvement and Market Access Reform","the government will continue to improve the business climate, promote an environment that increases productivity and innovative capacity, enforce regulations that enhance consumer welfare and expand market access",""],[1,"80","4","Business Registration Streamlining through PBR","The average processing time to register sole proprietorships was reduced to 30 minutes with the use of the PBR.",""],[1,"88","3","Transparent and Predictable Business Policy Framework","The government will continue to promote transparent and predictable policies to create an environment conducive to business to encourage investments.",""],[1,"88","4","Business Climate Governance and Regulatory Reform","To improve the business climate, the first strategy is to improve governance by streamlining procedures, implementing policy reforms and the e-commerce law, combating smuggling, rationalizing economic zone development, promoting mutually agreed upon work arrangements and maintaining industrial peace.",""],[1,"88","5","Transparent and Predictable Business Policy Promotion","The government will continue to promote transparent and predictable policies to create an environment conducive to business to encourage investments.",""],[1,"88","5","Streamlined Business Permit and Licensing System Adoption","By 2016, the government aims that all LGUs have adopted streamlined BPLS.",""],[1,"88","5","Automation of the Business Permit and Licensing System","Moreover, efforts to automate the BPLS for faster and more efficient transactions with government will be continued.",""],[1,"88","6","Linking the PBR with Local Government Units for Easier Business Registration","The government will likewise continue to undertake measures to link the PBR with LGUs to ensure that businesses in local communities will enjoy the benefits of easier registration.",""],[1,"88","6","Doing Business Dashboard for Business Start-Up Simplification","These programs will be complemented by the efforts of the National Competitiveness Council (NCC), with the help of the DTI, Department of the Interior and Local Government (DILG), SEC, BIR, SSS, PhilHealth, Pag- IBIG and the Quezon City government, under the Doing Business Dashboard, to bring down the number of steps (from 16 to 3) and days (from 36 to 6) to start a business by 2016.","DTI | Department of the Interior and Local Government (DILG) | SEC | BIR | SSS | PhilHealth | Pag- IBIG"],[1,"89","7","Anti-trust and Competition Policy Act","Level the business playing field by strengthening the legal and institutional framework to prevent unfair and anti-competitive practices through the enactment of the Anti-trust/Competition Policy Act;",""],[1,"190","2","Investment Climate Improvement Initiatives","Various initiatives put in place to make the country more conducive for investment will be continued and improved.",""],[1,"190","4","Ease of Doing Business Action Plan Implementation","The interagency Task Force on Ease of Doing Business (EODB), created under AO 38 in 2013 to improve the ease of doing business in the country, will implement the action plan prepared by the National Competitiveness Council (NCC) to enhance the business competitiveness of the Philippines.",""],[1,"190","4","Game Plan for Competitiveness Implementation","The task force will implement the Game Plan for Competitiveness to raise Philippine competitiveness rankings to the top third in the world by 2016.",""],[1,"190","5","National Business Permit and Licensing Streamlining","through the national streamlining of the BPLS, a joint effort of the DILG and the DTI, all cities and municipalities will have standard BPLS by the end of 2014.","DILG | DTI"],[1,"190","5","Technical Assistance for Local Regulatory Service Streamlining","the DILG will also begin providing technical assistance to LGUs in the streamlining of other local regulatory services, such as building/ construction and occupancy permitting in an effort to make them more competitive and business friendly.","DILG"]],"26":[[1,"94","3","MSME Support Programme","Government will continue to support MSMEs to increase their contribution to the country's GDP and total employment.",""],[1,"94","4","SME Roving Academy Program Scale-Up","The government will scale up implementation of the SME Roving Academy Program.",""],[1,"94","5","SME Roving Academy Business Support and Training Programme","Under the SME Roving Academy, start-up enterprises will be provided assistance on business registration procedures, training on managerial skills, customer relations management, financial management, green values, marketing management, costing and pricing, and market information.",""],[1,"94","5","SME Technology Upgrading and Export Readiness Support","Existing enterprises will be assisted on technology application, productivity improvement, Hazard Analysis Critical Control Point (HACCP), Good Manufacturing Practice (GMP) awareness, waste minimization in the manufacturing process, Total Quality Management, basics on exporting, and trade fairs participation, among others.",""],[1,"94","6","MSME Loan Access Improvement Programme","Programs under this strategy will help ensure reasonable and affordable cost of obtaining MSME loans; reasonable and manageable requirements for compliance by MSMEs to obtain loans; and simplified and streamlined process to obtain loans.",""],[1,"94","6","Insurance Risk Parameter Development Support","The government will also promote institutions that could develop insurance parameters against risks.",""],[1,"94","6","Risk-Based Lending Training for Rural Banks and Financial Institutions","More rural banks and financial institutions will be trained on risk-based lending.",""],[1,"314","8","MSME Credit Enhancement Scheme","A credit enhancement scheme developed by the Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas (Bangko Sentral) which aims to increase the credit worthiness of micro, small and medium enterprises (MSMEs) that are experiencing difficulty in obtaining loans from banks due to lack of acceptable collaterals, credit knowledge and credit track records.","Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas"]],"27":[[1,"36","3","Investment Promotion Campaign","government will continue to promote the country as a desirable investment destination.",""],[1,"37","4","Trade Agreement and ASEAN Business Advocacy Program","the government will intensify advocacy programs that will encourage businesses to take advantage of benefits offered by Philippine participation in free trade agreements and the ASEAN Economic Community 2015.",""],[1,"37","4","Expanded Investment Promotion Activities","Investment promotion activities will be undertaken not only in the traditional investor countries (i.e., US, Japan, European Union), but also in member-countries of economic groups to which the Philippines belongs.",""],[1,"37","4","Unified Country Branding Campaign","the government will aggressively promote unified country branding that will bring home the message that the Philippines is a producer and supplier of high quality, ethical, sustainable and world-class products and services which are valued worldwide.",""],[1,"89","13","Trade Negotiation Capacity Building","Improve the negotiation process and build the capacity of trade negotiators.",""],[1,"95","5","Trade Agreement Awareness and Business Matching Support","The government will intensify advocacy programs that will encourage businesses, particularly MSMEs, to maximize benefits from opportunities offered by Philippine participation in free trade agreements and the ASEAN Economic Community 2015.",""],[1,"95","5","Preferential Trade Agreement Utilization Campaign","Local industries will be encouraged to make use of preferential agreements not only through education and information campaigns but also through business matching activities.",""],[1,"95","6","Philippine Export Development Plan 2014-2016","The Philippine Export Development Plan (PEDP) 2014-2016 will be formulated and implemented.",""],[1,"104","7","Trade Facilitation for Agricultural Export Growth","The continued trade facilitation activities of the government, through the Department of Agriculture (DA), to increase market access alongside the sustained Avian Influenza (AI)- and foot and mouth disease (FMD)-free livestock and poultry sectors are seen to support exports growth.","Department of Agriculture (DA)"]],"28":[[1,"91","4","National Innovation Centers for MSME Product Development","Innovation centers will be established nationwide to support MSMEs to undertake innovative product development.",""],[1,"91","4","Testing, Calibration, and Quality Assurance Facility Upgrade","Existing testing, calibration and quality assurance facilities and services will be enhanced and upgraded.",""],[1,"91","4","Small Enterprise Technology Upgrading Program Expansion","The Small Enterprise Technology Upgrading Program (SETUP) will be expanded to focus on identified priority geographical locations where the poor reside.",""],[1,"93","3","Technology Business Incubation and Shared Service Facilities","These industries will also continuously upgrade their technology and facilities with government's proactive support through the establishment of technology business incubation centers, shared service facilities that provide testing laboratories for safety and quality standards, agro-industrial hubs and central storage.",""],[1,"94","7","Small Entrepreneur Technology Access Support","Small entrepreneurs will be provided access to innovative, cost-effective and appropriate technologies, such as the Shared Service Facilities.",""],[1,"120","7","Shared Service Facilities for MSMEs","In support of this, the Department of Trade and Industry (DTI) has been establishing shared service facilities (SSFs) or production centers to provide micro-, small and medium enterprises (MSMEs) better access to technology and more sophisticated equipment.","Department of Trade and Industry (DTI)"]],"29":[[1,"250","2","Mining Law Amendment for Sector Reform Implementation","Amendment of the mining law will be needed to provide policies and guidelines for the institutionalization and implementation of reforms in the mining sector.",""],[1,"250","6","Mining Law Amendment and Sector Reform Package","amendment of the mining law will be needed to provide policies and guidelines for the institutionalization and implementation of reforms in the mining sector",""],[1,"259","2","Mining Revenue Sharing Scheme Rationalization","This will rationalize existing mining revenue sharing scheme and arrangement.",""],[1,"259","6","Designation of Mining Industry Zones","All mining areas will be declared as Mining Industry Zones.",""],[1,"320","8","Extractive Industries Revenue Transparency Initiative","A tripartite initiative between government, civil society and business to ensure greater transparency in revenues from extractive industries, specifically through the publication of a report that compares government and industry figures in government revenues in mining, oil and gas.",""]],"30":[[1,"210","1","Expansion of Crime/Forensic Laboratory Network","planned to establish similar laboratories in Mindanao and Northern Luzon to augment the lone facility in Manila",""],[1,"220","4","Police Presence Expansion in Crime-Prone Areas","Increasing police presence in crime-prone areas and strategic locations through recruitment of additional uniformed personnel, provision of complete mission- essential equipment and construction of additional police stations;",""],[1,"220","6","Law Enforcement Against Organized Crime Groups","Intensifying law enforcement interventions against organized crime groups;",""],[1,"220","7","Crime Investigation and Forensic Capacity Upgrade","Improving crime investigation, prosecution, and resolution by upgrading crime investigation facilities and equipment, providing additional forensic laboratories in Baguio and Davao, and augmenting personnel augmentation;",""],[1,"220","12","Crime Victimization Survey","Establishing a crime victimization survey.",""],[1,"223","6","PNP Reorganization Plan","PNP Reorganization Plan, strengthening the PNP's organizational and functional structures by streamlining administrative functions from the uniformed to non-uniformed personnel and maximizing various police field services in maintaining peace and rule of law;",""],[1,"223","7","PNP Modernization Program","PNP Modernization Program, outlining a five-year program on the development of its human resources, doctrine, infrastructure and facilities, and equipment acquisition and support system, over and above the annual Capability Enhancement Program;",""]],"31":[[1,"50","1","Natural Resource Conservation, Protection and Rehabilitation Programme","effective management of natural resources will require strengthening the conservation, protection and rehabilitation of forest and watershed, coastal and marine life, land and mineral resources, and the entire biodiversity.",""],[1,"50","2","Environmental Quality Standards and ENR Sector Strengthening","It is imperative for the ENR sector in the next midterm to encourage research, development and extension, sustain financing, improve law enforcement and strengthen coordination and institutional mechanisms.",""],[1,"121","7","Natural Resource Base Rehabilitation and Restoration for Agriculture and Forestry Production","Adopt effective approaches to develop, rehabilitate and restore the natural resource base for A&F production;",""],[1,"121","9","Integration of Agricultural Priorities into Land Use Planning","Promote the integration of agricultural development priorities/thrusts in land use and development, especially at the sub-national level.",""],[1,"125","1","Land Use Policy and Zoning Bill","The passage of the bill, pending for two decades now, is expected to provide legal and other mechanisms not only for land reform areas, but also zoned areas for water and water uses, especially for agriculture.",""],[1,"125","1","Integrated Land Allocation and Land Use Conflict Resolution Policy","Further, it is envisioned that the policy will serve as guide to the optimum allocation of land among competing uses within the framework of sustainable development.",""],[1,"125","1","Land Use Policy Conflict Resolution Mechanism","It will also provide a mechanism for resolving land use policy conflicts by taking into consideration the principles of social equity and economic efficiency.",""],[1,"125","4","National Soil and Water Conservation Program","a National Soil and Water Conservation Program will be established as the framework for addressing the problem of land degradation.",""],[1,"234","3","Reforestation in Priority River Basins","The Department of Environment and Natural Resources (DENR) continues to intensify reforestation activities, particularly in 18 priority river basins.","Department of Environment and Natural Resources (DENR)"],[1,"234","3","Deforestation Control Through Executive Order 23","EO 23 was issued to curb deforestation of remaining natural and residual forests",""],[1,"234","3","Reforestation Intensification Through Executive Order 26","EO 26, to intensify reforestation activities.",""],[1,"234","4","Forest Protection Programs","To sustain these positive gains, forest protection programs will be intensively pursued with civil society organizations (CSOs) and the private sector.","DENR"],[1,"234","4","Commodity Road Map for Timber and Non-Timber Plantations","As the lead agency, the DENR will develop a commodity road map for timber and non- timber plantations within NGP sites, as well as in Integrated Forest Management Agreement (IFMA) areas, to harness the forests' production potential.","DENR"],[1,"234","6","Timber Harvesting Moratorium and Anti-Illegal Logging Task Force","Executive Order No. 23 \"Declaring a Moratorium on the Cutting and Harvesting of Timber in the Natural and Residual Forest and Creating the Anti-Illegal Logging Task Force issued February 2011",""],[1,"236","1","Carbon Sequestration Assessment for the National Greening Program","DENR will also explore the NGP's potential on carbon sequestration following established standards in the Philippine National REDD (Reduced Emissions from Deforestation and Forest Degradation)-Plus Strategy.","DENR"],[1,"236","3","Expansion and Strengthening of NIPAS through ICCAs and LCAs","Efforts are also underway to expand and strengthen NIPAS by establishing indigenous community conserved areas (ICCAs) and local conservation areas (LCAs) managed by local government units (LGUs).",""],[1,"236","5","Biodiversity Area Establishment and Protected Area Management","Sustaining conservation efforts are greatly dependent on the availability of adequate financial resources particularly in the establishment of additional key biodiversity areas, effective management of proclaimed PAs and continuous implementation of conservation programs for threatened species.",""],[1,"247","12","Forest Reforestation and Protection Programme","Forest quality, which will serve as habitat to the threatened species, is improved through reforestation and protection efforts.",""],[1,"247","12","Forest Conservation Financing and Legal Enforcement","Adequate financial resources are timely provided and relevant laws are strictly implemented.",""],[1,"249","5","Philippine National REDD-Plus Strategy","Forest protection activities will be strengthened through: (a) the Philippine National REDD-Plus Strategy;",""],[1,"249","5","Forest Manager Capacity Improvement for Fire and Pest Response","capacity improvement of forest managers in addressing forest fires, pest and diseases;",""],[1,"249","5","Forest Patrol Support Facilities","provision of support facilities in patrolling forests;",""],[1,"249","5","Anti-Illegal Logging Campaign Strengthening","strengthening of the anti-illegal logging campaign.",""],[1,"250","1","Protected Area Management Strengthening","management of PAs will be strengthened by: (a) assessing the effectiveness of PA management; (b) establishing additional critical habitats and key biodiversity areas; (c) issuing security of tenure and providing alternative livelihood for local communities; (d) completing maps for all PAs under NIPAS; and (e) preparing PA management plans incorporating CCA/M and DRRM considerations.",""],[1,"250","3","Biodiversity Conservation Initiatives","The following biodiversity conservation initiatives will be continuously implemented: (a) National Biosafety Framework; (b) Nagoya Protocol; (c) Updated National Wetland Action Plan; (d) Coral Triangle Initiative National Plan of Action; (e) Sulu-Sulawesi Marine Eco-region Conservation Plan; (f) Integrated Coastal Management (ICM) program; (g) 2012-2020 Sustainable Coral Reef Ecosystem Management Program; (h) cave management, protection and conservation programs; and (i) the \"Adopt-a-Wildlife Species\" program.",""],[1,"251","3","Protected Areas Ecotourism Development Initiative","Harnessing the potential of PAs in ecotourism will help improve not only the areas' environmental quality through improved ENR management but also the rural communities' state of living through additional livelihood and income, and the empowerment of the marginalized, including women and indigenous peoples.","DENR-Protected Areas and Wildlife Bureau"],[1,"258","2","Forestland Boundary Delimitation and Oversight Law","This will provide permanent boundaries of forestlands in the country, set guidelines in determining the specific limits of forestlands, and create a national review and evaluation committee as implementation oversight in the actual marking of forest lines.",""],[1,"258","4","Sustainable Forest Ecosystems Management Strategy Adoption","This will adopt the Sustainable Forest Ecosystems Management Strategy as the overarching policy framework for all plans and programs in the forestry sector, identify the river basins and component watersheds as basic planning units in forest resources management, and recognize the administrative jurisdiction of LGUs and owners of ancestral domains as the basic management unit in forestry.",""],[1,"331","16","Protected Areas Classification and Administration","The classification and administration of all designated protected areas to maintain essential ecological processes and life-support systems, to preserve genetic diversity, to ensure sustainable use of resources found therein, and to maintain their natural conditions to the greatest extent possible.",""],[1,"337","9","Performance-Based Forest Conservation Incentive System","A proposed incentive system for reducing GHG emissions.",""],[1,"339","4","National Integrated Protected Areas System Establishment and Management","An act providing for the establishment and management of national integrated protected protected areas system, defining its scope and coverage, and for other purposes.",""]],"32":[[1,"243","8","Environmental Law Enforcement Strengthening","Strengthen the enforcement of solid waste management, hazardous waste management, clean air and water act",""],[1,"243","18","Multi-Stakeholder Environmental and Natural Resources Governance Partnership","13. Strengthen multi-stakeholder participation and partnership in ENR management and governance",""],[1,"243","19","Continuous Capacity Building, Institutional Strengthening and IEC Campaign","Continuous capacity building, institutional strengthening and IEC campaign",""],[1,"249","7","Environmental Law Enforcement and Green Courts Advocacy","Stakeholders, including CSOs, local communities and IPs, will be involved in the vigorous enforcement of environmental laws and policies, promotion of environmental justice, and in advocating the resolution of ENR cases through Supreme Court-designated green courts.",""],[1,"249","7","Strengthened Natural Resources Policy Compliance and Enforcement","Strict implementation of natural resources policies will be strengthened, particularly on the compliance of mining companies with environmental and social development commitments; apprehension of illegal logging and fishing, poaching and trading of endangered species; and reversion of abandoned, underutilized and unproductive coastal fishponds to mangroves.",""],[1,"257","2","Stakeholder Participation Enabling Mechanisms for Environmental Governance","Enabling mechanisms will be created to encourage greater participation of stakeholders, including women and Filipino migrants, in CCA/M, DRRM and ENR governance.",""],[1,"257","2","Community-Based Environmental Resource Management","This will be achieved through: (a) community-based ENR management efforts;",""],[1,"257","2","Public-Private Partnership Promotion for Environmental Management","promotion of public-private partnership in ENR management;",""],[1,"257","2","Mandatory Creation of Environmental and Natural Resources Offices for LGUs","mandatory creation of ENR offices for LGUs;",""],[1,"257","2","Stewardship Agreements and Contracts for Community Environmental Management","stewardship agreements and contracts between government and community.",""],[1,"257","3","ENR Capacity Building and Public Awareness Programme","A key in sustaining ENR management gains is to continuously build capacities and educate managers, policy and planning officers, technical personnel, law enforcers, and the general public.",""],[1,"257","3","ENR Stakeholder Coordination Mechanism Institutionalization","Strengthening of ENR institutions will require institutionalization of various stakeholder coordination mechanisms, as mandated by different ENR laws, for greater transparency and accountability in environmental governance.",""],[1,"257","3","ENR Training and Communication Initiative","Trainings, seminars and other communication tools will be provided to instill awareness and build consciousness on ENR management.",""],[1,"257","3","Women’s Participation and Gender Mainstreaming in ENR Management","Women's enhanced roles in ENR management will be highlighted through policies, capacity building and gender mainstreaming mechanisms.",""],[1,"257","6","Gender Mainstreaming for Women's Environmental Participation","Women's enhanced roles in environment and natural resource management will be highlighted through policies, capacity building and gender mainstreaming mechanisms.",""]],"33":[[1,"243","14","Waste Management Technology Promotion and Recycling Market Development","Promote appropriate technology for waste management and establishment of sustainable markets for recyclables and recycled products",""],[1,"254","7","Strict Enforcement of RA 9003 for Solid Waste Management","LGUs prioritize strategies that will help reduce waste and improve solid waste management by strictly implementing RA 9003.",""],[1,"254","9","Environmental Compliance and Waste Management Enforcement Measures","The government will strictly enforce the following: (a) industry compliance with environmental standards; (b) compliance with emission-testing and mandatory vehicle inspection and maintenance; (c) full establishment of monitoring stations in Metro Manila and other major urban centers; (d) publication of the list of non-environmentally acceptable packaging and products; (e) compliance on the establishment of disposal facilities and MRFs; (f) establishment of a separate cell for disposal of treated healthcare wastes; (g) LGU compliance in the submission of SWM Plans; and (h) conversion of wastes into useful resources.",""],[1,"255","3","LGU-Wide Ecological Solid Waste Management Systems","The continuous implementation of ecological solid waste management (ESWM) will focus on the establishment of LGU-wide ESWM systems.",""],[1,"255","3","Recycling Market Development Support","The promotion of recycling will be supported by markets capable of converting recycled and recyclable materials to productive use.",""],[1,"255","3","Demand Stimulation for Recycled Products","Various options to stimulate market and consumer demand for recyclable and recycled products will be exhausted.",""],[1,"259","4","Amendment of the Ecological Solid Waste Management Act","Amending the Ecological SWM Act will reconcile provisions of other laws on fines, penalties and local taxation (RA 7160), environmental impact assessment (PD 1586), air emissions (RA 8749), environmental education (RA 9512), compost quality requirements (RA 10068), climate-proofing of SWM facilities (RA 9729), and incentives (EO 226).",""],[1,"259","4","Update Hazardous Waste Management and Disposal Framework","the Toxic Substances and Hazardous and Nuclear Waste Control Act needs to be updated to provide a framework on management and disposal of toxic, hazardous and nuclear wastes, including e-wastes;",""],[1,"274","5","Expansion of Sanitary Landfills and Materials Recovery Facilities","around 1,500 LGUs and 32,000 barangays still need to be covered by additional sanitary landfills and materials recovery facilities, respectively, until 2016.",""],[1,"274","5","E-Waste Management Legislation and Infrastructure Framework","Specific legislation, policy framework and infrastructure facilities are needed for managing the country's e-wastes.",""],[1,"284","10","Solid Waste Management Act Amendment","Amendment of Solid Waste Management Act, to harmonize conflicting/ overlapping provisions with existing laws on fines, penalties, and local taxation (RA 7160), environmental impact assessment (PD 1586, s. 1978), air emissions (RA 8749), environmental education (RA 9512), compost quality requirements (RA 10068), climate-proofing of facilities (RA 9729), and incentives (EO 226, s. 1987); and, to incorporate appropriate management of electronic wastes",""],[1,"290","8","Waste-to-Energy Facilities Development and Operation","Development and Operation of Waste-to-Energy Facilities",""],[1,"291","6","Philippine National Solid Waste Management Strategy Implementation","the government will strictly implement the Philippine National Solid Waste Management Strategy",""],[1,"291","6","Review of Solid Waste and Clean Air Acts on Incineration Policy","both the Solid Waste Management and Philippine Clean Air Acts will be revisited in connection with the policy on incineration technology",""],[1,"291","8","Philippine National Solid Waste Management Strategy Implementation","The government will strictly implement the Philippine National Solid Waste Management Strategy, which is anchored on the National Solid Waste Management Framework adopted in 2004.",""],[1,"316","11","Integrated Solid Waste Management System","The systematic administration of activities which provide for segregation at source, segregated transportation, storage, transfer, processing, treatment, and disposal of solid waste and all other waste management activities which do not harm the environment.",""],[1,"339","15","Ecological Solid Waste Management Program","An act providing for an ecological solid waste management program, creating the necessary institutional mechanisms and incentives, declaring certain acts prohibited and providing penalties.",""],[1,"342","1","Engineered Waste Disposal Site Development and Operation","A waste disposal site designed, constructed, operated and maintained in a manner that exerts engineering control over significant potential environmental impacts arising from the development and operation of the facility.",""]],"34":[[1,"237","1","Coral Triangle Initiative National Plan of Action for Sustainable Marine Management","Marine eco-region and West Philippine Seas-have been designated as areas for sustainable management under the Coral Triangle Initiative (CTI) National Plan of Action.",""],[1,"247","20","Stakeholder Partnerships for Coastal Management","Establish partnerships among stakeholders in coastal management activities (DENR, DA, NCIP, LGUs)","DENR | DA | NCIP | LGUs"],[1,"247","20","Local Policy and Budget Support for Coastal and Marine Protected Areas","LGUs recognize their role in ENR management (e.g., formulation of local policies and provision of budget for projects that will support effective management of coastal and marine protected areas)","LGUs"],[1,"250","4","Local Government Coastal and Marine Resource Management Empowerment","This is necessary to empower LGUs to manage coastal and marine resources and provide preferential rights to small fisherfolk.",""],[1,"258","3","National Integrated Coastal Management Program","A National Integrated Coastal Management (ICM) Program will guide LGUs in formulating and implementing ICM programs in their respective areas.",""],[1,"258","5","Coastal MPA Establishment and Management Incentive Mechanism","This will mandate coastal LGUs to establish at least one MPA within their area, sanction LGUs that fail to establish MPAs, allow the DENR to continue to manage MPAs established under the NIPAS, and develop incentive mechanisms to promote effective management of MPAs;","DENR"],[1,"258","6","Institutionalize Integrated Coastal Management as a National Strategy","This will institutionalize ICM as a national strategy of sustainable development of coastal and marine environment and resources.","Department of Education | National Economic and Development Authority"],[1,"319","7","Integrated Coastal Management National Strategy","An order adopting an Integrated Coastal Management as a National Strategy to ensure the sustainable development of the country's coastal and marine environment and resources in order to achieve food security, sustainable livelihood, poverty alleviation and reduction of vulnerability to natural hazards, while preserving ecological integrity.","DENR"],[1,"319","8","Integrated Coastal and Marine Development Support Mechanisms","The EO seeks to address environmental and socioeconomic issues in a and integrated manner in order to promote optimum resource utilization and comprehensive sustainable coastal and marine development; and establishes support mechanisms for its implementation.",""]],"35":[[1,"234","2","Climate Change Adaptation and Disaster Risk Reduction Mainstreaming","The past two years focused on preparatory activities toward full operation of long- term actions on climate change adaptation and mitigation (CCA/M) and disaster risk reduction and management (DRRM).",""],[1,"242","5","Institutionalization of Climate Change Adaptation and Disaster Risk Reduction Measures","It highlights strategies that increase resiliency from climate risks and natural disasters through institutionalization of CCA/M and DRRM measures, as shown in Figure 9.5.",""],[1,"243","12","Development and Adoption of Vulnerability Assessment Tools","Development and adoption of more effective Vulnerability Assessment tools",""],[1,"244","8","Climate Change Adaptation and Disaster Risk Reduction Mainstreaming Initiative","This strategy involves: (a) supporting initiatives for mainstreaming CCA/M and DRRM in the development process; (b) integrating CCA/M and DRRM in all education levels and in specialized technical training and research programs; (c) formulating criteria for identifying CCA/M and DRRM responsive projects; and (d) adopting a responsive national and local legal and policy framework on CCA/M and DRRM through multi-stakeholder dialogues.",""],[1,"245","3","Science-Based Vulnerability Assessment Tools Development and Adoption","Developing and adopting science-based VA tools will allow for the proper identification of highly susceptible communities, which will be useful for formulating DRRM plans.",""],[1,"256","3","Nationwide High-Resolution Elevation Data Acquisition","The acquisition of nationwide high-resolution elevation data from Interferometric Synthetic Aperture Radar and satellite imageries will support geo-hazard mapping and serve as the primary inputs to the production of multi-scale topographic base maps.",""],[1,"256","5","Provincial Climate Projection Downscaling for Development Planning","it is necessary to further downscale the outputs to the provincial level to aid local development planning;",""],[1,"256","6","Fast-Track Vulnerability Assessment and Climate Risk Mapping","Fast-track VA, mapping of highly vulnerable areas, communities and priority sectors and integration of CCA/M and DRRM in development plans and programs",""],[1,"256","7","Climate-Sensitive and Disaster-Risk Community Identification and Mainstreaming of CCA/M and DRRM","All these will identify climate-sensitive and disaster-risk communities and mainstream CCA/M and DRRM in sectoral, development and land use plans.",""],[1,"257","5","Integrated Land Use Planning and Policy Harmonization","it is expected to harmonize sector- spatial land use policies to address competing uses of limited land resources and cross-cutting land use issues (e.g., food security, settlement development, industry development and environmental protection), and integrate ongoing CCA/M and DRRM efforts in national and local development planning;",""],[1,"259","3","Weather Forecasting and Warning Services Modernization Program","This will enhance the agency's capability in providing timely and reliable weather forecasting and warning services by setting up an interagency body that will formulate the modernization program and establish a modernization fund to finance said program;",""],[1,"290","7","Telemetry Equipment Improvement and Restoration for Flood Control Operations","Improvement/Restoration of Telemetry Equipment of the Effective Flood Control Operation System (EFCOS)",""],[1,"291","2","Flood Forecasting and Warning System Improvement","The government will improve the existing flood forecasting and warning systems through strengthened coordination among the National Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council (NDRRMC), Advanced Science and Technology Institute (ASTI), Philippine Atmospheric, Geophysical and Astronomical Services Administration (PAGASA), DPWH, Metro Manila Development Authority and LGUs.","National Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council (NDRRMC) | Advanced Science and Technology Institute (ASTI) | Philippine Atmospheric, Geophysical and Astronomical Services Administration (PAGASA) | DPWH | Metro Manila Development Authority | LGUs"],[1,"319","10","National Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Institutionalization","An EO adopting the SNAP and its 18 priority programs and projects in order reduce economic losses from the adverse impacts of climate variability including extreme events as the country undergoes economic growth, population increase and rapid urbanization.",""],[1,"331","14","Climate Change Adaptation Framework Strategy","A framework strategy of the Philippines that serves as basis for a program for climate change planning, research and development, extension, and monitoring of activities to protect vulnerable communities from the adverse effects of climate change.",""],[1,"334","7","Climate Change Adaptation Financing Fund","A special fund in the National Treasury, established under Republic Act 10174 of 2012, for the financing of adaptation programs and project based on the National Strategic Framework and Program on Climate Change.",""],[1,"340","10","Climate Change Mainstreaming Framework Strategy and Programme","An act mainstreaming climate change into government policy formulations, establishing the framework strategy and program for climate change.",""]],"36":[[1,"239","1","Air Quality Monitoring and Emissions Control Program","policies and programs providing additional monitoring stations, imposing higher emission standards for vehicles, intensifying the anti-smoke belching program (Bantay Tambutso) and monitoring major industry and stationary sources of pollution (Bantay Tsimneya)","Department of Transportation and Communication | DENR-Environmental Management Bureau"],[1,"243","11","Air and Water Quality Standards Update and Monitoring","Update air and water quality standards and intensity monitoring",""],[1,"252","3","Environmental Quality Improvement Programme","the quality of air, land and water will be improved to meet the minimum safety standards",""],[1,"253","5","Local Air Pollution Reduction Ordinances and Budget Support","LGUs prioritize strategies that will help reduce air pollution through provision of local ordinances and budget support to programs contributing to the achievement of this outcome.",""],[1,"255","1","Air and Water Quality Standards Monitoring and Enforcement Program","Activities on updating and monitoring of air and water quality standards include the following: (a) formulation of science-based policies, abatement measures and strategies; (b) strengthening implementation of Bantay Tsimineya, Bantay Tambutso, Adopt-an-Estero Program and rehabilitation programs of Pasig River, Laguna Lake, and Manila Bay, among others; (c) establishment of additional environmental management areas; (d) installation of additional PM10 and PM2 monitoring stations for a more comprehensive analysis; and (e) promotion of residual waste management, among others.",""],[1,"275","19","Air Quality Improvement Support Measures","Support measures to improve air quality",""],[1,"338","17","Toxic Substances and Hazardous Waste Control Act","An act to control toxic substances and hazardous and nuclear wastes, providing penalties for violations thereof.",""],[1,"339","13","Comprehensive Air Pollution Control Policy","An act providing for a comprehensive air pollution control policy.",""],[1,"340","2","Comprehensive Water Quality Management Act","An act providing for a comprehensive water quality management.",""]],"38":[[1,"243","15","Research and Development and Extension Support","Support research and development and extension",""],[1,"243","16","Environmental Research, Development and Extension Programme","Pursue research, development and extension to im- prove the quality of the environment",""],[1,"243","17","Knowledge Management Systems and Tools Improvement","12. Improve Knowledge Management (KM) systems and tools",""],[1,"245","4","Priority Research on Climate Change Impacts and Low-Carbon Technologies","Priority research in the next three years will include, but not be limited to, the impacts of climate change on natural ecosystems, CCA/M technologies (e.g., resistant planting stocks), and cost-benefit analysis of eco-friendly and low- carbon technologies.",""],[1,"251","2","Collaborative ENR Research and Study Programme","The government will collaborate with research and academic institutions on ENR in conducting studies focused on, but not limited to, the following areas: (a) approaches to effective ENR management; (b) extent of forest cover needed to sustain ecosystem services; (c) carrying capacity of ecosystems; (d) geological assessment and exploration of undiscovered mineral resources; and (e) studies linking gender concerns and resource use, to profile women's roles and opportunities in ENR initiatives.",""],[1,"251","2","ENR Research Accessibility Mechanism","Mechanisms to improve the accessibility of ENR-related researches will also be established.",""],[1,"255","4","Research and Development for Pollution Control and Clean Technologies","RD&E will be pursued to: (a) identify air and water pollution impacts to human health and economy; (b) develop and replicate low-cost technologies to optimize solid waste recycling, reuse, and recovery, including the conversion of residual organic materials into clean renewable energy; (c) develop clean and energy- efficient technologies; (d) develop and propagate low-cost non-combustion technologies for infectious and hazardous wastes; (e) identify environmentally sound management and disposal of toxic and hazardous waste, including e-waste; (f) conduct life cycle assessment of proposed non-environmentally acceptable packaging and products; and (g) develop and manufacture non-mercury-based technologies used in healthcare facilities.",""],[1,"256","8","ENR Indicators, Tools, and Methodologies Development","This effort will address demand for ENR indicators, tools and methodologies that will help determine sustainable use of ENR, correlate sustainable use of ENR with economic growth, and make informed development planning and policy analysis;",""]],"39":[[1,"242","1","Water Sector Governance Restructuring","A comprehensive review and subsequent restructuring of water sector governance will help address fragmented and weak water resources management.",""],[1,"242","1","Integrated Water Resources Management Adoption","The sector also needs to adopt the principles of the Integrated Water Resources Management (IWRM);",""],[1,"242","1","Waterworks and Service Provider Regulation","regulate the management of waterworks, water supply, and sewerage service providers;",""],[1,"242","1","Water Policy Enforcement Agency Designation","and identify agencies that enforce water-related policies (see Chapter 10: Accelerating infrastructure development).",""],[1,"249","4","Integrated River Basin Management Framework","The IRBM will serve as the systematic framework for ridge-to-reef management (i.e., forest management through comprehensive river administration system for flood control, water use and environmental conservation).",""],[1,"249","4","River Basin Master Plans for Priority Rivers","Along with this is the completion of river basin master plans for 18 priority rivers.",""],[1,"281","5","Eco-efficient Water Infrastructure Development","As an overarching strategy in the pursuit of water security, eco-efficient approaches/ interventions for developing water infrastructure will be considered.",""],[1,"281","5","River Basin Master Plan Development","To guide water security objectives, river basin master plans will be developed, including water resource assessments or water availability studies particularly for water- critical areas, to identify new water sources for domestic, commercial, industrial, irrigation and other needs.",""],[1,"284","2","Water Resources Sector Apex Agency Establishment","establishment of a lead/ apex agency in the water resources sector for the coordination of policies, plans and programs related to water resources",""],[1,"284","2","River Basin Assessment and Master Planning","prioritizing water resources assessments and developing river basin master plans in priority river basins",""],[1,"284","2","Water Supply and Sanitation Coordination Agency","creation of a lead coordinating agency for water supply and sanitation (WSS) provision",""],[1,"288","3","Water Resources Sector Apex Agency Establishment","the following interventions will be pursued: (a) establishment of a lead/apex agency in the water resources sector for the coordination of policies, plans, and programs related to water resources",""],[1,"288","3","River Basin Assessment and Master Planning","prioritization of water resources assessments and development of river basin master plans in priority river basins",""],[1,"288","3","Unified WSS Coordination and Financing Framework","creation of a lead coordinating agency and adoption of a unified financing framework/policy for WSS provision",""],[1,"288","6","Unified Water Supply and Sanitation Financing Framework","a unified financing framework/policy will be developed.",""],[1,"326","13","Water Resources Sector Interagency Coordination Committee","An interagency committee for the Water Resources Sector established through NEDA Board Committee on Infrastructure (INFRACOM) Resolution No. 2, Series of 2008.",""]],"40":[[1,"46","10","Rural Water Supply and Sanitation Expansion","provide water supply and sanitation facilities in rural and hard-to-reach areas",""],[1,"259","5","Resource Regulation and Water Efficiency Improvement","This will strengthen resource regulation and promote more efficient use of water resources.",""],[1,"281","6","Raw Water Pricing Exploration and Stakeholder Capacity Development","Raw water pricing will also be explored and complemented with capacity development for stakeholders, particularly for the agriculture sector (which is the largest consumer of water), to promote efficient water utilization/extraction.",""],[1,"281","6","Domestic and Municipal Water Supply Expansion","Domestic and municipal water supply provision targets the increase of Level III and 24-hour service coverage and the reduction of non-revenue water.",""],[1,"281","6","Water Supply Provision for Priority Tourism Destinations","the government will ensure adequate water supply in priority tourism destinations under the NTDP.",""],[1,"281","7","Metro Manila Water Source Diversification","For Metro Manila, new water sources will be identified and developed to eliminate the risks arising from being dependent on a single water source for various consumption needs.",""],[1,"284","11","Water Code IRR Amendment for Resource Regulation","Amendment of the IRR of the Water Code, to strengthen resource regulation and promote more efficient use of water resources",""],[1,"285","3","Water Supply Infrastructure and Capacity Development Support for Waterless Poor Areas","Adequate water supply infrastructure and capacity development support will be provided to the target waterless poor areas.",""],[1,"285","3","Bottom-Up Planning and Budgeting for Rural Water and Sanitation Services","Provision of WSS for rural and hard- to-reach areas will be augmented through the bottom-up planning and budgeting approach,143 among others.",""],[1,"285","3","Regional Water and Sanitation Hub Expansion","The government will scale up coverage of regional water and sanitation (WatSan) hubs using standardized local capacity development materials, such as WatSan toolboxes and localized customer service codes, among others.",""],[1,"285","3","Community-Based Zero Open Defecation Programme","Zero open defecation at the barangay level through community-based methodologies, as well as mainstreaming of sanitation in emergency/disaster response areas, will also be improved.",""]],"41":[[1,"43","1","Human Capital Enhancement for Workforce Development","the government will facilitate enhancement of the human capital of the present and potential workforce to ensure that they have the knowledge and skills that are relevant to the needs of industry and services, particularly the key sectors.",""],[1,"43","1","Industry-Led TVET and Higher Education Curriculum Design","Firms will be encouraged to provide inputs to the design of technical-vocational education and training (TVET) and higher education institution (HEI) programs to increase the employability of the workforce, especially from the poor households.",""],[1,"44","8","Education Investment and Public Investment Quality Improvement","Investment in education will be increased and the quality of public investments will be improved.",""],[1,"44","9","K to 12 Education Reform Program","The K to 12 program represents the government's commitment to investing in education.",""],[1,"45","1","Equitable Distribution of Educational Materials and Facilities","materials and educational facilities are provided.",""],[1,"45","2","TVET Access Expansion and Workforce Competency Development","Strategies consist of expanding access to quality TVET and developing workforce competencies required in key growth areas, as well as in leadership, management and innovation.",""],[1,"45","2","Higher Education Student Performance Improvement","The Updated Plan will focus on improving the performance of higher education students in licensure examinations across disciplines.",""],[1,"46","10","Student Classroom Gap Reduction Initiative","close the student-classroom gap",""]],"42":[[1,"157","10","Conducive Learning Institutions Development","This involves: (a) creating conducive learning institutions;",""],[1,"157","10","Affirmative Action for Learners with Special Needs","providing affirmative action to learners with special needs and those in special circumstances;",""],[1,"157","10","Private Sector Engagement for Basic Education Expansion","engaging the private sector in broadening more opportunities for basic education;",""],[1,"157","10","Technology-Enabled Expansion of Education Access","using technology in expanding reach.",""],[1,"157","11","Enhanced Learner-Centered Curriculum Development","the government will pursue the: (a) development of enhanced learner-centered curriculum",""],[1,"157","11","Instructional Materials and Equipment Provision","the government will pursue the: (b) provision of adequate instructional materials and equipment",""],[1,"157","11","Teacher Quality Improvement and Professional Development","the government will pursue the: (c) improvement of quality of instruction and professional development of teachers.",""],[1,"157","12","K to 12 Program Implementation Alignment and Synchronization","As the government gears towards full implementation of the K to 12 program, aligning and synchronizing efforts are crucial to achieve optimum use of resources.","DepEd"],[1,"157","12","Internal Systems and Processes Improvement in Education","the government, through the DepEd, will: (a) improve internal systems and processes;","DepEd"],[1,"158","1","Education Leadership and Management Capacity Building","leadership and management and build people capacities;",""],[1,"158","1","Stakeholder Participation Expansion in Basic Education Delivery","expand the network of stakeholders and enhance participation in the delivery of basic education.",""],[1,"158","1","Equitable Resource Targeting for Basic Education","These will be accompanied by the proper targeting of areas, prioritizing those with severe shortages to ensure equitable distribution of resources and address low performance in terms of education indicators among regions, divisions and schools.",""],[1,"328","8","K to 12 Basic Education Program","The K to 12 Program covers Kindergarten and 12 years of basic education (six years of primary education, four years of Junior High School, and two years of Senior High School [SHS])",""]],"43":[[1,"92","5","Market-Driven Senior Secondary Curriculum Reform","Market-driven education and training will be pursued to address the needs of the I&S sectors.","Department of Education"],[1,"92","6","University Participation in Technology Parks and Business Incubators","Colleges/universities will be encouraged to participate in technology parks and business incubator facilities and introduce entrepreneurship training in their curricula to inspire students to take research from the academe to firms.",""],[1,"92","7","Philippine Qualifications Framework","The competency of Filipino workers and professionals will be strengthened to prepare them for regional and global integration (e.g. AEC 2015) through the following: (a) Philippine Qualifications Framework;",""],[1,"92","7","Competitiveness Roadmaps for Professions","The competency of Filipino workers and professionals will be strengthened to prepare them for regional and global integration (e.g. AEC 2015) through the following: (b) competitiveness roadmaps of different professions;",""],[1,"92","7","Outcome-Based Education and Learning Outcomes Reform","The competency of Filipino workers and professionals will be strengthened to prepare them for regional and global integration (e.g. AEC 2015) through the following: (c) outcome-based education and the use of learning outcomes; and (d) continuing professional development.",""],[1,"92","7","Continuing Professional Development","The competency of Filipino workers and professionals will be strengthened to prepare them for regional and global integration (e.g. AEC 2015) through the following: (d) continuing professional development.",""],[1,"93","1","Workforce Enhancement Training Program for I&S Sectors","The government, through TESDA, will continuously provide enhancement trainings/programs to produce highly skilled Filipino workforce needed by the I&S sectors.",""]],"44":[[1,"147","12","TVET Workforce Competencies and Life Skills Development","Develop workforce competencies and life skills through TVET",""],[1,"158","4","TVET Access Expansion and Workforce Competency Development","Strategies consist of expanding access to quality TVET and developing workforce competencies required in key growth areas.",""],[1,"158","8","LGU TVET Capability-Building Programs","designing and developing capability-building programs for LGUs in establishing, managing and implementing TVET programs;",""],[1,"159","1","Technical Assistance for LGU-Led TVET Implementation","providing technical assistance to LGUs in the area of trainers development, curriculum and learning materials development, center administration, and assessment and certification;",""],[1,"159","1","LGU Partnership Models for TVET Delivery","developing viable models and partnership arrangements for LGU-led TVET implementation in the localities;",""],[1,"159","1","Community-Based Skills Development Support Mobilization","mobilizing multi-stakeholder support and participation in community-based skills development programs.",""],[1,"159","2","Expansion of Enterprise-Based Training Schemes","This will involve the following measures: (a) strengthening and promoting EBT schemes (e.g., dual training system, apprenticeship and \"learnership\" and on- the-job training as pre-employment modalities);",""],[1,"159","2","Workplace Skills Upgrading and Lifelong Learning Support","encouraging training in the workplace for skills upgrading, retooling and multi-skilling, and other skills development interventions to improve productivity and promote lifelong learning;",""],[1,"159","2","Private Sector Incentives for TVET Investment","pushing for the expansion of incentives for the private sector investing in TVET and making availment easier;",""],[1,"159","2","Scholarships and Assistance for TVET Participants","making available incentives such as scholarships and other assistance for EBT participating industries and technical-vocational institutions (TVIs);",""],[1,"159","2","Corporate Social Responsibility Support for TVET","tapping the corporate social responsibility programs of industry/private sector for TVET.",""],[1,"159","3","Agricultural Value-Adding and Agribusiness Training Programme","workers in the sector need to be trained on value-adding, agribusiness development and value-chain management.",""],[1,"160","4","Academe-Industry Linkage Strengthening Initiative","This will be pursued by strengthening the academe-industry linkages to address the problem of mismatch between competencies and jobs on the one hand, and to encourage research and development (R&D) collaboration between the two sectors, on the other.",""],[1,"328","14","Flexible TVET and College Progression System","A new system of education in the Philippines that allows learners to progress between TVET and college, and vice-versa.",""]],"45":[[1,"160","5","Curriculum Upgrading and Alignment Initiative","This will be pursued by (a) upgrading and aligning the curricula with international standards; and (b) identification of Centers of Excellence (COE) and Centers of Development (COD) capable of producing globally competitive graduates and cutting-edge research outputs relevant to the needs of the disciplines and the country's development objectives.",""],[1,"160","6","Higher Education Institutional Consolidation and Harmonization","This is to improve efficiency in the delivery of quality programs, minimize duplication, and promote harmonization and complementation of program standards between and among public and private HEIs.",""],[1,"160","7","Revision of Programs, Policies, and Standards for Learning Competency-Based Standards","This will be implemented through the continuing revision of programs, policies, standards along learning competency-based standards or learning outcomes-a",""]],"46":[[1,"91","1","Science, Technology and Innovation Capacity Building","Increasing productivity will require harnessing science, technology and innovation, enhancing the competencies of the labor force, and expanding industry cluster development.",""],[1,"91","2","Local Research and Development Capacity Building","The country will make full use of existing technologies to make local industries competitive and innovative while building local research and development (R&D) capacity to address local problems.",""],[1,"91","2","Transformative Technology R&D Capability Development","The government will build local R&D capabilities for transformative, cutting-edge and sustainable technologies with broad applications (e.g. information and communications technology or ICT, biotechnology, advanced manufacturing technology and new materials technology, among others).",""],[1,"91","2","National Research and Development Agenda","To ensure the efficient use of resources, a national R&D agenda will be adopted that will guide relevant government agencies on the prioritization of programs.",""],[1,"91","7","National Research and Development Agenda","A national research and development agenda will be adopted that will guide relevant government agencies on the prioritization of programs.",""],[1,"92","2","Networking and Cooperation Mechanism for Filipino Scientists and Engineers","The government will strengthen the networking, cooperation and exchange mechanisms to mobilize Filipino scientists and engineers to support social and technological innovations at the community level.",""],[1,"92","3","Scientist and Engineer Mobilization Mechanism for Community Innovation","The government will strengthen the networking, cooperation and exchange mechanisms to mobilize Filipino scientists and engineers to support social and technological innovations at the community level.",""],[1,"92","4","Expansion of Science and Technology Graduate Scholarship Programs","Science and technology (S&T) graduate scholarship programs, such as the Engineering R&D and Technology (ERDT) Program and the Accelerated S&T Human Resource Development Program (ASTHRDP) will be expanded to promote S&T-related professions.",""],[1,"92","4","Universalized Undergraduate S&T Scholarship Program","The undergraduate S&T scholarship program for poor but deserving students will be democratized with at least one DOST scholar in each town by 2016.",""],[1,"92","4","Regional Philippine Science High School Campus Establishment","A Philippine Science High School (PSHS) campus will also be established in each region.",""],[1,"117","3","Partnerships for RD&E and Training Initiatives","Encourage partnership between and among higher education institutions, LGUs, private and business sector on RD&E and training initiatives;",""]],"47":[[1,"79","5","Infrastructure Development Investment Programme","government has been investing heavily in infrastructure development.",""],[1,"83","3","Infrastructure Backlog Reduction and Spending Scale-Up","the government ramps up its effort to address infrastructure backlogs and targets infrastructure spending at 5 percent of GDP by 2016",""],[1,"83","3","Disaster-Affected Area Rehabilitation and Reconstruction","The bulk of the rehabilitation and reconstruction efforts in areas affected by disasters, especially Typhoon Yolanda, is expected to be undertaken in 2014",""],[1,"88","4","Adequate Infrastructure Provision","The second strategy is to provide adequate infrastructure.",""],[1,"266","2","Public Infrastructure Investment Expansion","The overall strategy outlined in this chapter is to invest massively in infrastructure development by increasing public infrastructure spending to at least five percent of the country's gross domestic product (GDP) by 2016.",""],[1,"266","5","Infrastructure Support for Development Outcomes","Moving forward, the country's infrastructure development agenda will focus on providing the necessary infrastructure support for attaining and sustaining the development outcomes of the five key result areas of the Aquino administration, while further reaffirming the government's commitments to address issues earlier identified in 2010.",""],[1,"272","6","Public-Private Partnership Infrastructure Development Framework","The PPP approach is a major strategy to mobilize the private sector as a partner in infrastructure development.",""],[1,"273","4","Value Engineering and Value Analysis for Priority Projects","The NEDA introduced the conduct of Value Engineering/Value Analysis (VE/VA) in appraising priority projects to ensure that these are not overdesigned or over-specified and to minimize cost overruns, project implementation delays and changes in scopes of works.","NEDA"],[1,"275","18","Infrastructure Investment Optimization","Optimize infrastructure investment",""],[1,"275","20","Public Infrastructure Spending Increase","The overall strategy is to increase public infrastructure spending to enhance the quality, adequacy and accessibility of infrastructure facilities and services.",""],[1,"275","21","Public Infrastructure Spending Increase","the government will increase public infrastructure spending from 2.2 percent of GDP in 2012 to at least 5.0 percent by 2016",""],[1,"275","21","Public-Private Partnership Financing for Infrastructure","The spending will still be supplemented by private sector investments through PPP",""],[1,"275","21","Synchronized Planning and Budgeting Efficiency Reform","it will be anchored on a conscious effort to increase efficiency based on the synchronized planning and budgeting processes",""],[1,"284","6","Amendment of the BOT Law","Amendment of the BOT Law, to further enhance transparency, competitiveness, impartiality and mobilization of private sector for infrastructure development",""],[1,"284","14","Right-of-Way and Site Acquisition Law Amendment","Amendment of law on right-of-way, site or location acquisition for government projects, to balance State and private rights",""],[1,"288","4","Institutionalization of Value Engineering and Value Analysis","NEDA will continue to study the full institutionalization of VE/VA and address concerns including the optimal timing of conducting VE/VA and consideration of social component in VE/VA activities, among others.","NEDA"],[1,"313","2","Public Asset Concession and Management Delegation","The award by the government to a qualified private entity of the responsibility for financing, operating, expanding, maintaining and managing specific Government-owned assets.",""],[1,"328","3","Public-Private Joint Venture Investment Framework","An arrangement whereby a private sector entity or a group of private sector entities on one hand, and a Government Entity or a group of Government Entities on the other hand, contribute money/capital, services, assets (including equipment, land, intellectual property or anything of value), or a combination of any or all of the foregoing to undertake an investment activity.",""]],"48":[[1,"255","2","Clean Energy Promotion and Green Architecture Incentives","This includes promoting the use of clean fuel and indigenous resources as sources of clean energy, advocating green architecture, and devising related tax or market incentives mechanisms.",""],[1,"273","1","Net Metering Renewable Energy Incentive Scheme","The Net Metering Program, a consumer-based RE incentive scheme that offsets DU-provided electric energy with electric power generated by end- users from eligible RE facilities and delivered to local DUs, has also been initiated.",""],[1,"273","1","Renewable Portfolio Standards Review","the Renewable Portfolio Standards, which requires suppliers to source part of their supply from RE resources, is being reviewed.",""],[1,"282","9","278.4 MW Renewable Energy Project","278.4 MW Renewable Energy Project",""],[1,"292","11","Promotion of Clean Alternative Fuels and Technologies","The use of clean and environment-friendly alternative fuels and technologies, including increasing biofuel blend and use of natural gas, will be promoted in the energy sector.",""],[1,"292","11","National Energy Efficiency and Conservation Programme","energy efficiency and conservation will continue to be implemented through the NEECP (see strategy 3).",""],[1,"310","7","Greenhouse Gas Mitigation Measures","The prevention of greenhouse gas build-up in the earth's atmosphere by methods such as planting trees to absorb carbon dioxide or pumping carbon dioxide into underground reservoirs.",""],[1,"320","10","Renewable Electricity Purchase Obligation Mechanism","A policy mechanism that involves the obligation on the part of electric power industry participants to source electricity from renewable energy generation at a guaranteed fixed rate per kilowatt-hour for renewable energy generation for a given period of time.",""],[1,"337","17","Renewable Electricity Obligation Mechanism","A policy mechanism which places an obligation to electric power industry participants to source or produce a specified fraction of their electricity from eligible renewable energy resources.",""],[1,"340","4","Renewable Energy Development Framework and Strategic Utilization Program","An act that establishes the framework for the accelerated development and advancement of renewable energy resources, and the development of a strategic program to increase its utilization.",""]],"49":[[1,"38","1","Agrarian Reform Acceleration and Land Titling Programme","Agrarian reform will be fast-tracked; in particular, the distribution of individual land titles will be accelerated to provide greater security of tenure and access to finance for agrarian reform beneficiaries.",""],[1,"46","2","Technical Assistance for Local Land Use Planning","the Housing and Land Use Regulatory Board will continue to extend technical assistance to LGUs in the formulation and/or updating of comprehensive land use plans.",""]],"50":[[1,"69","6","Good Governance Mainstreaming in Government Institutions","the government will deeply embed good governance measures in the policies, processes, and practices of government institutions",""],[1,"69","6","Digital Public Service Delivery Improvement","A way of embedding these reforms is to leverage technology to radically improve the pace and quality of public service delivery",""],[1,"69","6","Inclusive Social and Economic Service Delivery Reform","The government will also ensure that the reforms actually bring immediate and substantial benefit to our people by way of adequate social and economic services, as well as inclusive growth",""],[1,"90","1","E-Commerce Law Implementation for Digital Public Services","The government will fully implement the e-Commerce law to ensure speedy and better delivery of government services and information, including health and education, especially in the countryside.",""],[1,"92","1","e-Government Master Plan Implementation","This will be complemented by the implementation of the e-Gov Master Plan (EO 47), which aims to broaden the access of citizens to government services (i.e., health and education) with the use of ICT.",""],[1,"92","1","ICT Infrastructure and Shared Services Rollout","This includes the provision of the needed ICT infrastructure and shared services, standards and interoperability for publicly funded systems, particularly the rolling out of the TV White Space Public Service Infrastructure.",""],[1,"92","1","Community e-Centers Expansion","The latter will serve as a platform for 1,500 community e-Centers covering 42,000 barangays.",""],[1,"275","10","ICT-Enabled Good Governance Initiative","Promote good governance through ICTs",""],[1,"275","10","Government Coordination and Process Streamlining Reform","Improve coordination and planning, streamline government processes.",""],[1,"287","10","E-Government Master Plan 2013-2016","The e-Government Master Plan 2013-2016 will serve as the blueprint for introducing innovations within government work processes, enhancing administrative productivity and allowing more citizen participation.",""],[1,"287","10","iGovPhil Shared Government Network Project","The iGovPhil Project will set up a government-shared network among agencies and other infrastructure for e-governance.",""],[1,"288","5","Medium-term ICT Harmonization Initiative","The government will ensure a systematic process for planning, budgeting, implementation, monitoring and evaluation of government-wide ICT programs and projects with the implementation of the Medium-term ICT Harmonization Initiative (MITHI) for FY 2014-2016",""],[1,"289","5","Government Web Hosting Service","It will also implement the Government Web Hosting Service, as issued through Administrative Order No. 39 (s. 2013), to enhance security and robustness of government websites.",""],[1,"317","1","Online Public Services Development","The development of online services for the public, providing services such as e-tax; business registration; birth, wedding, and death certificates; voting or public opinion polling; passport or identification renewal; social benefits; licenses and approvals, planning or business applications; or e-health.",""],[1,"317","1","Networked Government ICT Systems","Also included are networked ICT systems supporting various levels of government in the administration and delivery of mandated services.",""],[1,"323","2","Integrated Human Resource Management System","An integrated system encompassing the full cycle of human - from recruitment and hiring to retirement - initially focusing on an NPS that will remove ghost employees in the government payroll, as well as ensure the timely payment of government employees' insurance premiums.",""],[1,"323","4","Integrated Public Financial Management IT Solution","An integrated information technology (IT) solution that will improve efficiency in the use of public resources through real-time online accounting, monitoring and control of public funds, an improved cash management system, and a more systematic recording of all real and contingent liabilities of government.",""],[1,"330","11","E-Government and ICT Interoperability Support Initiative","An electronic-government and information and communication technology (ICT) support initiative that aims to harmonize and ensure interoperability among ICT-related resources, programs, and projects in all national government agencies (NGAs),as well as address the gaps in computer network and broadband connectivity within government.",""]],"51":[[1,"179","11","Anti-Corruption Efforts Intensification","Intensifying anti-corruption efforts is likewise important in earning citizens' trust.",""],[1,"191","6","Intensified Anti-Corruption Efforts","intensifying anti-corruption efforts is necessary to be able to make a significant dent in this area over time.",""],[1,"191","7","Strengthening Internal Control Systems for Public Funds","The first requires strengthening of internal control systems in relation to the generation and allocation of government funds;",""],[1,"191","7","Strict Enforcement of Anti-Corruption Penalties","the second involves strict enforcement of penalties against those found guilty of corrupt practices.",""],[1,"192","5","Revenue Integrity Protection and Anti-Corruption Enforcement","The Revenue Integrity Protection Service (RIPS), the Department of Finance's anti-corruption arm created under EO 259, will continue to prosecute public officers of its revenue-generating agencies who have committed acts of corruption and to improve the public's perception on the current state of corruption.","Department of Finance"],[1,"192","5","RIPS Case Management Software Acquisition and Customization","The acquisition and customization of case management software will aim to increase the sources of \"leads\" for RIPS through its case profiling function.",""],[1,"192","5","Integrity Investigation Skills Training for Revenue Agencies","To improve the quality of cases filed, training programs will be conducted and will focus on improving the investigative skills and technical knowledge of the Bureau of Internal Revenue (BIR) and Bureau of Customs (BOC).",""],[1,"192","6","Office of the Ombudsman Anti-Corruption Agenda","The Policy Thrust and 8-point Agenda from 2011 to 2018 to curtail corruption will focus on: (a) disposition of high-profile cases; (b) zero backlog; (c) improved \"survival\" rate of fact-finding; (d) enforced monitoring of referred cases; (e) improved responsiveness of public assistance; (f) improved anti-corruption policy and program coordination among sectors; (g) rationalization of the functional structure; and (h) enhanced transparency and credibility.","Office of the Ombudsman"],[1,"192","7","Policy Thrust and 8-Point Agenda Assessment","The Ombudsman is doing an assessment of the Policy Thrust and 8-point Agenda to determine its progress in attaining its development objectives.",""],[1,"193","2","UNCAC Compliance Action Plan","the Ombudsman facilitated the multi-stakeholder compliance assessment and adoption of a 21-point Action Plan",""],[1,"193","2","Witness, Whistleblower, and Freedom of Information Legislation","passage of laws on witness and whistleblower protection and freedom of information, and allowing the Ombudsman to look into bank deposits",""],[1,"193","2","Gift Solicitation and Acceptance Rules","promulgation of rules clarifying solicitation and acceptance of gifts",""],[1,"193","2","UNCAC Monitoring CSO Coalition Framework","The CSO coalition framework on UNCAC monitoring will be established and implemented",""],[1,"193","2","Integrity Pledge and Unified Business Code of Conduct","The integrity pledge and the unified code of conduct for business will be promoted and expanded",""],[1,"193","2","Project SHINE","Project SHINE (Strengthening High level commitment for Integrity initiatives and Nurturing collective action of Enterprise) advocating for fair market conditions will likewise be pursued",""],[1,"198","2","Transparency and Participatory Governance Initiative","The DBM, DOF (including BIR and BOC), COA, CSC, and DILG will be at the forefront of activities aimed at increasing transparency and intensifying participatory governance","DBM | DOF | BIR | BOC | COA | CSC | DILG"],[1,"198","2","Strengthened Performance Management and Anti-Corruption Initiative","the CSC, DAP, OMB and COA will spearhead strengthened performance management and anti-corruption initiatives","CSC | DAP | OMB | COA"]],"52":[[1,"194","12","Justice Sector Good Governance Reform","The DOJ will institute good governance reforms, including performance and integrity management systems, and expedite the recruitment of investigators and prosecutors.","DOJ"],[1,"194","12","Computerization of Justice Processes and Services","Computerization of processes and services will also be pursued and sustained.",""],[1,"194","12","Expansion of Justice Agency Staffing and National Funding","To minimize reliance on LGU resources/support, the Department will work on expanding the staff complement and increasing funding from the national government.","Department"],[1,"194","12","Justice Resource Management Capacity Improvement","It will also seek to and improve its resource management capability/systems towards optimal allocation/utilization at the regional and local levels.",""],[1,"194","12","National Support for Field Justice Agencies","The national government will explore other means of support to field justice agencies to lessen or eliminate dependence on LGUs in improving judicial systems and infrastructure.",""],[1,"195","4","Criminal Investigation Process Streamlining Reform","Streamlining of the criminal investigation process will be pursued through legislation.",""],[1,"195","5","National Justice Information System Implementation","sustained implementation of the National Justice Information System (NJIS) will be pursued in close coordination and collaboration among justice sector agencies",""],[1,"195","5","Justice Sector Coordination and Partnership Roadmap","Existing mechanisms will be maximized, particularly the Justice Sector Coordinating Council (JSCC) and Philippine Development Forum (PDF), in setting the strategic justice sector agenda and partnership roadmap, as well as implementing the NJIS and other critical justice reforms",""],[1,"195","5","Justice Research Center Establishment","Establishment of a Justice Research Center (JRC) will also be explored and pursued based on international best practices in order to formulate, integrate, harmonize or rationalize policies, programs, systems procedures and capacity development in the justice system in a sector-wide approach",""],[1,"198","3","Justice Sector Agenda and Partnership Roadmap Implementation","The JSCC will be utilized as a collaborative mechanism to implement the justice sector agenda and partnership roadmap towards strengthened rule of law.",""]],"53":[[1,"305","6","Improved Judicial Services Delivery Programme","A comprehensive set of programs and projects aimed at enhancing conditions and performance for an improved delivery of judicial services.",""],[1,"310","15","Judiciary Automation Modernization Program","An automated modernization program to improve overall efficiency of the Judiciary in the administration of justice in the Supreme Court and the Appellate courts (e.g. Court of Appeals, Court of Tax Appeals and Sandiganbayan.)",""],[1,"317","11","Judiciary-Wide ICT Systems Development for Case Flow Management","An offshoot project of the Case Flow Management (CFM) System that aims to establish a judiciary-wide ICT systems development for increasing efficiency in the management of dockets of all first and second level courts.",""],[1,"317","13","High Court Mobile Court Outreach Program","A program created by the High Court to reach out to poor Filipinos and expedite litigation of cases they are involved in.",""],[1,"328","5","Judiciary Case Management Reform Project","A management system of the Supreme Court and one of the Judiciary's reform projects aimed at declogging congested dockets and helping solve delays in case management and resolution through the use of information technology.",""]],"55":[[1,"272","4","Community e-Center Expansion Program","The government expanded the Community e-Center (CeC) Program that provided ICT service centers and shared Internet access facilities in remote areas.",""],[1,"278","1","National New Technologies and Digital Connectivity Development Framework","The government will provide the overall development framework on the deployment of new technologies and improvement of the country's digital connectivity through the following plans:",""],[1,"278","2","National Broadband Deployment Plan","National Broadband Deployment Plan, to address current gaps and recommend appropriate initiatives on optimizing broadband service;",""],[1,"279","7","Enabling Policy and Regulatory Framework for Coverage Expansion","Enabling policies/ regulations on increasing coverage to be issued by government (DOST- ICTO, NTC, etc.)","DOST- ICTO | NTC"],[1,"287","1","Community e-Center Expansion Program","the government will aggressively implement the CeC Program and establish 2,586 CeCs by 2016 to provide alternative means of access to information and government services",""],[1,"287","1","TV White Space Broadband Access Initiative","Another strategy is to pursue the TVWS initiative to provide broadband access in rural, remote, unserved and underserved areas",""],[1,"287","6","Connectivity Budget Allocation","Government will allocate budget for connectivity of",""],[1,"312","16","Government-Owned One-Stop ICT Service Facility","A self-sustaining shared facility owned and operated by the government as a one-stop shop for ICT needs of the citizens, providing affordable access to ICT-enabled services and relevant content.",""]],"56":[[1,"204","2","Negotiated Political Settlement and Conflict Mitigation Strategy","The government intends to sustain these gains by continuing the strategy of negotiated political settlement alongside a determined and deliberate complementary track that mitigates the impact of armed hostilities to affected communities.",""],[1,"206","2","Institution Building and Reform for Inclusive Governance","Legitimate institutions need to be built, reformed and strengthened to increase citizens' participation, guard against interests that are inimical to socioeconomic and political empowerment, and guarantee inclusive development.",""],[1,"206","3","Tripartite Implementation Review for Peace Agreement Implementation","The conduct of the Tripartite Implementation Review addressed the issues on the full implementation of the 1996 Final Peace Agreement between the GPH and the MNLF.",""],[1,"206","3","Inclusive Governance Reform Framework for Peace Agreement Delivery","An inclusive framework has been pushed to ensure governance reforms and implementation of the Peace Agreement.",""],[1,"206","6","Closure Agreement Implementation and Community Development Support","A Closure Agreement with the Tabara Paduano Group of the RPM-P/ RPA/ABB is expected to be signed and implemented soon.",""],[1,"213","5","Negotiated Political Settlement of Internal Armed Conflict","Strategies and programs to win the peace will follow two tracks: pursuing negotiated political settlement of internal armed conflict; and effectively addressing the causes and impacts of internal armed conflicts and other issues affecting the peace process.",""],[1,"213","5","Conflict Drivers and Peace Process Support Measures","Strategies and programs to win the peace will follow two tracks: pursuing negotiated political settlement of internal armed conflict; and effectively addressing the causes and impacts of internal armed conflicts and other issues affecting the peace process.",""],[1,"214","23","Amendatory Bill to RA 9054","Amendatory bill to RA 9054 drafted based on the common proposals and common grounds of the GPH and MNLF signed by both parties;",""],[1,"215","3","Closure Memorandum of Agreement Formulation","Formulation of closure MOA with TPG of RPM-P/ RPA/ABB ongoing (2011)",""],[1,"215","6","Closure Memorandum of Agreement Formulation","Formulation of closure MOA with TPG of RPM-P/ RPA/ABB ongoing (2011)",""],[1,"215","9","Reintegration Programs for Peace Tables","Formulation of reintegration programs for the different peace tables ongoing (2011)",""],[1,"215","11","Bangsamoro Basic Law Enactment and Transition Institutions","Completion and implementation of the Comprehensive Peace Agreement with the MILF will lead to the enactment of the Bangsamoro Basic Law that will establish an all-inclusive Bangsamoro Government in 2016.",""],[1,"215","12","Peace Process Completion and Rebel Mainstreaming Measures","Within the Plan period, the government also targets the following: (a) final completion of the Tripartite Implementation Review Process and inclusion of the MNLF legislative agenda into the Bangsamoro Basic Law; (b) the resumption of time-bound and agenda-based talks with the CPP/NPA/NDF; (c) completion of signed final closure agreements with the CBA-CPLA and RPM-P/RPA/ABB; and (d) the final disposition of arms of said groups and mainstreaming of former rebels as productive members of society, in accordance with peace agreements.",""],[1,"216","25","Third-Party Monitoring and Transparency Mechanisms","Third party monitoring; (b) Web posting; (c) Project and community billboards; (d) Performance-based fund releases; and (d) Grievance Redress System",""],[1,"216","25","Public Disclosure and Accountability Measures","Web posting; Project and community billboards; Performance-based fund releases; and Grievance Redress System",""],[1,"222","4","Bangsamoro Basic Law","Bangsamoro Basic Law, establishing the Bangsamoro political entity that will replace the existing ARMM;",""],[1,"224","1","Peace Negotiation Leadership and PAMANA Coordination","The Office of the Presidential Adviser on the Peace Process (OPAPP) is the lead agency in the peace negotiations.","Office of the Presidential Adviser on the Peace Process (OPAPP)"],[1,"275","11","Development Support for Conflict-Affected Areas","11. Enable development in conflict-affected areas",""],[1,"290","1","Infrastructure Support for Conflict-Affected and Impoverished Areas","The government will continue providing infrastructure support to conflict- affected and impoverished areas through the Investment Support Program (ISP) for Autonomous Region for Muslim Mindanao (ARMM) and the Payapa at Masaganang Pamayanan or PAMANA Program",""],[1,"290","2","ARMM Stimulus Development Plan Reform Roadmap","the Stimulus Development Plan (SDP) for ARMM was prepared as a reform roadmap towards economic recovery and development through strategic projects promoting basic services, livelihood and basic infrastructure such as national roads.",""],[1,"318","12","Comprehensive Integrated Peace Framework","An EO that mandates government to continue to pursue a comprehensive, integrated and holistic approach to peace; provides the framework for",""],[1,"318","14","Comprehensive Peace Process Implementation and Coordination Framework","implementation, coordination, for monitoring and integration of all government peace initiatives and guides its partnership with civil society in pursuit of just and enduring peace.",""],[1,"318","14","Administrative Structure for Comprehensive Peace Process","It also identifies the components of the comprehensive peace process; establishes an administrative structure for implementing the comprehensive peace process;",""],[1,"318","14","Government Peace Negotiating Panels","establishes government peace negotiating panels for negotiations with different rebel groups;",""]],"57":[[1,"43","5","Disaster Risk Reduction and Mitigation Strategy for Vulnerable Areas","The strategies to be implemented in the vulnerable areas belonging to Category 3 should focus on disaster-risk reduction and mitigation, social insurance and social protection, and income diversification.",""],[1,"43","7","Disaster Risk Reduction and Livelihood Resilience Measures for Vulnerable Areas","The strategies to be implemented in the vulnerable areas belonging to Category 3 should focus on disaster-risk reduction and mitigation, social insurance and social protection, and income diversification.",""],[1,"45","3","Social Protection Programs for Catastrophic Situations","social protection from catastrophic situations will be designed to prevent the poor from falling deeper into poverty and the near-poor from joining the ranks of the poor.",""],[1,"45","5","Community-Based Employment Program Social Protection Redesign","The CBEP will also be re-designed to function as a social protection mechanism that replaces lost income in times of crises or disasters.",""],[1,"49","7","Mainstream Climate Adaptation and Disaster Risk Reduction into Local Development Plans","more climate change adaptation and disaster risk reduction activities being mainstreamed into local development plans.",""],[1,"49","7","Increase Investment in Climate Adaptation, Mitigation, and Disaster Risk Reduction","this Updated Plan aims for an annual increase in the level of investments for climate change adaptation and mitigation (CCA/M) and disaster risk reduction and management (DRRM).",""],[1,"49","7","Promote Climate and Disaster-Resilient Infrastructure Financing","It will entail promotion of climate/disaster resilient infrastructure for which innovative financing will have to be designed.",""],[1,"49","7","Develop and Adopt Vulnerability Assessment Tools","The government is also set to invest in developing and adopting more effective vulnerability assessment tools to identify highly susceptible communities and prevent and mitigate potential disaster impacts.",""]],"58":[[1,"196","1","Expansion of Philippine Mediation Center Units","new Philippine Mediation Center (PMC) units will be opened in Bohol, Legazpi City, Sorsogon, Dipolog City, Ilocos Norte, Ilocos Sur and Negros Oriental in 2013 and 2014.",""],[1,"196","2","Alternative Dispute Resolution Promotion and Expansion","The DOJ, through the Office for Alternative Dispute Resolution (OADR), will continue efforts to (a) promote and maximize the use of ADR by accrediting more practitioners in mediation and arbitration nationwide; (b) putting up ADR facilities in strategic cities/regions; and (c) strengthening research, policy/program development, information campaign and capacity building.","DOJ | Office for Alternative Dispute Resolution (OADR)"],[1,"196","2","Barangay Justice System and Mediation Strengthening","Within the next few years, strengthening of the Barangay Justice System, prosecution-level mediation and contractual dispute resolution will be pursued.",""],[1,"196","3","Lupong Tagapamayapa Incentives and Awards","the DILG will continue to institutionalize the granting of economic benefits and other incentives through the Lupong Tagapamayapa Incentives and Awards.","DILG"],[1,"196","3","Lupong Tagapamayapa Capacity Development Interventions","The Lupons will be provided with the needed capacity- development interventions to strengthen the efficacy of the Lupong Tagapamayapa as an ADR mechanism or indigenous mediation structure in resolving disputes within a community, and beyond the court system.",""]],"59":[[1,"179","12","Legal Aid and Access to Justice Expansion","This involves, among others, (a) enhancing access by the poor to law enforcement and legal assistance;",""],[1,"195","3","Justice on Wheels Mobile Court Services","The Justice on Wheels buses will continue to visit various courts and jails.",""],[1,"195","3","Free Legal Services for Indigent Litigants and Detainees","Access to legal information through free legal services has also been provided to indigent litigants and detainees.",""],[1,"196","4","Implementation of the Recognizance Act and Bail Bond Reform","the Recognizance Act of 2012 (RA 10389) will be implemented together with reforms in the bail bond system to benefit the poor and vulnerable sectors",""],[1,"196","4","Expansion of Public Attorney Positions","More public attorney positions nationwide will be created to ensure adequate free legal assistance and representation, especially for indigents",""],[1,"196","4","Review and Improvement of Justice Sector Procedures and Facilities","Relevant procedures and necessary facilities will be reviewed/improved to better serve these vulnerable sectors, particularly women, children, persons with disabilities, senior citizens and indigenous peoples",""],[1,"196","4","Jail Decongestion and Corrections Reform","Jails will be decongested and reforms in corrections will be sustained/pursued for persons deprived of liberty (detainees/prisoners) and their families",""],[1,"211","5","Expanded Anti-Trafficking in Persons Act","RA 10364 expands the Anti-Trafficking in Persons Act and gives special attention to women and children through additional protection and support.",""],[1,"216","12","Mechanisms to Address Grave Human Rights Violations","Mechanisms to address grave human rights violations established and implemented",""]],"60":[[1,"331","20","Criminal Justice Information Sharing Program","A program that is intended to address and remedy the current information gaps in the Philippine criminal justice system by enabling effective sharing of data between the police, judiciary, probation services, custodial authorities, and criminal information registries, at key decision points in our criminal justice system process.",""],[1,"344","13","Judiciary Administrative Integrity Assessment and Reform Programme","A program of the Judiciary that aims to: (a) provide the Judiciary with effective tools and techniques to systematically assess the level of integrity of its administrative processes; (b) guide the Judiciary as it conducts a comprehensive review of its administrative processes that will provide the basis for the design of reform measures; and (c) assist the Judiciary in effectively implementing the selected reforms.",""]],"61":[[1,"116","7","Agricultural Research, Development and Extension Investment Increase","Increase investments in research, development and extension (RD&E) to generate appropriate technologies and innovations to improve farm productivity.",""],[1,"116","16","Investment in Agricultural Research, Development and Extension","Increase investments in RD&E on agri-processing, product development of A&F products, agri-tourism, and agro-forestry;",""],[1,"116","24","National and Local Agricultural and Food Commodity Roadmaps","Pursue the formulation of national and local A&F commodity roadmaps",""],[1,"117","2","National RD&E Database and Information System Upgrade","Update databases and information systems for the formulation of a reliable and responsive national RD&E agenda;",""],[1,"120","2","Increased Investment in Agricultural Research, Development, and Extension","Strategy 9: Increase investments in RD&E on agri-processing, product development of A&F products, agri-tourism, and agro-forestry",""]],"62":[[1,"116","17","Asset Reform Through Land Title Distribution","Fast-track the completion of asset reform through the distribution of land titles",""],[1,"118","4","Land Acquisition and Distribution Process Streamlining","DAR has instituted several policy and operational measures to speed up completion of land distribution by 2016 and ensure post-LAD tenurial stability.","DAR"],[1,"118","4","LAD Balance Assessment and Monitoring Strengthening","These include: (a) streamlining of LAD processes; (b) accurate assessment of actual magnitude and status of LAD balance and corresponding issues; and (c) intensification of the monitoring of performance of provincial/municipal agrarian reform offices.","DAR"],[1,"123","3","Agrarian Reform Acceleration","Hence, fast-tracking agrarian reform and social protection programs will be prioritized.",""],[1,"123","3","CARPER Completion Support","The completion of CARPER will be facilitated along with social protection interventions (i.e., cash-for-work program, Self-employment Assistance for Kaunlaran or SEA-K, universal PhilHealth and scholarship program) to augment subsistence farm incomes.",""],[1,"123","5","Integrated Land Acquisition and Distribution Roadmap Pilot Rollout","For the first year of implementation, the integrated roadmap will focus on 12 pilot provinces, including Camarines Sur, Masbate, Eastern Samar, Samar, Northern Samar, Zamboanga del Norte, Davao Oriental, North Cotabato, Sarangani, Agusan del Sur, Surigao del Norte and Surigao del Sur.",""],[1,"123","5","Accelerated Land Acquisition and Distribution Expansion","The program will likewise help fast-track LAD to cover additional provinces with highest LAD balance, including Agusan del Norte, Albay, Camarines Norte, Compostela Valley, Davao del Sur, Lanao del Norte, Leyte, Misamis Occidental, Quezon, Sibugay, Sorsogon and Zamboanga del Sur.",""],[1,"124","6","Completion of the LAD Component","It should include the completion of the LAD component and continued delivery of support services to ARBs.",""],[1,"126","1","Land Tenure Security Improvement","DAR and DENR are mainly responsible for improving land tenure security.","DAR | DENR"],[1,"305","10","Land Redistribution and Agrarian Reform Support","The redistribution of lands, regardless of crops or fruits produced, to farmers and regular farm workers who are landless, irrespective of tenurial arrangement, to include the totality of factors and support services designed to lift the economic status of the beneficiaries and all other arrangements alternative to the physical redistribution of lands, such as production or profit-sharing, labor administration, and the distribution of shares of stock, which will allow beneficiaries to receive a just share of the fruits of the lands they work.",""]],"63":[[1,"112","6","Rationalization of Government Functions and Policies","There is a need to rationalize government functions and policies to establish a strategic approach in addressing the needs of stakeholders and in creating an enabling environment for their participation.",""],[1,"112","6","Unified Support Services for Farmers and Fisherfolk","At present, there is an apparent overlap of functions of DA and DAR, particularly in the provision of support services to farmers and fisherfolk, which requires a systematic and more unified approach to enhance its efficiency.","DA | DAR"],[1,"112","6","Coordinated Fisheries Management in Marine-Protected Areas","Such is also the case between the DA and DENR in terms of fisheries management in marine-protected areas, as well as among DAR, DENR, Land Registration Authority (LRA) and National Commission on Indigenous Peoples (NCIP) in terms of land titling and distribution.","DA | DENR | DAR | Land Registration Authority (LRA) | National Commission on Indigenous Peoples (NCIP)"],[1,"112","6","Coordinated Land Titling and Distribution","Such is also the case between the DA and DENR in terms of fisheries management in marine-protected areas, as well as among DAR, DENR, Land Registration Authority (LRA) and National Commission on Indigenous Peoples (NCIP) in terms of land titling and distribution.","DAR | DENR | Land Registration Authority (LRA) | National Commission on Indigenous Peoples (NCIP)"],[1,"122","1","Agriculture Bureaucracy Rationalization and AARNR Agency Convergence","The agriculture bureaucracy, including the DA, DAR, and DENR, will be rationalized through the efficient and effective convergence and complementation of the agriculture, agrarian reform and natural resources (AARNR) service agencies and related offices.","DA | DAR | DENR"],[1,"122","3","Local Agricultural Development Planning","Formulation of provincial and municipal agricultural development plans will support and strengthen the implementation of national agricultural commodity and subsector roadmaps at the local level.",""],[1,"122","4","Agriculture and Fisheries Roadmap Formulation","The formulation of A&F roadmaps will guide the overall development of the sector.",""],[1,"122","5","Agriculture Bureaucracy Rationalization and Agency Convergence","The agriculture bureaucracy, including the Department of Agiculture, Department of Agrarian Reform, and Department of Environment and Natural Resources, will be rationalized through the efficient and effective convergence and complementation of the agriculture, agrarian reform and natural resources service agencies and related offices.","Department of Agiculture | Department of Agrarian Reform | Department of Environment and Natural Resources"],[1,"125","5","Agriculture and Fisheries Sector Plan and Policy Implementation","the DA, DAR and DENR will continue to spearhead the formulation and implementation of relevant plans, programs and policies.","DA | DAR | DENR"]],"64":[[1,"115","16","Climate Change Adaptation Mainstreaming Program","Climate change adaptation programs are mainstreamed and implemented in all government programs.",""],[1,"118","2","Climate-Resilient Infrastructure Design Enhancement","Enhance the technical design of irrigation, drainage systems and facilities, FMRs, bridges and other infrastructure to take into account climate risks and extreme climate events;",""],[1,"121","3","Crop-Weather and Crop Diversification Training","Conduct training in crop-weather relationships and crop diversification to mitigate risks on off-seasons;",""],[1,"121","8","Investment in Sustainable and Climate-Responsive Agricultural Technologies","Increase investments in sustainable and climate change-responsive technologies and innovations in the production and processing of A&F products;",""],[1,"121","10","Climate-Responsive Agricultural and Food Technology Adoption","Promote the adoption of climate-responsive technologies and innovations in the production, processing and distribution of A&F products;",""],[1,"121","13","Vulnerability and Adaptation Assessment Programme for Agriculture and Fisheries","Continuously conduct vulnerability and adaptation assessments, especially in critical A&F products.",""]],"65":[[1,"46","8","IT-BPM Sector Development Framework","government will provide the overall development framework on the deployment of new technologies and improvement of the country's digital connectivity.",""],[1,"87","3","IT-BPM Services and Next-Wave Cities Development","The government will also nurture the Filipino talent pool by promoting and accelerating the development of high-value IT-BPM services and the Next-Wave Cities.",""],[1,"87","4","Philippines IT-BPM Destination Promotion Campaign","Both the public and the private sectors will promote the Philippines as a preferred IT-BPM destination.",""],[1,"87","5","IT-BPM Investment Promotion Campaign","Both the public and the private sectors will promote the Philippines as a preferred information technology and business process management (IT-BPM) destination.",""],[1,"92","1","IT-BPM Sector Development Strategy","The government will adopt strategies aimed at making the country a global leader in IT-BPM services.",""],[1,"277","9","ICT Promotion for IT-BPM Industry Development","The government will continue to promote the spread of ICT to develop the information technology-business process management (IT-BPM) industry, as guided by the 2012-2016 IT-BPM Road Map",""]],"66":[[1,"338","11","National Responsible Parenthood and Reproductive Health Policy","An act providing for a national policy on responsible parenthood and reproductive health.",""]],"67":[[1,"158","5","TVET Institutional Strengthening and Good Governance System","There is also a need to strengthen TVET institutions in terms of leadership, management and innovation.",""],[1,"158","5","Digital Access Improvement for TVET Institutions","Strategies include implementing a good governance system that encourages TVET institutions to meet quality standards and to use information technology to ease access to TVET.",""],[1,"158","6","TESDA Institutional Strengthening and Quality Assurance Reform","Strengthen the Technical Education and Skills Development Authority (TESDA) and focus on development planning, resource allocation, standard- setting and quality assurance","Technical Education and Skills Development Authority (TESDA)"],[1,"158","7","Rationalization Plan Approval and Implementation","push for the approval and implementation of the Rationalization Plan, which takes into consideration the changing environment and demands of operations, particularly at the frontlines",""],[1,"158","7","TESDA Organizational Capacity and Capability Strengthening","build up the organizational capacity and capability of TESDA continuously in line with its mandate",""],[1,"158","7","TESDA Resource Allocation and Interagency Coordination Framework","implement the resource allocation mandate of TESDA under the framework of interagency coordination",""],[1,"160","3","Philippines Qualifications Framework Institutionalization","This will be done through the Philippines Qualification Framework (PQF), which was institutionalized through Executive Order 83 in 2012.",""]],"68":[[1,"332","4","Disaster Prevention and Mitigation Program","A responsive program of the government for disaster prevention and mitigation.",""],[1,"338","3","National Disaster Risk Reduction and Management System Strengthening","An act that seeks to strengthen the Philippine disaster risk reduction and management system through the adoption of the National Disaster Risk",""],[1,"338","5","National Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Framework and Plan","It further aims to recognize and strengthen the capacity of the national government and the local government units (LGUs), together with partner stakeholders, to build the disaster resilience of communities, and to institutionalize arrangements and measures for reducing disaster risks, including projected climate risks, and enhancing disaster preparedness and response capabilities at all levels.",""]],"70":[[1,"147","19","Convergence Mechanism Establishment","Set up convergence mechanism at all levels",""],[1,"168","1","Guaranty Line Due Diligence and Post-Audit","Due diligence and post-audit of approved guaranty lines were conducted to ensure that guaranteed housing loans are used for home purchase or construction.",""],[1,"171","1","Balanced Housing Development Compliance Mechanism","The resolution requires developers of proposed residential subdivision projects to develop an area for socialized housing through balanced housing development, slum upgrading, joint venture with LGUs, participation in the Community Mortgage Program, and development of new settlements.",""],[1,"171","2","Technical Assistance for Comprehensive Land Use Plan Formulation and Updating","the HLURB will continue to extend technical assistance in the formulation/updating of comprehensive land use plans (CLUPs) to 652 LGUs composed of 101 cities and 551 municipalities",""],[1,"171","3","Homeowner Association Orientation and Housing Regulation Review","The HLURB will continue its orientation of homeowner associations under the Magna Carta for Homeowners' Associations (RA 9904) and review of its IRR.",""],[1,"171","3","Housing Standards and IRR Revision for Green Technology","The agency will also review existing IRRs on the Subdivision and Condominium Buyers' Protective Decree (PD 957) and the act authorizing HLURB to establish standards and technical requirements for economic and socialized housing projects (BP 220), to include green technology and other revisions on national standards for housing projects.",""],[1,"171","3","ISO Certification of HLURB Core Processes","Another important project is the International Organization for Standardization (ISO) certification of the core processes, which include planning assistance, registration and adjudication nationwide to improve delivery of service.",""],[1,"171","4","Amendment of the Urban Development and Housing Act for Vertical Development","The amendment of Section 18 of the Urban Development and Housing Act will be pursued to qualify vertical development as eligible in compliance with the balanced housing development requirement.",""],[1,"171","4","Technical Assistance for Scaling Up the Community Mortgage Program","The policy change works in tandem with the ongoing technical assistance to the Social Housing Finance Corporation on the scaling up of the Community Mortgage Program through Medium-Rise Buildings and the citywide approach to urban planning and development.",""],[1,"171","5","Integrated Sustainable Urban Development Planning","The pursuit of sustainable urban development will entail the adherence to a systematic approach to planning from the preparation of the CLUPs and local shelter plans as well as the creation and operation of local housing boards in the LGUs that will be guided at the national level by the DHUD.","Department of Housing and Urban Development (DHUD)"],[1,"172","1","Plan Implementation Monitoring Mechanism","The progress of Plan implementation, using the RMs (Tables 6.1, 6.2 and 6.5) and the annual target indicator matrix in Table 6.12 below, will be monitored through the Social Development Committee (SDC), an interagency committee under the National Economic and Development Authority (NEDA) Board, as well as through the Human Development and Poverty Reduction Cabinet Cluster (HDPRC).",""]],"71":[[1,"52","4","Revenue Mobilization and Tax Administration Strengthening","The government aims to increase the revenue effort to 17.1 percent of GDP by 2016.",""],[1,"59","7","Run After the Smugglers (RATS) and RATE Tax Enforcement Programs","In addition to the current programs being implemented (e.g., Run After the Smugglers or RATS, and RATE), reducing the leakage from individual income tax collection, particularly among the self-employed, will provide additional boost to the government's collection effort.",""],[1,"67","1","Revenue Collection Enhancement and Anti-Smuggling Strategy","Revenue-enhancing measures will focus on heightened collection efforts of the BIR in tandem with anti-smuggling strategies of the BOC in coordination with relevant government agencies.",""],[1,"67","1","Enhanced Tax Collection and Revenue Intelligence Measures","In the case of the BIR, enhanced tax collection will be supported by increased collection efficiency from the self-employed business and professionals, better assessment of estate taxes, and strengthened Fiscal Unit/ Revenue Intelligence Unit.",""],[1,"67","1","Comprehensive Anti-Smuggling Enforcement Package","the BOC's comprehensive anti- smuggling strategies will include port accreditation, import mapping, fuel marking alongside the conduct of audit on oil companies, trade statistics reconciliation, and the requirement to submit a rolling import plan from all importers of sensitive commodities.",""],[1,"90","2","Anti-Smuggling Measures","The government will curb and prevent smuggling by putting in place specific measures identified under Chapters 2 (Macroeconomic policy) and 7 (Good governance and the rule of law).",""]],"72":[[1,"61","2","Stable Monetary Policy","The Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas (BSP) remains committed to a stable monetary policy that is conducive to achieving sustainable economic growth.","Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas (BSP)"],[1,"70","3","Exchange Rate and Reserve Stabilization Policy","A market-determined exchange rate and a comfortable level of international reserves will be maintained to better insulate the economy from external shocks.",""],[1,"70","4","Monetary Policy Monitoring and Adjustment","monetary authorities will continue to monitor emerging price and output conditions to ensure that monetary policy remains supportive of sustained non-inflationary economic growth.",""],[1,"70","5","External Shock Buffering and Debt Sustainability Management","policymakers will ensure that the economy is cushioned from the adverse financial impact of external shocks.",""],[1,"71","2","Expansion of the Monetary Policy Toolkit","the monetary authorities will continue to pursue the expansion of its monetary policy toolkit and to adopt best practices used by other central banks.",""],[1,"71","2","Amendment of the BSP Charter","the BSP's policy agenda will continue to be geared towards the amendment of the BSP Charter.",""],[1,"71","5","Restoration of Authority to Issue Negotiable Certificates of Indebtedness","Restoration of authority to issue negotiable certificates of indebtedness even during normal times;",""],[1,"71","11","BSP Charter Amendment","The proposal to amend the BSP charter was also included in the priority legislative measures supported by the Economic Development Cluster (Econ Cluster).",""],[1,"71","12","Monetary Policy Toolkit Expansion","Monetary authorities will continue to pursue the expansion of its monetary policy toolkit and to adopt best practices used by other central banks.",""]],"73":[[1,"179","12","Competition Regulation Against Monopolistic Practices","ensuring equal opportunity for businesses through effective regulation against monopolistic practices;",""],[1,"196","6","Competition Strengthening and Tax Enforcement Reform","To achieve economic justice, the government will work to strengthen competition, improve efficiency in commercial dispute resolution, and intensify tax enforcement.",""],[1,"197","5","Unified Competition and Anti-Trust Law Enforcement","The DOJ, through its Office for Competition, will pursue the enactment of a unified competition/anti-trust law and intensify enforcement efforts.","DOJ | Office for Competition"],[1,"197","5","Competition Policy Partnership and Capacity-Building Mechanism","It will expand partnerships with and among sector regulators and other stakeholders in policy development, regulatory impact assessment, information sharing, capacity building, investigation/case build-up, and eventual filing cases and prosecution in court against monopolistic practices.","DOJ | Office for Competition"]],"75":[[1,"211","6","Armed Forces Modernization Extension","The Revised AFP Modernization Act (RA 10349) extends the military modernization program to another 15 years to boost the AFP's defense capability program and move closer to achieving a minimum credible defense posture against external threats.",""],[1,"211","6","National Coast Watch System Expansion","the creation of the National Coast Watch System through EO 57 in 2011 expanded the scope of the Coast Watch South from Southern Philippines to the entire Philippine archipelago.",""],[1,"211","6","Maritime Surveillance and Patrol Enhancement","This, along with the acquisition of modern equipment, strengthened patrol coverage and naval presence in the West Philippine Sea, thus improving monitoring and apprehension of foreign vessels poaching within the country's exclusive economic zone.",""],[1,"220","1","National Security Strategy and Programmes","Strategies and programs to ensure national security are expected to contribute to four intermediate outcomes: (a) internal stability sustained; (b) capability to uphold sovereignty and territorial integrity of the stated assured; (c) highest standard of capability and preparedness against disasters and emergencies achieved; and (d) security sector reforms implemented.",""],[1,"220","13","International Support and Maritime Rights Diplomacy","The Philippines will continue to secure international support and cultivate international relations in pursuing legitimate rights over the West Philippine Sea.",""],[1,"220","13","Formal Establishment of Archipelagic Sea Lanes and Maritime Zones","The government will also work towards formally establishing the Philippines' archipelagic sea lanes and maritime zones.",""],[1,"221","1","Strengthened Security and Defense Cooperation with External Partners","Strengthened cooperation with external bilateral and multilateral partners will help the country address security and defense issues through capacity building and operations support in matters related to transnational crime, human assistance, disaster relief, and the protection and preservation of natural resources.",""],[1,"221","2","Defense and Security Establishment Modernization","Modernizing defense and security establishments will enable concerned agencies to perform the full spectrum of their roles in accordance with the comprehensive and updated definition of national security.",""],[1,"221","4","Modern Equipment Acquisition for Territorial Defense","Acquiring modern equipment to support territorial defense activities;",""],[1,"221","5","Enhanced Surveillance and Monitoring in Disputed Areas","Establishing the presence of effective and competent forces in disputed areas through greater surveillance and monitoring capability;",""],[1,"221","6","Maritime and Coastal Security Capability Upgrade","Ensuring that maritime assets, territorial integrity, and coastal areas are protected in accordance with the Archipelagic Baselines Law (RA 9522) by upgrading air and maritime capability and expanding coverage of coast watch stations;",""],[1,"221","7","Maritime Incident Response Service","Providing expedient and efficient response to maritime incidents.",""],[1,"221","8","Border Security Surveillance and Detection Upgrade","This entails enhancement of border security through upgrading of surveillance, detection capacity and information systems to thwart the entry of foreign terrorists, human traffickers and smugglers of antisocial goods and weapons of mass destruction.",""],[1,"221","8","Alien Registration Database Program","The country will build up and update its database of aliens through an Alien Registration Program, as well as strengthen coordination with the International Criminal Police Organization and other intelligence/law enforcement agencies.",""],[1,"221","8","Border Control Legal and Customs Modernization Reform","The enactment of the new Philippine Immigration Law and Customs Modernization Act will further improve border control and management in the face of transnational crimes, migration trends, continued increase of overseas workers, and tourism development.",""],[1,"339","8","AFP Modernization Programme","A comprehensive modernization of the AFP primarily for defense capability with support mechanisms for national development.",""]],"76":[[1,"47","2","Infrastructure Sector Strategies for Livable and Safe Environment","Infrastructure sector strategies will be implemented to ensure a livable and safe environment.",""],[1,"47","2","Master Plan for Flood Management in Metro Manila and Surrounding Areas","The Master Plan for Flood Management in Metro Manila and Surrounding Areas will be implemented to protect lives, property and livelihood",""],[1,"48","1","Flood Management Structures Construction","Flood management structures in highly vulnerable areas based on river basin master plans will be constructed.",""],[1,"48","2","Flood Forecasting and Warning System Coordination Strengthening","The government will strengthen the coordination among the National Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council (NDRRMC), Advanced Science and Technology Institute (ASTI), Philippine Atmospheric, Geophysical and Astronomical Services Administration (PAGASA), Department of Public Works and Highways (DPWH), Metro Manila Development Authority and LGUs to improve existing flood forecasting and warning systems, particularly in provinces vulnerable to flooding.","National Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council (NDRRMC) | Advanced Science and Technology Institute (ASTI) | Philippine Atmospheric, Geophysical and Astronomical Services Administration (PAGASA) | Department of Public Works and Highways (DPWH) | Metro Manila Development Authority | LGUs"],[1,"243","9","Climate and Disaster-Resilient Infrastructure Facilities","Promote climate/ disaster resilient infrastructure facilities",""],[1,"244","9","Engineering Standards and Design Update for Climate-Resilient Infrastructure","existing engineering standards and designs will be reviewed and updated to integrate emerging technologies and retrofitting techniques.",""],[1,"244","9","Disaster and Climate Infrastructure Program Continuation","Disaster and climate infrastructure programs and projects will be continuously pursued, even beyond the Updated Plan period.",""],[1,"274","3","Metro Manila Flood Risk Management Master Plan","In September 2012, the NEDA Board approved the implementation of a master plan for effective flood risk management (FRM) in Metro Manila and surrounding areas, with an initial allocation of PhP5 billion for immediate, high-impact flood management interventions.",""],[1,"274","3","Flood Risk Management Project for Principal Rivers","It also approved the FRM Project along selected principal rivers.",""],[1,"290","5","Immediate High-Impact Flood Management Projects","Implementation of immediate high-impact projects identified under the Master Plan for Flood Management in Metro Manila and Surrounding Areas",""],[1,"290","6","Flood Risk Management Project along Principal Rivers","Flood Risk Management Project (FRIMP) along principal rivers (Cagayan River, Tagoloan River, Imus River and Cagayan de Oro River)",""],[1,"291","1","Master Plan for Flood Management Implementation","The government will implement the Master Plan for Flood Management in Metro Manila and Surrounding Areas.",""],[1,"291","1","Flood Management Structure Construction Prioritization","Related to this is the prioritization of construction of flood management structures in highly vulnerable areas based on river basin master plans, and expediting immediate financing for the rehabilitation of flood management structures.",""],[1,"291","3","Disaster Recovery Infrastructure Reconstruction Program","the government will fast-track the mobilization of funds and provision of infrastructure program for rebuilding and reconstructing priority infrastructure",""],[1,"291","3","LGU Capacity Building for Disaster-Resilient Local Service Delivery","it will undertake capacity building for LGUs to improve basic service delivery and exercise of regulatory powers, specifically in ensuring integrity and sustainability of local structures from disasters",""],[1,"291","4","Coordinated Disaster Recovery and Rehabilitation Strategy","a coordinated response strategy for the immediate rehabilitation/provision of necessary infrastructure for disaster relief and recovery (e.g., water supply and sanitation, electricity, roads, etc.) will be established",""]],"77":[[1,"281","1","Interruptible Load Program Support","Pending new capacity addition, rehabilitation and uprating of existing power plants in Mindanao, the DOE supports the DUs' implementation of Interruptible Load Program (ILP) as a short-term solution to the region's power situation.","DOE"],[1,"281","2","Modular Genset Program","Modular Genset Program, wherein electric cooperatives may purchase or rent modular generator sets to fill the gap between demand and contracted supply, particularly during peak hours;",""],[1,"281","3","Interim Mindanao Electricity Market","Interim Mindanao Electricity Market, which encourages the use of available uncontracted and unutilized capacities in the Mindanao grid for real-time correction of electricity supply-demand imbalance.",""],[1,"282","5","AHEPP Auxiliary Turbines 4 and 5 Rehabilitation, Operation and Maintenance through PPP","Rehabilitation, Operation and Maintenance of the Angat Hydro Electric Power Plant (AHEPP) Auxiliary Turbines 4 & 5 through PPP",""],[1,"327","10","Interim Wholesale Electricity Market for Mindanao","An interim wholesale market for the trading of electricity in the Mindanao System intended to facilitate the transparent and efficient utilization of all available capacities in Mindanao in order to minimize the perennial power shortages in the region.",""],[1,"333","2","Retail Wheeling Access Framework","The system of allowing any qualified person the use of transmission, and/or distribution system, and associated facilities subject to the payment of transmission and/or distribution retail wheeling rates duly approved by the Energy Regulatory Commission (ERC).",""],[1,"339","17","Electric Power Industry Restructuring and Privatization Framework","An act that provides a framework for the restructuring of the electric power industry, including the privatization of the assets of National Power Industry",""],[1,"346","6","Transmission System Management Program","The program for managing the transmission system through efficient planning for the expansion, upgrading, rehabilitation, repair and maintenance, to be formulated by the Department of Energy (DOE) and implemented by the National Transmission Corporation (TransCo)/National Grid Corporation of the Philippines (NGCP) pursuant to Republic Act No. 9136.","Department of Energy (DOE)"],[1,"348","18","Electricity Market Trading Reform","The market where competitive, efficient, transparent and reliable market/ trading of electricity will be made.",""]],"78":[[1,"46","9","Energy Generation Capacity Expansion","Energy security will also be pursued by increasing energy generating capacity, encouraging efficient use of energy and implementing various transmission projects.",""],[1,"272","2","Household Electrification Development Plan","The 2013-2017 Household Electrification Development Plan (HEDP) issued by the Department of Energy (DOE) sets the plans and strategies to attain 86.2-percent household electrification by 2016 and 90-percent by 2017.","Department of Energy (DOE)"],[1,"272","2","Sitio Electrification Target under the Philippine Energy Plan","For the sitios, the Philippine Energy Plan 2012-2030 targets a100-percent electrification by 2015.",""],[1,"272","2","Missionary Electrification Development Plan","Its 2012-2016 Missionary Electrification Development Plan includes strategies for private sector participation in SPUG and distribution utility (DU)-covered unviable areas, improved technical efficiency of SPUG and DUs in small-island and isolated grids, and rationalized Universal Charge for missionary electrification subsidy, among others.",""],[1,"280","7","Transmission Development Plan Projects","To help ensure the reliability of power supply, the National Grid Corporation of the Philippines will implement various transmission projects under its Transmission Development Plan 2012.",""],[1,"285","5","Sitio and Household Electrification Expansion","Along with this is the expansion of energy access to remaining sitios and households without electricity in the country to achieve 100-percent sitio electrification by 2015, 86.2-percent household electrification by 2016 and 90-percent household electrification by 2017.",""],[1,"285","5","Off-grid Power Capacity Expansion","This will entail installation of 65.225-mW additional power capacity in off-grid areas, as well as accelerating the implementation of retail competition and open access up to the household level and providing support to DUs.",""]],"79":[[1,"281","4","Bright Now Campaign for Smart Energy Use","The Bright Now Campaign under the National Energy Efficiency and Conservation Program (NEECP) will promote smart energy use through the dissemination of basic information on energy standards, energy efficient products and innovative technologies.",""],[1,"281","4","Expansion of Energy Labeling Program","As part of the NEECP, the DOE will also expand its existing energy labeling program to include television sets, washing machines and new models of passenger cars and light duty vehicles, apart from the current coverage of air conditioners, refrigerators and compact fluorescent lamps or CFL.","DOE"]],"80":[[1,"271","3","Classroom Construction Budget Expansion","the government significantly increased the budget for classroom construction from only PhP6.14 billion in 2010 to PhP17.9 billion in 2013",""],[1,"271","3","Public-Private Partnership School Infrastructure Project","Through the Public-Private Partnership (PPP) for School Infrastructure Project (PSIP), around 19,980 classrooms will be completed by 2013 or early 2014 in regions with acute classroom shortage",""],[1,"285","4","Classroom Construction and Completion Programme","The government will fast-track the completion of classrooms under the first and second phases of the PSIP.","Department of Education"],[1,"285","4","Basic Education School Building Expansion","It will also construct additional batches of classrooms for PSIP and for the Basic Education Facilities Program, Regular School Building Program and School Building Program for Basic Education through increased private sector and public spending.",""]],"81":[[1,"12","21","Wastewater and Solid Waste Management Improvement","Revalidated RM on improving wastewater and solid waste management",""],[1,"239","2","Sagip-Ilog River Clean-up, Rehabilitation, and Maintenance Program","Water quality management of 19 rivers has been prioritized for clean-up, rehabilitation and maintenance under the Sagip-Ilog Program.",""],[1,"239","2","Industrial Establishment Monitoring for River Water Quality","Still, the quality of priority rivers has partially improved due to a number of notable interventions, such as close monitoring of industrial establishments",""],[1,"239","2","Adopt-an-Estero Program","Still, the quality of priority rivers has partially improved due to a number of notable interventions, such as close monitoring of industrial establishments and the implementation of the Adopt-an-Estero Program.",""],[1,"253","13","Local Water Pollution Reduction Ordinances and Budget Support","LGUs prioritize strategies that will help reduce water pollution through provision of local ordinances and budget support to programs contributing to the achievement of this outcome.",""],[1,"254","2","Local Water Pollution Reduction Ordinances and Budget Support","LGUs prioritize strategies that will help reduce water pollution through provision of local ordinances and budget support to programs contributing to the achievement of this outcome.",""],[1,"274","5","Expansion of Sewerage Coverage in Metro Manila","In Metro Manila, 4.07 million households are not yet covered by sewerage systems.",""],[1,"275","16","Wastewater and Solid Waste Management Improvement","13. Improve wastewater and solid waste management",""],[1,"291","4","Mainstreaming of Water Supply and Sanitation in Disaster Response Areas","mainstreaming of WSS in emergency/disaster response areas will be promoted",""],[1,"291","5","Wastewater Management Investment","The government will prioritize treatment and proper discharge of wastewater by investing in adequate wastewater management to minimize the impact on the environment, fisheries, livelihood and the food chain.",""],[1,"291","5","National Sewerage and Septage Management Program Implementation","The full implementation of the operational plan of the National Sewerage and Septage Management Program (NSSMP), which started in December 2012, will be undertaken to improve water quality and public health in highly urbanized cities (HUCs), as also required by the Clean Water Act of 2004.",""]],"82":[[1,"53","1","Diaspora Remittance Investment Instrument","What is needed is a financial instrument that matches the risk-return profile of overseas Filipinos and overseas Filipino workers so that this resource can be channeled to investments that would lead to job creation in the country.",""],[1,"95","4","Financial Literacy Campaigns for Overseas Filipinos","The Commission on Filipinos Overseas, DTI, and the Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas will continue to conduct financial literacy campaigns among OFs and their families to educate them on business opportunities, investment and remittance options.","Commission on Filipinos Overseas | DTI | Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas"]],"83":[[1,"28","7","Household Family Size Management Mechanism","The passage of two important pieces of long-pending legislation- one restructuring taxes on tobacco and alcohol, and the other providing mechanisms for households to manage family size-attest to the political capital of the current",""],[1,"45","7","Housing Assistance for Vulnerable Households","For the remaining Plan period, the target is to deliver 510,683 units of housing assistance focusing on vulnerable households.",""],[1,"45","8","Catastrophic Social Protection Design","Social protection from catastrophic situations will be designed to prevent the poor from falling deeper into poverty and the near- poor from joining the ranks of the poor.",""],[1,"46","1","Needs- and Affordability-Based Housing Assistance Scheme","assistance based on the needs and affordability of intended housing beneficiaries will also be developed.",""],[1,"46","10","Affordable Housing Provision for Households","provide housing units to over 500,000 households",""],[1,"147","14","Housing Options and Assistance Menu","8. Provide a menu of housing options/ assistance",""],[1,"147","18","Socialized Housing Policy Agenda","Pursue the policy agenda for socialized housing",""],[1,"167","2","Secure Shelter and Adequate Housing Expansion","Providing secure shelter will thus form part of the strategy for inclusive development and poverty reduction aimed at reducing vulnerabilities and enhancing opportunities.",""],[1,"168","1","Housing Loan Guarantee Scheme","To encourage greater private sector participation in housing construction and finance, housing loans are protected from credit default risk through the Home Guaranty Corporation (HGC) guaranty.",""],[1,"168","1","Mortgage Purchase Operations","The National Home Mortgage Finance Corporation (NHMFC) also continued to purchase mortgages using proceeds from the issuance of Bahay Bonds.",""],[1,"168","9","National Shelter Program Housing Assistance Delivery","For 2014-2016, the National Shelter Program seeks to deliver 510,683 units of housing assistance focusing on vulnerable households with an investment cost of PhP203.31 billion (breakdown in Table 6.10) based on the resource projections of key shelter agencies.",""],[1,"170","7","Housing Options and Assistance Menu","Strategy 8: Provide a menu of housing options/assistance based on the needs of intended housing beneficiaries",""],[1,"170","9","Informal Settler Family Upgrading and Relocation Programme","Addressing the needs of informal settler families (ISFs), through upgrading of structures in slums and development of relocation sites for those in danger areas.",""],[1,"170","10","Alternative Shelter and Housing Reconstruction Assistance","Providing either temporary or permanent alternative shelters or assistance in rebuilding the homes of victims of calamities such as typhoons, earthquakes, fire, and armed conflict.",""],[1,"170","11","Low-Cost and Socialized Housing Development","Meeting growing demand for housing from low-salaried employees by directly constructing and financing low-cost and socialized housing projects and by encouraging greater private sector participation in housing.",""],[1,"170","12","Pro-Poor Community-Led Housing and Shelter Security Program Scale-Up","In partnership with various agencies and LGUs, housing agencies will scale up implementation of pro-poor, community-led housing/shelter security programs.",""],[1,"274","4","Metro Manila Waterway Relocation and Housing Program","the government allocated PhP50 billion for the relocation of 104,219 informal settler families residing along Metro Manila waterways, with the National Housing Authority (NHA) implementing the program for off- and in-city relocation, the latter involving the construction of medium-rise buildings.","National Housing Authority (NHA)"],[1,"285","5","Socialized Housing Delivery Programme","The 2011-2016 target of the National Housing Authority (NHA) and Social Housing Finance Corporation (SHFC) is to provide 578,756 socialized housing units.",""]],"84":[[1,"48","5","Capital Inflows Management for Real Sector Investment","Achieving this objective calls for: (a) managing capital inflows towards real sector investment; (b) building the needed financial market infrastructure; and (c) pursuing the financial inclusion agenda.",""],[1,"48","5","Financial Market Infrastructure Development","Achieving this objective calls for: (a) managing capital inflows towards real sector investment; (b) building the needed financial market infrastructure; and (c) pursuing the financial inclusion agenda.",""],[1,"48","5","Financial Inclusion Agenda","Achieving this objective calls for: (a) managing capital inflows towards real sector investment; (b) building the needed financial market infrastructure; and (c) pursuing the financial inclusion agenda.",""],[1,"48","8","Financial Inclusion Regulatory and Outreach Measures","the following strategies already identified in the original PDP will be continued: (a) establishment of a regulatory environment that balances financial inclusion objectives with financial stability goals; (b) promotion of use of alternative products and delivery of financial services in underserved and unserved areas of the country; (c) promotion of financial literacy",""],[1,"49","1","Inclusive Banking Product Development and Consumer Education","encouraging the continuing development of new loan products and other banking services aimed to address the special needs of the poor, women and persons with disability.",""],[1,"49","2","Economic and Financial Learning Program","the Economic and Financial Learning Program of the Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas (BSP) to promote greater public awareness of economic and financial issues and provide information to enable households and businesses to make well-informed economic and financial decisions","Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas (BSP)"],[1,"49","2","Credit Surety Program","the BSP's Credit Surety Program, which creates a trust fund from the contributions of a provincial government and a cooperative in the same province to encourage financial institutions to lend to MSMEs in the province using the surety cover as a collateral substitute","Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas (BSP)"],[1,"49","3","Movable and Intangible Asset Collateral Framework","A system that will encourage financial institutions to accept other than real property assets as security for lending to MSMEs is also being established, with its framework being finalized in June 2013.",""],[1,"49","4","Bank Regulatory and Supervisory Framework Strengthening","measures to strengthen the regulatory and supervisory framework and enhance the risk management capability of banks will be sustained to ensure the stability of the system",""],[1,"72","1","Financial Inclusion Mainstreaming","the BSP will also continue to mainstream financial inclusion in its domestic policy agenda.",""],[1,"72","1","Microfinance Development Support","it will continue to adopt a proactive role in microfinance development in areas of policy and regulation, advocacy, training and capacity building to support the development of a sustainable microfinance business environment in the country.",""],[1,"130","1","Inclusive and Development-Oriented Financial System","Towards this end, a responsive, development-oriented and inclusive financial system will be pursued to serve as a platform for the efficient management and mobilization of resources that will provide alternative sources of financing for the country's economic development.",""],[1,"130","1","Liquidity Deployment for Underserved Groups","The government sees this situation as an opportunity, as it intends to deploy the liquidity buildup to serve the needs of the previously underserved and disadvantaged members of society.",""],[1,"130","2","Financial System Expansion and Prudential Regulation","The Updated Philippine Development Plan (PDP) for 2011-2016 emphasizes the continuous expansion of the financial system in support of rapid growth while facilitating inclusive growth.",""],[1,"136","1","Expanded Rural Assistance for Small Farmers, Fisherfolk, and MSMEs","The government, through the Land Bank of the Philippines (LBP) and Development Bank of the Philippines (DBP), continues to promote inclusive growth and alleviate poverty by creating opportunities in the countryside through expanded assistance to small farmers, fisherfolk and micro, small and medium enterprises (MSMEs).",""],[1,"137","9","Economic and Financial Learning Program","Continued the implementation of a multi-dimensional Economic and Financial Learning Program",""],[1,"137","10","Public Information Campaigns and Consumer Education on Economic and Financial Issues","Disseminated public information, through campaigns and consumer education programs on economic and financial issues to promote awareness and understanding of essential economic and financial issues.",""],[1,"137","12","Financial Inclusion Promotion Initiatives","Enhanced promotion of financial inclusion initiatives.","BSP"],[1,"141","10","Financial Inclusion Reform and Consumer Protection Measures","the government will continue to pursue reforms in policy regulation, supervision and accessibility.",""],[1,"141","10","Financial Education and Consumer Protection","Financial education and consumer protection will also be provided.",""],[1,"142","1","Economic and Financial Learning Program","Through its Economic and Financial Learning Program, the BSP will continue to promote greater public awareness of economic and financial issues and provide information to enable households and businesses to make well-informed economic and financial decisions.",""],[1,"142","1","Financial Literacy Seminars and Literature for Overseas Filipinos","Filipinos overseas and their families left behind are offered seminars and/or literature on financial literacy.",""],[1,"142","2","Credit Surety Program","The BSP's Credit Surety Program, a PPP initiative, will continue to support the government's poverty alleviation program and efforts to increase access to credit in the countryside.",""],[1,"142","2","Consumer Assistance and Redress Mechanism","the BSP will continue to provide an accessible avenue for consumer assistance and redress.",""],[1,"142","3","Movable Assets Collateral Framework for MSME Lending","The government will also establish a system that will encourage financial institutions to accept non-real property assets as security for lending to MSMEs in order to further boost economic development, financial inclusion and job generation.",""],[1,"142","4","Islamic Finance and Shari'ah-Compliant Stock Listing","Recently, the PSE has formally ventured into Islamic finance and released a list of Shari'ah-compliant stocks.",""],[1,"142","5","Movable Asset Collateral Lending System for MSMEs","The government will also establish a system that will encourage financial institutions to accept non-real property assets as security for lending to micro, small and medium enterprises.",""],[1,"143","2","Financial Inclusion Framework Development","It is also important to establish a framework for financial inclusion that will serve as input to the design of financial inclusion strategies, as well as the necessary policies and regulations.",""],[1,"143","2","Financial Inclusion Monitoring, Evaluation, and Feedback Mechanism","The effectiveness and impact of these initiatives will also be thoroughly monitored and evaluated and the proper feedback mechanism be put in place.",""]],"85":[[1,"50","6","National Justice Information System Phase I Completion","Phase I of the National Justice Information System will have been 100 percent completed by 2016.",""],[1,"50","7","Justice System Backlog Reduction and Case Docket Decongestion","Strategies to improve administration of justice include reducing backlogs and decongesting case dockets; instituting good governance in the justice system,",""],[1,"50","7","Good Governance in the Justice System","Strategies to improve administration of justice include reducing backlogs and decongesting case dockets; instituting good governance in the justice system,",""],[1,"51","1","Performance and Integrity Management Systems and Process Computerization","including performance and integrity management systems and computerization of processes and services;",""],[1,"51","1","Criminal Investigation Streamlining Reform","streamlining criminal investigation;",""],[1,"51","1","Justice System Fragmentation Reduction Reform","addressing fragmentation in the justice system;",""],[1,"51","1","Alternative Dispute Resolution Promotion Programme","promoting and maximizing Alternative Dispute Resolution;",""],[1,"51","1","Access to Justice for Poor and Vulnerable Sectors","enhancing access to justice by the poor and other vulnerable sectors through the implementation of the Recognizance Act of 2012 (RA 10389);",""],[1,"51","1","Jurisprudence Consistency and Stability Initiative","ensuring consistency and stability of jurisprudence.",""],[1,"194","11","Court Case Decongestion and Delay Reduction Measures","Case decongestion and delay reduction activities will be conducted, especially for courts that have high caseloads.",""],[1,"194","11","Judicial Vacancy Filling and Equipment Upgrade","For this purpose, filling of vacancies will be a priority.",""],[1,"194","11","Judiciary Backlog Reduction Target","The Supreme Court (SC) aims to reduce case backlogs in the judiciary by 15 percent.",""],[1,"194","11","Investigation Backlog Reduction Governance Reforms","The Department of Justice (DOJ), for its part, will pursue good governance reforms to reduce investigation backlogs.","Department of Justice (DOJ)"],[1,"195","1","Electronic Court System Expansion","The Electronic Court System or e-Courts Project ... will be the first step towards the eventual automation of the operations of all courts.",""],[1,"195","2","Judiciary Human Resources Development Program","The Court will pursue an 18-year Human Resources Development Program (HRDP) for the judiciary.",""],[1,"195","2","Judiciary Organization Development Reviews","Furthermore, organization development reviews will be implemented in judiciary offices and the courts to strengthen institutional capacity and operational efficiency.",""],[1,"196","5","Judicial Jurisprudence Consistency and Rationality Initiative","the judiciary will ensure consistency and rationality in jurisprudence through the decisions it renders before the courts.",""],[1,"222","7","New Criminal Code Reform","New Criminal Code, amending/updating the old Revised Penal Code, to be more responsive to new laws, current social conditions and emerging crime trends;",""],[1,"222","8","Criminal Investigation Law Reform","Criminal Investigation Law, rationalizing the investigation of crimes and criminal complaints by integrating the functions of investigating law enforcers and prosecutors, and repealing RA 5180 that prescribes the conduct of preliminary investigation by prosecutor;",""],[1,"223","1","Witness Protection Law Amendment and Program Strengthening","Amended Witness Protection Law, strengthening the Witness Protection, Security and Benefit Program by expanding its coverage and security capability;",""],[1,"223","8","NBI Modernization Law","NBI Modernization Law, strengthening the NBI's organization and functional structure to enhance and modernize its investigative capacity.",""]],"86":[[1,"49","4","Financial Sector Forum Coordination Mechanism","Macroeconomic and financial sector policies will be closely coordinated through the government's Financial Sector Forum",""],[1,"71","8","Expansion of BSP Data Collection Authority","Expansion of the authority of the BSP to obtain data from the non-bank sector.",""],[1,"72","5","Development Budget Coordination Committee Monitoring and Review Mechanism","the Development Budget Coordination Committee (DBCC) will serve as the interagency committee that will review and monitor the implementation of strategies identified in this chapter and the macroeconomic indicators.",""],[1,"131","7","Financial System Regulatory Framework Strengthening","Regulatory framework for the financial system strengthened and improved",""],[1,"134","6","Insurance Coverage Expansion and Consumer Confidence Building","increasing insurance coverage requires building the confidence of consumers in the system, informing the public about their options and rights, and introducing various designs of the instrument to cater to different consumers.",""],[1,"135","1","Insurance Net Worth Requirement Increase","the New Insurance Code (RA 10607) took effect which will further increase the minimum net worth of insurance companies to PhP1.3 billion by 2022.",""],[1,"135","3","Microinsurance Regulatory Compliance Monitoring","Monitor compliance with microinsurance regulations, especially on the Circular on Performance Standards to ensure the financial strength and stability of the Microinsurance providers;",""],[1,"135","6","Innovative Distribution Channel Rules and Guidelines","Develop appropriate rules and guidelines on innovative distribution channels that are effective but still affordable;",""],[1,"135","7","Alternative Dispute Resolution Mechanism","Pursue implementation of an alternative dispute resolution (ADR) mechanism to address complaints and resolve disputes in an accessible, practical and efficient manner.",""],[1,"136","4","Financial Sector Confidence and Consumer Education Measures","Financial sector authorities have adopted a pragmatic approach consisting of three activities: (a) increasing the confidence of the public about the health of the financial sector; (b) educating the public on financial instruments and their rights; and (c) encouraging the offering of a variety of products to cater to different consumers.",""],[1,"137","16","Derivatives Market Rules and Regulations","Adoption of rules and regulations regarding derivative products and trading",""],[1,"138","8","Implementation of Enacted Financial Sector Legislative Measures","Proper and immediate implementation of the enacted Financial Sector legislative measures",""],[1,"139","1","Financial Sector Strategic Framework","the strategic framework for the financial sector must involve: (a) managing the capital inflows towards investments in the productive sector; (b) building the needed financial market infrastructure; and (c) pursuing the financial inclusion agenda.",""],[1,"139","5","Financial System Regulatory Framework Strengthening","Regulatory framework for the financial system strengthened and improved",""],[1,"139","7","Capital Inflow Management for Productive Sector Investment","Manage the capital inflows towards investments in the productive sector",""],[1,"139","8","Financial Market Infrastructure Development","2. Build the needed financial market infrastructure",""],[1,"141","7","Mandatory Financial Market Infrastructure Governance Strengthening","In the immediate term, it is important to define the mandatory financial market infrastructures and the strategies to strengthen their governance structure.",""],[1,"142","7","Financial Sector Regulatory and Supervisory Framework Strengthening","Key reforms that will strengthen the regulatory and supervisory framework and enhance responsible risk management by banks will be sustained to maintain the stability of the financial system.",""],[1,"142","7","Alignment of Prudential Standards with International Norms","Policy initiatives will continue to focus on aligning prudential standards with international norms, and enhancing the implementation of existing banking rules and regulations.",""],[1,"142","7","Financial Sector Forum Coordination Mechanism","closer coordination of macroeconomic and financial sector policies shall be enhanced through the government's Financial Sector Forum (FSF).",""],[1,"142","8","Financial Stability Policy and Regulatory Guidance","However, these can be influenced by policy directions and regulatory instruments consistent with the financial stability agenda.",""],[1,"142","9","Financial Sector Coordination Framework","The FSF principally provides an institutionalized framework for coordinating the supervision and regulation of the financial system, for strengthening the exchange of information among the different regulators, and for the promotion of better consumer protection.",""],[1,"143","1","Financial Stability Institutional Mandate and Macroprudential Policy Framework","Going forward, it is important to designate an institution whose mandate is to maintain financial stability, and recognize the role the Financial Stability Coordinating Council (FSCC) plays in the overall financial stability agenda.",""],[1,"143","3","Financial Sector Regulatory Strengthening","To prevent and minimize systemic risks, efforts will be made to strengthen regulations in the face of current challenges.",""],[1,"143","3","Timely Legislative Agenda for Financial Sector Targets","Emphasis will be placed on the timely passage of legislative agenda to achieve financial sector targets by prioritizing the following:",""],[1,"143","9","Real Estate Investment Trust Law Amendment","· Amendments to the Real Estate Investment Trust Law (REIT);",""],[1,"143","10","Pension Fund Regulation Bill","Bill on Pension Fund Regulation;",""],[1,"143","15","Designation of Financial Stability Institution","It is important to designate an institution whose mandate is to maintain financial stability, and recognize the role the Financial Stability Coordinating Council plays in the overall financial stability agenda.",""],[1,"320","15","Interagency Financial Sector Coordination Framework","It principally provides for an institutionalized framework for coordinating the supervision and regulation of the financial system, for strengthening the exchange of information among the different regulators and for the promotion of better consumer protection.",""],[1,"320","17","Voluntary Interagency Council on Systemic Risk","A voluntary interagency council whose key objective is to identify, manage and mitigate the build-up of systemic risks.","Insurance Commission | Department of Finance | Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas | Securities and Exchange Commission | Philippine Deposit Insurance Corporation"]],"87":[[1,"150","4","Expand Health Insurance Coverage","To ensure financial risk protection, efforts will be geared towards increasing insurance coverage to 90 percent by 2015 and 95 percent by 2016.",""],[1,"151","3","Expand National Health Insurance Coverage and Benefits","Improve financial risk protection by expanding national health insurance coverage and benefits;",""],[1,"151","6","Sin Tax Reform Law","The Sin Tax Reform Law (RA 10351) and Responsible Parenthood and Reproductive Health Act of 2012 (RA 10354) are two major opportunities now available to intensify KP interventions that will eventually contribute to improved health status.",""],[1,"151","7","Sin Tax Revenue Financing for Health Investments","The Sin Tax Reform Law is expected to generate enough revenue to finance much needed investments in health.",""],[1,"151","7","Expanded National Health Insurance Coverage for Poor and Near-Poor Families","A total of 14.7 million poor identified in the National Household Targeting System for Poverty Reduction (NHTS-PR) from Category 1 provinces, as well as near-poor families, can be enrolled under the National Health Insurance Program (NHIP) with the expected windfall from sin tax revenues.",""],[1,"152","3","PhilHealth Coverage and Benefits Expansion","This strategy entails increasing Philippine Health Insurance (PhilHealth) coverage and benefits.",""],[1,"152","4","Point-of-Care Coverage for Informal and Self-Employed Workers","A strategy to reach more of the poor self-employed and those in the informal sectors is to cover them at the point of care.",""],[1,"152","5","Health Benefit Coverage Improvement and Provider Payment Reform","the necessary improvement includes a full shift in provider payment system from fee-for-service to case-based rates, providing no-balance billing arrangements for indigent members, strengthening gatekeeping mechanisms through the implementation and gradual expansion of the primary care benefits, and financing more catastrophic conditions.",""],[1,"152","6","Point-of-Care Coverage for Informal and Self-Employed Workers","A strategy to reach more of the poor self-employed and those in the informal sectors is to cover them at the point of care.",""],[1,"338","9","Excise Tax Restructuring for Universal Health Care Financing","An act restructuring the excise tax on alcohol and tobacco products.",""],[1,"347","5","Focused Health Reform Implementation for the Poor","A focused approach to health reform implementation, ensuring that all Filipinos especially the poor receive the benefits of health reform.",""]],"88":[[1,"146","4","Human Capabilities Improvement Programme","the PDP seeks to (a) improve human capabilities through better health and nutrition and through enhancement of knowledge and skills",""],[1,"151","2","Preventive and Promotive Health Program Scale-Up","Achieve health-related MDGs by scaling-up promising preventive and promotive health programs and improving health-seeking behavior among the most vulnerable population;",""],[1,"151","6","Responsible Parenthood and Reproductive Health Act Implementation","The Sin Tax Reform Law (RA 10351) and Responsible Parenthood and Reproductive Health Act of 2012 (RA 10354) are two major opportunities now available to intensify KP interventions that will eventually contribute to improved health status.",""],[1,"152","1","Hiring and Training of Skilled Health and Nutrition Workers","The government's policy to focus on poor families would also require hiring and training of additional skilled health and nutrition workers especially in disadvantaged areas to deliver the required public health care services for poor families.",""]],"89":[[1,"179","11","Access to Information and Citizen Participation Mechanisms","Opening access to information and establishing venues for participation on various dimensions of governance empowers the citizenry.",""],[1,"180","2","Public Access to Information Law and Procedures","There is a need to provide uniform, clear, and speedy procedures for accessing information on all government transactions.",""],[1,"181","13","Open Government Partnership Country Action Plan","the Philippines will develop and implement a Country Action Plan that contains initiatives in line with the OGP's principles of engagement",""],[1,"182","1","Annual People's Budget Publication","The People's Budget will be published on an annual basis",""],[1,"182","1","Budget ng Bayan Citizen Budget Portal","The Budget ng Bayan website will continue to be an interactive platform where citizens can learn more about the government budget and file reports on budget utilization.",""],[1,"182","3","National Government Portal","The Official Gazette (www.gov.ph), the official journal of the Republic of the Philippines, will serve as the National Government Portal-a unified interface in the form of a one-stop source for information and service delivery.",""],[1,"182","3","Online Feedback Mechanism Enhancement","The online feedback mechanism featured in the site will continually be enhanced.",""],[1,"182","4","Open Data Portal Development","the Open Data Portal (data.gov.ph) will be created to provide citizens and government researchers with the means to access, scrutinize, and analyze raw aggregate datasets from the government",""]],"90":[[1,"321","4","Responsible Fiscal Management Bill","A proposed bill which aims to strengthen fiscal discipline in the public sector by prescribing principles of responsible fiscal management, establishing control mechanisms on spending, and adopting preventive measures against the erosion of the tax base of the government.",""]],"91":[[1,"43","3","Peace-Building and Conflict Resolution Efforts","peace-building efforts should be earnestly pursued by addressing the fundamental bases of the conflicts.",""],[1,"44","1","Peace and Sustainable Development Promotion Measures","At the same time, efforts to promote lasting peace and sustainable development will be implemented.",""],[1,"51","5","Negotiated Political Settlement of Internal Armed Conflict","the government will continue to pursue negotiated political settlement of internal armed conflict",""],[1,"51","5","Payapa at Masaganang Pamayanan (PAMANA) Flagship Development Program","The Payapa at Masaganang Pamayanan (PAMANA) will remain as the flagship development program that aims to bring back the government's presence in conflict-affected communities through improved access to basic social services, strengthening of institutions, and protection of children's and women's rights, as well as ensuring their participation in peace building and development efforts.",""],[1,"51","7","Negotiated Political Settlement of Internal Armed Conflict","The government will continue to pursue negotiated political settlement of internal armed conflict.",""],[1,"207","1","Community Resilience and Peacebuilding Support","The complementary track facilitates positive sociopolitical conditions that support peace negotiations and operates under three general themes: (a) building community resilience against armed violence; (b) strengthening institutions; and (c) mainstreaming conflict-sensitive, peace-building and gender-sensitive lens in governance.",""],[1,"207","2","PAMANA Focused Development Program","The \"Payapa at Masaganang Pamayanan\" or PAMANA is the national government's focused development program for isolated, hard-to-reach, and conflict-affected communities (Table 8.1).",""],[1,"207","2","Autonomous Region in Muslim Mindanao Transition Investment Support Program","Another development initiative is the PhP8.5-billion Autonomous Region in Muslim Mindanao Transition Investment Support Program (ARMM-TISP) that addresses infrastructure and support-services gaps in the region.",""],[1,"213","1","Whole-of-Society Peacebuilding and Security Approach","peace and security efforts will be anchored on a whole-of-society approach by creating a national consensus and understanding of security and deepening of commitment and involvement towards peace building.",""],[1,"213","4","Community Peacebuilding and Recovery Support","The government aims to significantly increase the number of communities in conflict-affected areas that are able to return to peaceful conditions where they can achieve their desired quality of life.",""],[1,"217","13","PAMANA Conflict-Affected Area Development Program","PAMANA will remain as the flagship development program in areas affected by conflict, but with greater convergence with other existing government programs and LGU plans.",""],[1,"218","1","PAMANA Implementing Partners Capacity-Building","All PAMANA implementing partners will be continuously capacitated in order to ensure that PAMANA implementation helps mitigate existing causes of conflict and prevent the occurrence of new ones.",""],[1,"218","2","ARMM Governance Reform and Basic Services Delivery Acceleration","The government will continue to strengthen reforms initiated when the interim ARMM Governor took office in 2012, as well as accelerate the delivery of basic services to catch up with the attainment of the Millennium Development Goals",""],[1,"333","16","Peacebuilding, Reconstruction and Development Framework for Conflict-Affected Areas","The national government's peace and development framework to respond and strengthen peace building, reconstruction and development in conflict- affected areas.",""]],"92":[[1,"186","1","Seal of Good Local Governance Incentive and Performance Challenge Fund","As an incentive for improving LGU performance, the DILG confers an SGLG to LGUs that practice accountable, transparent, and participatory governance and improve frontline service performance.","DILG"],[1,"186","2","Government Quality Management Program","The Development Academy of the Philippines (DAP) implemented the Government Quality Management Program (GQMP) to align the agencies' planning, service, and support operations with ISO 9001 International Standards and to make \"citizen satisfaction\" as the focus of quality improvement efforts.","Development Academy of the Philippines (DAP)"],[1,"186","7","Performance Monitoring, Evaluation, Reporting and Incentive Systems Improvement","Improve performance M&E, reporting and incentive systems;",""],[1,"188","6","Performance Monitoring, Evaluation, Reporting and Incentive Systems Improvement","The government will further improve systems for performance M&E, reporting and incentive systems.",""],[1,"188","7","RBPMS Framework Improvement","The Interagency Task Force created under Administrative Order (AO) 25 will continue to improve the RBPMS framework.",""],[1,"189","1","Strategic Performance Management System Enhancement","the performance monitoring and appraisal system embodied in the Strategic Performance Management System (SPMS), designed by the Civil Service Commission (CSC), will be enhanced.","Civil Service Commission (CSC)"],[1,"189","2","Strategic Performance Management System Implementation","In 2012, 390 SPMS were already approved for initial implementation.",""],[1,"189","3","Local Governance Performance Incentive System","In terms of LGU performance, the DILG will scale up the SGLG to include gauging LGU performance not only in the areas of good financial housekeeping and people's participation, but also on important areas such as business competitiveness, disaster preparedness, environmental protection, social protection, peace and order and public safety.","DILG"],[1,"189","3","Gawad Pamana ng Lahi Award Continuation","Moreover, conferment of the Gawad Pamana ng Lahi award will be continued for LGUs that have shown exemplary performance in administrative, social, economic and environmental governance.","DILG"],[1,"189","3","Provincial Competitiveness Fund Incentive Support","The DILG will also continue to incentivize good performing LGUs through the PCF.","DILG"],[1,"189","3","PCF Project Monitoring and Governance Performance Management Reform","To make this initiative felt by the public, the DILG will improve the M&E of PCF-supported projects and strengthen policies on local governance performance management and incentive systems.","DILG"],[1,"189","5","Public Officials Competence Enhancement Program","Government will continue and strengthen programs that enhance the competence of public officials to efficiently deliver quality public services.",""],[1,"189","6","ISO 9001 Quality Management System Adoption","Under the GQMP, established through EO 605, the government has adopted the ISO 9001 QMS.",""],[1,"189","6","Career Executive Service Development Program Enhancement","The government will also enhance the Career Executive Service Development Program (CESDP) by addressing the development and team",""],[1,"190","1","Public Management Development Program","the Public Management Development Program (PMDP) will foster careerism in government and promote stability in the bureaucracy by producing a corps of development-oriented, competent, dedicated and honest government senior executives and middle managers.",""],[1,"191","1","Philippine Quality Awards for the Public Sector","The conferment of the Philippine Quality Awards (PQAs) for the public sector will be continued to recognize government agencies that excel in quality and productivity and with established quality management system.",""],[1,"334","14","Employee Incentive Bonus Scheme","An incentive/ bonus that is provided to employees across the board, regardless of their actual performance.",""],[1,"334","16","Performance-Based Bonus Program","A merit-based incentive program that recognizes and rewards exemplary performance in government.",""],[1,"335","8","National Performance Excellence Award Program","A national award program that recognizes achievements of public and private sector organizations in their efforts to attain performance excellence.",""],[1,"340","17","Unified Performance Monitoring, Evaluation, and Reporting System","A unified system for monitoring, evaluating, and reporting the performance of national government agencies (NGAs) that serves as basis for determining entitlement of the performance-based bonus (PBB) for national government personnel in the executive department.",""],[1,"342","4","Local Government Performance Monitoring and Recognition Mechanism","A mechanism that monitors and recognizes adherence of local government (LGUs) to performance criteria on any of the following areas: good financial housekeeping, disaster preparedness, social protection for the basic sector, business friendliness and competitiveness, environmental compliance, and law and order and public safety.",""],[1,"342","15","Service Delivery Enhancement Program","A program of the Civil Service Commission (CSC) which aims to immediately assist and provide solutions for agencies that have failed to comply with their Citizen's Charter.","Civil Service Commission (CSC)"]],"93":[[1,"186","10","Interagency Coordination Strengthening","Strengthen interagency coordination.",""],[1,"188","5","Migration Data Harmonization and SGISM Operationalization","administrative and field data of various government agencies on international migration will be harmonized for evidence-based policymaking and planning.",""],[1,"188","5","Shared Government Information System on Migration Operationalization","The Shared Government Information System on Migration (SGISM) will be operationalized in response to the challenges and opportunities of migration.",""],[1,"191","2","Public Sector Openness and Collaboration Reform","government agencies will move toward greater openness and collaboration.",""],[1,"191","3","Interagency Coordination Strengthening through Cabinet Systems","Interagency coordination will be strengthened through the Cabinet Clusters (EO 43) and the Cabinet Assistance System (CAS) (EO 99).",""],[1,"191","3","Agency Issue Resolution and Project Streamlining Forum","Agencies will use these systems as a forum to discuss, streamline and resolve issues affecting their day-to- day operations, as well as their respective projects.",""],[1,"191","5","Cabinet Assistance System for Priority Project Coordination","under EO 99, the CAS was created to provide support to the Cabinet Secretary, who is in charge of monitoring and ensuring timely execution of priority projects or programs under the President's Social Contract and PDP.",""],[1,"191","8","Government Openness and Collaboration Initiative","government agencies will move toward greater openness and collaboration.",""],[1,"198","2","GGACC Strategy Coordination and Oversight Mechanism","The GGACC, created under EO 43 of 2011, will coordinate and oversee the implementation of these strategies",""],[1,"328","7","Inter-Agency Coordination Body for Joint Initiatives","An inter-agency body composed of senior representatives from the Judiciary, the of Justice (DOJ), the Department of the Interior and Local Government (DILG), and their relevant attached agencies, which serves as a joint forum for dialogue on issues of common interest and mechanism for effective coordination and sharing of information for planning and implementation of joint initiatives.","Judiciary | Department of Justice (DOJ) | Department of the Interior and Local Government (DILG)"],[1,"328","10","Barangay Small-Scale Projects Support Program","A program for implementing small-scale projects by barangays following their own plans, priorities, and processes, with funding support and in-kind support from the national and local governments.",""]],"94":[[1,"310","11","Government Executive Development Program","A program of the Development Academy of the Philippines (DAP) that aims to produce a cadre of government executives that are knowledgeable, skilled, and committed to multi-sectoral development and high quality of public service.",""],[1,"336","6","Public Managers Capacity-Building Program","An intensive program that provides comprehensive and multi-modal learning opportunities for public managers.",""],[1,"336","15","Executive Branch Efficiency and Core Functions Reform","A move to transform the Executive Branch into a more effective and efficient government.",""]],"95":[[1,"53","3","Strategic Public Investment and Regulation for Inclusive Service Delivery","government will intervene strategically where the private sector cannot be relied upon to deliver the goods, services and facilities needed by the poor and marginalized.",""],[1,"53","4","Agency Program Convergence and Multi-Stakeholder Coordination Mechanism","PDP implementation calls for convergence of agency programs and coordination among agencies at different levels as well as the private sector and development partners to be able to make a significant impact.",""],[1,"53","4","Implementation Progress Monitoring Mechanism","During the implementation period, the efficiency and effectiveness of these strategies will be monitored alongside implementation progress.",""],[1,"53","5","Planning Committee Monitoring and Reporting Mechanism","The different Planning Committees (PC), constituted to update the Plan, will be responsible for monitoring welfare outcomes and implementation progress as indicated in their corresponding Results Matrices.",""],[1,"53","5","Interagency Reporting and Coordination Arrangement","The outcomes and progress will then be reported by the PC Chair before an appropriate interagency committee of the National Economic and Development Authority (NEDA) Board or Cabinet Cluster, as shown in Table 1.9.","National Economic and Development Authority (NEDA) Board | Cabinet Cluster"],[1,"53","6","Annual Socioeconomic Report Preparation","The NEDA Secretariat will also prepare an annual Socioeconomic Report (SER), where each SER presents the accomplishment in terms of output and desired outcomes, identifies key challenges and recommends solutions going forward.","NEDA Secretariat"],[1,"68","3","International Finance Management Enhancement","international finance management will be enhanced through strategic mobilization and allocation of funds.",""],[1,"126","2","Plan Target Monitoring and Reporting System","For proper monitoring of Plan targets, all concerned agencies are expected to regularly submit progress reports (e.g. quarterly and annual) to the NEDA Secretariat for consolidation and subsequent transmittal to the Economic Development Cluster (Econ Cluster).",""],[1,"126","2","Plan Target Oversight and Tracking Mechanism","The Econ Cluster will exercise oversight functions in tracking the progress and achievements of the implementing agencies vis-a-vis the Plan targets.",""],[1,"126","2","Annual Plan Indicator and Target Updating Process","The indicators and targets will continue to be enhanced and updated annually through an iterative process involving collaboration of sector agencies, statistical agencies, research institutions, the academe and civil society organizations.",""]],"96":[[1,"328","13","Employment Opportunity Enhancement Measures","Measures aimed at enhancing employment opportunities and protection of the rights and welfare of workers.",""]],"97":[[1,"14","8","National Industry Cluster Capacity Enhancement Project","The National Industry Cluster Capacity Enhancement Project: Bolstering pilot industry clusters",""],[1,"36","3","Business Climate Improvement and Productivity Enhancement Measures","specific interventions need to be undertaken to improve business climate, increase productivity and improve innovative capacity.",""],[1,"37","1","Business Intelligence Support and Product Quality Monitoring Infrastructure","the government will provide comprehensive business intelligence to enable businesses to make informed decisions.",""],[1,"37","1","Product Quality Monitoring Infrastructure Investment","It will also invest in the needed product quality monitoring infrastructure to ensure that the country's products meet international standards to penetrate export markets.",""],[1,"37","2","Industry Clustering Expansion Program","The industry clustering program will be expanded.",""],[1,"37","3","Innovation and Product Development Support Programme","Innovation and product development will be supported.",""],[1,"42","3","Investment Promotion for Employment Creation","interventions should be aimed at increasing investments to create more employment opportunities.",""],[1,"43","3","Agriculture-Based Enterprise Support for Supply Chains","Small agriculture-based enterprises linked to the supply chain of product or service providers in the more developed areas of the region should be encouraged as a way of increasing employment and ensuring incomes.",""],[1,"43","4","Integrated Coconut Industry Development and Poverty Reduction Project","The implementation of this project, initially in Category 2 provinces, will be continuously monitored for possible replication to cover other areas producing coconuts and/or other commodities.",""],[1,"83","2","Industry Roadmap Implementation","Industry roadmaps will be implemented and will serve as bases of the Comprehensive National Industrial Strategy (CNIS).",""],[1,"83","2","Comprehensive National Industrial Strategy Development","The CNIS will include strategies to strengthen the link with basic sectors as suppliers (i.e., link to agriculture sector for raw materials) or markets (i.e., potential for downstream link) and to make local industries more competitive in preparation for greater regional and global integration.",""],[1,"85","14","Industry Cluster Development Expansion","5. Expand industry cluster development",""],[1,"85","17","Agriculture-Industry Linkage Strengthening Program","The government will pursue programs/interventions that strengthen agriculture- industry linkage.",""],[1,"85","17","Large Enterprise-MSME Partnership Promotion","Large enterprises will be encouraged to partner with MSMEs.",""],[1,"85","18","Agriculture-Based Sector Development","Agriculture-based sectors, such as, but not limited to, coconut, coffee, furniture, garments, fisheries and forest-based sectors, will be developed given their potential",""],[1,"86","4","Manufacturing Revival Program","The manufacturing sector will be revitalized through the implementation of the Manufacturing Revival Program by various national agencies.",""],[1,"86","5","Promotion of Nearby Product Manufacturing","The private sector will be encouraged to venture to \"nearby products\" with highest spillover effects including, among others, manufacture of digital data processing machines, watches, cameras, television, and clocks.",""],[1,"86","5","Promotion of Labor-Intensive Manufacturing Subsectors","To boost employment, labor-intensive manufacturing subsectors (e.g. garments, footwear, processed foods, furniture, etc.) will also be promoted.",""],[1,"91","1","Industry Cluster Development Initiative","Increasing productivity will require harnessing science, technology and innovation, enhancing the competencies of the labor force, and expanding industry cluster development.",""],[1,"91","3","Technology Catch-Up Programs for Local Industries","Local industries will be encouraged to benchmark processing technologies with countries considered leaders in specific industries (e.g. food processing in Thailand and Taiwan) and to design and implement technology catch-up programs to make them at par with benchmarked countries.",""],[1,"93","2","Industry Cluster Development Approach","To the extent possible, the industry-cluster approach will be used to develop the identified key sectors.",""],[1,"93","2","Agriculture-Industry Linkage and SME Integration","The approach will promote linkage between agriculture and industry (processing) to increase value- added of products.",""],[1,"93","3","Industry Clustering Expansion Program","The industry clustering program will be expanded.",""],[1,"93","3","Sectoral Roadmap Development for Industry Linkages","Industries need to prepare sectoral roadmaps that will show linkage with basic sectors as suppliers and/or markets.",""],[1,"93","7","Sectoral Roadmap Development for Industry Linkages","Industries need to prepare sectoral roadmaps that will show linkage with basic sectors as suppliers and/or markets.",""],[1,"120","6","National Industry Cluster Capacity Enhancement Project","The National Industry Cluster Capacity Enhancement Project (NICCEP) is a three- year technical cooperation project funded by the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA).",""],[1,"120","7","NICCEP Capacity-Building Trainings","Through the NICCEP, the government is able to provide capacity-building trainings and related activities that help boost sector stakeholders' participation in the value chain, thereby enabling them to maximize available entrepreneurial opportunities beyond farming.",""]],"98":[[1,"86","3","Halal Industry Development Initiative","The halal industry will be developed, especially in Mindanao.",""],[1,"86","6","Halal Industry Development Programme","The halal industry will be developed, especially in Mindanao.",""],[1,"86","6","Producer Support on Manufacturing Standards and Clean Production","The government will continue to provide information to producers on good manufacturing practices, international standards, and clean production technologies, among others, as well as provide metrology, calibration and accreditation services.",""],[1,"86","7","Shipbuilding Industry Investment Expansion","The country will also continue to promote and expand investments in the shipbuilding industry especially in the Visayas area.",""],[1,"86","8","Mineral Processing and Value-Adding Framework","A framework for mineral processing/value-adding will be formulated.",""],[1,"91","4","Sustainable Mining and Green Technology Support","Mining and minerals processing industries will be provided with sustainable practices and green technologies, not only to add value to extracted minerals, but also to promote better and responsible mining practices.",""],[1,"91","5","Advanced Product Development Support Facilities","The government will provide state-of-the-art facilities to assist local companies to undertake design, prototyping, and product development (e.g. Advanced Materials Testing Laboratory, Electronic Product Development Center, and Philippine IC Design Center, among others).",""]],"99":[[1,"89","3","Investment Liberalization Reform","Liberalize certain investment areas, except those provided in the Constitution, to increase investments and generate more and decent employment;",""],[1,"90","3","Private-Sector-Led Economic Zone Development Support","The government will continue to adhere to its policy that the development of economic zones is private sector-led but with appropriate and strategic support from the government.",""],[1,"90","7","Economic Zones Development Support","The development of economic zones is private sector-led but with appropriate and strategic support from the government.",""],[1,"95","2","Priority Sector Investment Promotion and Business Intelligence Support","The government will focus its investment promotion activities in the identified priority sectors and provide comprehensive business intelligence to enable businesses to make informed decisions.",""],[1,"95","2","Harmonization of Investment Promotion Programs","Investment promotion programs of the national IPAs and LGUs will be harmonized.",""],[1,"95","3","Investment Promotion Outreach Expansion","The IPAs will intensify promotion efforts in countries such as Japan, Netherlands, US and Korea, while at the same time strategically reach out to developmental markets with strong potential for outward investments such as Russia, Brazil, Middle East, among others.",""],[1,"96","3","Targeted Media Campaign in Priority Investment Source Countries","The government will undertake a highly targeted media campaign in priority investment source countries.",""],[1,"96","3","Unified Country Branding Promotion","The Philippines will aggressively promote unified country branding that will bring home the message that it is a producer and supplier of high quality, ethical, sustainable and world-class products and services that are valued worldwide.",""],[1,"96","3","Promotion of Philippine-Made Products and Local Technology","Buying of Philippine-made products and local technology works will also be promoted.",""]],"100":[[1,"91","2","Climate-Smart and Clean Technology Promotion","Climate-smart/clean technologies will also be developed and promoted.",""],[1,"94","8","MSME Green Economy Awareness Initiative","Initiatives will be undertaken to increase awareness among MSMEs on the effects of climate change and how green economy can foster long-term competitiveness.",""],[1,"94","8","Climate-Smart and Eco-Efficient Industrial Support","the government will promote, develop and sustain I&S that are climate-smart and -resilient, eco-efficient and environment friendly.",""]],"101":[[1,"5","3","Direct Investment in Health, Education, and Employment","we need to invest directly in health, education, and employment to enhance the power of growth to reduce poverty",""],[1,"6","2","Public Investment, Public Services, and Social Program Financing","Now, the government has considerable fiscal space for making investments to catalyze private ventures, provide public goods and services, as well as fund social programs all aimed at reducing poverty and creating opportunities for everyone.",""],[1,"6","5","Quality-of-Life and Multidimensional Poverty Reduction Strategy","Also, the Updated Plan is committed to quality-of-life targets such as creating the conditions for productive and remunerative work and improving overall well-being.",""],[1,"6","6","Poverty Constraint Removal Efforts","Instead, we are engaging in concerted efforts to remove the constraints experienced by the poor to enable them to take advantage of growth opportunities.",""],[1,"28","7","Wide-Ranging Economic and Social Reform Agenda","the present government is in a position to institute wide-ranging economic and social reforms in pursuit of inclusive development.",""],[1,"31","3","Geographically and Sectorally Tailored Growth Strategy Design","key growth strategies will need to be informed by geographical and sectoral specificities, as different sectors or groups of the population are differently situated and respond differently to interventions based on their geography",""],[1,"39","1","Province-Based Poverty Constraint Targeting","the Updated Plan will deliberately address the constraints faced by the poor as summarized by their province of residence.",""],[1,"43","3","Basic Social Services Expansion in Category 2 Provinces","the imperative is to ensure that basic social services in the form of health services, basic education, water and sanitation are available.",""],[1,"43","3","Spatially Blind Infrastructure Investment","These \"spatially blind\" investments promote economic and physical mobility, making it possible for people in these areas to out-migrate, if necessary, to gain access to opportunities wherever these may be while economic opportunities in the area are still being created.",""],[1,"44","1","Human and Physical Capital and Financing Support Measures","The above strategies will be supported by a menu of interventions to improve the quality of human and physical capital and access to financing.",""],[1,"47","1","Infrastructure Support for Conflict-Affected and Impoverished Areas","The government will continue providing infrastructure support to conflict-affected and impoverished areas through the Investment Support Program (ISP) for the ARMM and the Payapa at Masaganang Pamayanan or PAMANA Program.",""]],"102":[[1,"342","8","Secondary Mortgage Market Development","A market for the purchase and sale of existing mortgages, designed to provide greater liquidity for selling mortgages.",""],[1,"347","9","Land and Real Property Valuation Reform Legislation","A proposed legislative measure that seeks to institutionalize reforms in land and real property valuation intended to improve the administration of real property and related taxes.",""]],"103":[[1,"44","7","Health Service Delivery Improvement","The Updated Plan commits to achieving these unmet targets by improving the delivery of health services.",""],[1,"44","7","Health and Nutrition Workforce Recruitment and Training","government will intensify programs to hire and train additional skilled health and nutrition workers especially in disadvantaged areas to deliver the required public health care services for poor families.",""],[1,"45","4","PhilHealth Coverage and Benefits Expansion","Increasing Philippine Health Insurance (PhilHealth) coverage and benefits is a major social protection program.",""],[1,"46","10","Basic Health Care Infrastructure Expansion","the government will massively construct, rehabilitate and upgrade basic health care hospitals and facilities",""]],"104":[[1,"223","3","Philippine Maritime Zones Legislation","Philippine Maritime Zones, providing the necessary flexibility in the enactment of subsequent laws pertinent to the rights and obligations of the Philippines over its own maritime zones in accordance with the UNCLOS;",""],[1,"223","4","Philippine Archipelagic Sea Lanes Establishment","Philippine Archipelagic Sea Lanes, establishing the Philippines' archipelagic sea lanes as espoused in Article 53 of the UNCLOS;",""],[1,"223","5","New Philippine Immigration Law","New Philippine Immigration Law, amending the old immigration law to improve border control and management in the face of transnational crimes, human trafficking, migration trends, continued increase of overseas workers, and tourism development;",""],[1,"259","1","Maritime Zone Delimitation Framework","This will define the limits of the country's various maritime zones, including internal and archipelagic waters, territorial sea, contiguous and exclusive economic zones, consistent with the United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea;",""]],"105":[[1,"51","6","Intensified Law Enforcement Operations Against Criminality and Armed Violence","The police and other law enforcement agencies will intensify their operations against criminality, armed violence and transnational",""],[1,"52","2","Rules-Based Collective Security Framework","The government will also exert all efforts to ensure the country's sovereignty over its territories by pursuing a rules-based collective security framework in international relations.",""],[1,"52","2","Disaster and Emergency Preparedness Capacity Enhancement","Moreover, given the increasing occurrences of extreme natural hazard events, the government will increase its capability in preparedness against natural as well as human-induced disasters and emergencies to protect lives and properties of its citizens.",""],[1,"212","1","Disaster Preparedness and Response Capacity Upgrade","the government strengthened its disaster preparedness and response operations by upgrading capability and response skills and conducting reorientation of its forces down to the local level",""],[1,"221","9","Security Sector Disaster Response Capability Development","it is also imperative to strengthen the security sector in emergency relief and rescue operations by developing its organic capability to respond to calamities and disasters.",""],[1,"221","9","Stakeholder Synergy for Disaster Prevention and Preparedness","it will promote synergy among stakeholders and the communities in disaster prevention and preparation",""],[1,"221","9","Critical Infrastructure Protection Measures","it will secure and protect critical infrastructures, facilities and other high value assets of the public and private sector",""]],"106":[[1,"88","2","Construction Investment Promotion","The country will also promote investments in construction (e.g. infrastructure projects, mass housing and housing related materials, etc.).",""],[1,"88","2","Public-Private Partnership Governance and Monitoring for Construction","A strong public-private partnership will be pursued to effectively govern and monitor the sector.",""],[1,"88","2","Contractors Licensing and Registration Liberalization","The government in partnership with the private sector will pursue the liberalization of contractors licensing and registration, promotion and development of domestic and overseas construction, and efficient implementation of the dispute resolution mechanism.",""],[1,"88","2","Domestic and Overseas Construction Development","The government in partnership with the private sector will pursue the liberalization of contractors licensing and registration, promotion and development of domestic and overseas construction, and efficient implementation of the dispute resolution mechanism.",""],[1,"88","2","Construction Dispute Resolution Mechanism","The government in partnership with the private sector will pursue the liberalization of contractors licensing and registration, promotion and development of domestic and overseas construction, and efficient implementation of the dispute resolution mechanism.",""]],"107":[[1,"279","9","Irrigation System Development and Rehabilitation","To intensify rice production, among others, development and rehabilitation of irrigation systems will be pursued.",""],[1,"279","9","Small Water Impounding Projects","Small water impounding projects, among others, will be established, where and when feasible, to augment the demand for water.",""],[1,"279","9","Irrigation Management Transfer","In parallel, irrigation management transfer will be undertaken so that irrigators' associations will be more efficient in operating and managing secondary canals and on-farm structures in larger systems, as well as entire systems covering more than 3,000 hectares.",""]],"108":[[1,"331","2","Basic Electricity Service Provision in Unviable Areas","The provision of basic electricity service in unviable areas with the aim of bringing the operations in these areas to viability levels.",""],[1,"347","4","Universal Charge Allocation Mechanism for Electricity End-Users","A fixed amount approved by the ERC pursuant to Section 34 of RA 9136 imposed on all electricity end-users for: a) the payment of stranded debts in excess of the amount assumed by the National Government and stranded contract costs of NPC; b) missionary electrification; c) equalization of the taxes and royalties applied to indigenous or renewable sources of energy vis-à-vis imported energy fuels; and d) environmental charge.",""]],"109":[[1,"208","4","Women, Peace and Security Participation Initiative","Major strides have also been made in ensuring women's participation in the peace process, with the National Steering Committee on Women, Peace and Security taking the lead.",""],[1,"208","4","Grassroots Women's Peacebuilding Empowerment","Greater efforts are exerted to empower women at the grassroots level to participate in local conflict resolution, peace- building and post-conflict rehabilitation.",""],[1,"208","4","Capacity Building for Gender-Based Violence Response","There is also a need to strengthen the capabilities and skills of security forces and service delivery agents to respond to sexual and gender-based violence in affected areas, and be able to provide victims with appropriate support.",""],[1,"217","5","Gender-Responsive and Conflict-Sensitive Support Services for Women and Children","Gender-responsive and conflict-sensitive policies / programs / support services for women and children in conflict situations identified and mainstreamed in national government agencies and LGUs in PAMANA provinces",""],[1,"217","7","Gender-Responsive and Conflict-Sensitive Support Services for Women and Children","Gender-responsive and conflict-sensitive policies / programs / support services for women and children in conflict situations identified and mainstreamed in 17 national government agencies and local government units in 43 PAMANA provinces",""],[1,"218","3","Gender Programs for Bangsamoro Women","Gender-related provisions in the FAB will be translated into concrete programs for Bangsamoro women.",""],[1,"218","3","Women’s Participation and Gender Mainstreaming in Peacebuilding","There will also be stronger support in implementing the NAP on related UN Security Council resolutions to increase women participation and incorporate gender perspectives in all peace-building and development efforts.",""],[1,"218","3","Minority Rights and Reconciliation Support","The government will also continue implementing the MRRS",""],[1,"218","3","Child Protection Framework for Armed Conflict","and enhance the comprehensive program framework for the protection of children in situations of armed conflict.",""]],"110":[[1,"82","1","Enforcement Against Substandard Products","There is also a need to step up enforcement activities to prevent proliferation of substandard products in the local market.",""],[1,"89","10","Consumer Protection Expansion and Lemon Law Amendment","Broaden protection of consumers46 and incorporate the Lemon Law through the amendment of the Consumer Act;",""],[1,"93","4","Consumer Protection and Trade Regulation Strengthening","it is important to protect and promote consumer welfare by taking into account consumer satisfaction and intensifying consumer protection and trade regulation.",""],[1,"93","5","Consumer Rights and Redress Information Initiative","The strategy will focus on empowering consumers by informing them of their rights, responsibilities and avenues for redress.",""],[1,"93","6","Market Visibility, Price Monitoring, and Enforcement","the government will increase market visibility through aggressive monitoring and enforcement activities.",""],[1,"93","6","Partnerships with Business, Consumer Groups, LGUs, and NGOs","Complementing these efforts need increased partnership with business and consumer groups, LGUs, and non- government organizations (NGOs).",""],[1,"94","1","Product Standards and Compliance Enforcement","product standards laws, rules and regulations will be strengthened and penalties imposed on violators.",""],[1,"94","1","Market Surveillance and Conformity Assessment Strengthening","Market surveillance activities (e.g. marking of products, declaration of conformity, among others) will be strengthened to push the need for accurate measurements, standards, and accredited conformity assessments.",""],[1,"94","2","Consumer Complaint Resolution and Mediation-Arbitration Enforcement","Consumer complaints will be resolved promptly.",""],[1,"94","2","Consumer Rights Recognition and Retail Self-Regulation Promotion","The government will also continue to recognize establishments that uphold the rights of consumers and sell quality products.",""],[1,"96","2","National Quality Infrastructure Harmonization and Strengthening","The government will harmonize and strengthen the different elements of NQI to be at par with those of ASEAN neighbors.",""]],"111":[[1,"180","9","Transparency Reform Continuation","Reform programs that promote transparency will be continued",""],[1,"180","10","Transparency Seal Compliance Monitoring and Performance-Based Bonus Enforcement","Full compliance by national government agencies (NGAs), government-owned and controlled corporations (GOCCs), and state universities and colleges (SUCs) with the Transparency Seal will be strictly monitored and reinforced through the performance-based bonus (PBB) that includes the Transparency Seal among the eligibility criteria.",""],[1,"180","11","Extractive Industries Transparency Initiative Implementation","With the Philippines' efforts to implement the standards of the Extractive Industries Transparency Initiative, data/information coming from extractive industries on payments they make to the government and where these were used by the government will now be transparent.",""],[1,"181","12","Open Budget Transparency Improvement","This will be done by improving the executive budget proposal and publishing the following documents: Pre-budget Statement, Citizen's Budget for at least two budget phases, Mid-year Review, and Year-end Report.",""],[1,"182","2","Electronic Transparency and Accountability Initiative for Lump Sum Funds","Information on releases for lump-sum funds will continue to be accessible in the website of the Department of Budget and Management (DBM) through the Electronic Transparency and Accountability Initiative for Lump Sum Funds or e-TAILS project.","Department of Budget and Management (DBM)"],[1,"182","2","Online Disclosure of School Building Program and Calamity and Quick Response Fund Releases","Fund releases for the School Building Program and the Calamity and Quick Response Fund are also made available on the website.",""],[1,"182","5","Local Government Full Disclosure Policy Compliance and Monitoring","Regular disclosure of pertinent information to the public and providing citizens with access to this information will be enhanced by ensuring that Memorandum Circular (MC) 2012-141 of the Department of the Interior and Local Government (DILG) entitled \"Full Disclosure of Local Budget and Finances, and Bids and Public Offerings\" is consistently complied with by all local government units (LGUs) and also unfailingly monitored by the agency.","Department of the Interior and Local Government"],[1,"182","5","Barangay Budget Disclosure Requirements","The barangays are also directed to disclose budget-related documents per MC 2010-149 (\"Posting of Barangay Budget, Statement of Income and Expenditures [SIE] and other Barangay Financial Transactions, and Annual Procurement Plan [APP]\").",""],[1,"182","5","Full Disclosure Policy Enforcement through Show Cause Orders","Show cause orders will await LGUs found not complying with the policy.",""],[1,"182","5","Full Disclosure Policy Compliance Target for Local Governments","By 2016, the DILG targets that all provinces, cities, and municipalities (PCMs) are fully compliant with the FDP and that majority of them are able to upload required budget documents in the FDP portal.","Department of the Interior and Local Government"],[1,"334","5","Public Budget Accessibility Publication","A publication that makes the national budget more accessible to the public, both published in print and electronic form.",""],[1,"338","1","Citizen's Charter Feedback and Hidden Cost Survey","The RCS shall also be used to obtain information and/ or estimates of hidden costs incurred by clients to access frontline services which may include, but is not limited to, bribes and payment to fixers.",""],[1,"346","9","Mandatory Online Disclosure of Agency Budget and Procurement Plans","The mandatory disclosure of key budget and major plans of national government agencies (statement of allotment, obligation and balances or SAOB, disbursement and income, procurement plans) in their respective websites under the Seal.",""]],"112":[[1,"69","1","Budget Process Digitalization and Financial Management Systems","the DBM is rolling out technological innovations to speed up budget release and procurement transaction, improve information flows and strengthen transparency and accountability.","DBM"],[1,"69","1","National Payroll System Pilot","the National Payroll System will be pilot-tested in 2014, as well as the Cashless Purchase Cards System in the military.",""],[1,"69","1","Cashless Purchase Cards System in the Military","the National Payroll System will be pilot-tested in 2014, as well as the Cashless Purchase Cards System in the military.",""],[1,"69","4","Public Financial Management Reform Roadmap","The roadmap for Public Financial Management (PFM) reforms will continue to be implemented, part of which includes the adoption of the Treasury Single Account by 2014.",""],[1,"180","9","Performance-Based Budgeting Reform","a new face of the budget that links performance and budget will be adopted",""],[1,"180","9","Performance-Based Budget Submission","Starting 2013, the Executive will submit a performance-based budget",""],[1,"186","5","Public Financial Management Improvement","Improve public financial management;",""],[1,"187","20","GIFMIS Public Financial Management System","The banner program for PFM is the GIFMIS, a tool to assist the government in maintaining fiscal discipline, fund allocation and operations for the effective delivery of government services, as well as in making financial decisions.",""],[1,"188","1","Treasury Single Account Development","the Treasury Single Account is being developed to unify the structure of government bank accounts, enabling consolidation and optimum utilization of cash resources.",""],[1,"192","1","Government Budgeting, Accounting and Auditing Reform","With respect to strengthening internal control systems, the following reforms in government budgeting, accounting and auditing systems will be pursued:",""],[1,"192","2","Rules-Based Public Fund Allocation Reform","Enforcement of a rules-based approach and limiting the scope for discretion in the allocation of public funds;",""],[1,"192","4","Public Sector Accounting Standards Harmonization","Harmonizing the Philippine Public Sector Accounting Standards (PPSAS) with the International Financial Reporting Standards (IFRS) and International Public Sector Accounting Standards (IPSAS).",""],[1,"192","8","Public Sector Accounting Standards Development","COA is also developing new PPSASs as well as an Integrated Results and Risk-Based Auditing Approach System (IRRBAAS).",""]],"113":[[1,"66","16","Medium-Term Debt Management Strategy","3. Formulate medium-term debt management strategy",""],[1,"70","1","Medium-Term Debt Strategy Formulation","a strategic framework will include the formulation of a medium-term debt strategy with cost-risk analysis.",""],[1,"70","1","Domestic Debt Issuance Program","Improvement of the domestic debt market will likewise be supported through the design and implementation of a domestic debt issuance program that produces liquid benchmarks, taking into account factors such as refinancing risk and market needs.",""],[1,"70","1","Investor Base Unification for Secondary Market Support","The DOF, with the Bureau of the Treasury (BTr) will also work for the unification of taxable and non- taxable investors to support the secondary market and reduce distortions on the true interest cost of debt instruments.","DOF | Bureau of the Treasury (BTr)"],[1,"70","2","Contingent Liabilities Management Framework","A framework for managing contingent liabilities will likewise be developed, consisting of regular analysis and quantification of contingent liabilities from all sources including public-private partnership (PPP) projects.",""],[1,"71","6","Reserve Buffer Creation Authority","Authority to create reserve buffers against future risks and contingencies;",""]],"114":[[1,"66","1","Fiscal Consolidation Strategy","it will sustain its strategy on fiscal consolidation, with the growth of revenues outpacing that of disbursements.",""],[1,"66","12","Revenue Enhancement Measures","Implement revenue enhancement measures",""]],"115":[[1,"52","6","Public Spending Efficiency Improvement","The efficiency of public spending also needs to be improved.",""],[1,"52","6","Government Fund Absorption Improvement","The slow absorption of funds of government agencies needs to be addressed",""],[1,"52","6","Revenue Leakage Reduction Measures","the revenue leakages plugged.",""],[1,"52","6","Infrastructure and Social Services Spending Increase","spending on infrastructure and social services needs to increase.",""],[1,"56","3","Public Spending Efficiency and Revenue Collection Reform","the efficiency of public spending and revenue collection needs to be improved.",""],[1,"66","14","Expenditure Management Reforms","Implement expenditure management reforms",""],[1,"68","4","Lump-Sum Budget Elimination Effort","Beginning 2013, the government has intensified efforts to weed out lump- sum budgets.",""],[1,"68","5","Expenditure Management Reform Programme","The government remains committed to the implementation of expenditure management reforms",""],[1,"68","6","Increase Productive Public Expenditure on Infrastructure and Social Services","Expenditure policy will seek to substantially increase productive expenditures especially for infrastructure and social services.",""],[1,"68","7","Budget Rationalization and Appropriations Reform","Beginning 2013, the government has intensified efforts to weed out lump-sum budgets.",""],[1,"68","7","Core Mandate Focus and Service Delivery Acceleration","Line agencies were also directed to focus on their core mandates and accelerate the delivery of services.",""],[1,"69","2","Budget Priorities Framework for Departmental Planning","The decisions and commitments were summarized in a Budget Priorities Framework to guide all departments in strategically planning their activities and crafting their budgets.",""],[1,"69","2","Performance-Informed Budgeting","The 2014 budget also adopts the Performance- informed Budgeting, integrating performance information from the strengthened Organizational Performance Indicator Framework (OPIF) strategy to the National Expenditure Program/General Appropriations Act (GAA).",""],[1,"69","3","General Appropriations Act Budget Release Reform","The greater disaggregation of the budget and the one-year validity of appropriations will pave the way for the implementation of the GAA, which will serve as the Budget Release Document for 2014.",""],[1,"69","5","Open and Participatory Budget Preparation","The budget preparation will be more open and participatory and will engage multi-sectoral stakeholders.",""],[1,"69","5","Expanded Zero-Based Budgeting Review of Major Programs and Projects","The evaluation of existing major programs/ projects, through the Zero-based Budgeting ( ) approach, will be widened in scope.",""],[1,"69","5","OPIF Performance Monitoring and Incentive System","The government's performance in achieving the target outputs and sectoral outcomes will be continuously monitored under the OPIF, where performing institutions will be rewarded under a performance-based incentive system.",""],[1,"69","5","Agency Spending Commitment Compliance Review","Spending commitments of government agencies will be constantly checked, so that prompt, efficient and effective public goods and services will be delivered.",""],[1,"69","7","Open and Participatory Budget Preparation","The budget preparation will be more open and participatory and will engage multi-sectoral stakeholders.",""],[1,"333","14","Budget Allocation Alignment with National Agenda","This will link budget allocation with the national agenda of the government to identify priority areas for spending and to incorporate the sectoral and regional implications in the dimension and distribution of the budget.",""],[1,"349","4","Program and Project Budget Evaluation Framework","A budgeting approach through which major agency programs and projects are evaluated to: (a) determine the continued relevance of program objectives vis-à-vis current developments/directions; (b) assess whether program objectives/outcomes are being achieved; (c) ascertain alternative or more viable ways of achieving the objectives, and ultimately; (d) guide decision makers on whether the program/project should continue to be funded at its present level, or if funding should be increased, reduced or discontinued.",""]],"116":[[1,"179","12","Lawful Tax Collection Reform","collection of taxes in accordance with the law and economic benefits.",""],[1,"197","7","Tax Evasion and Smuggling Enforcement Programs","The government will further intensify the implementation of the Run After Tax Evaders (RATE) and Run After The Smugglers (RATS) programs.","BIR | BOC | DOJ"],[1,"329","3","Performance-Based Transfer and Separation of Revenue Officers","Refers to the transfer in posts and/or separation from government service of internal revenue and customs officers, as well as collection officers of other revenue-generating units, who do not meet their respective revenue or collection goals for the year with all due considerations being taken, in accordance with civil service rules and regulations.",""],[1,"341","13","Revenue Anti-Evasion Investigation and Prosecution Program","A program initiated by the DOF and BIR to investigate and prosecute individuals and/or entities engaged in tax evasion and other criminal violations of the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC) of 1997.","DOF | BIR"]],"117":[[1,"67","11","Customs Modernization and Tariff Act","Other policy and legislative initiatives that will be pursued to support the expansion of fiscal space and to get on a sustainable revenue-and-spending path for the fiscal sector include (a) Customs Modernization and Tariff Act (CMTA);",""],[1,"67","11","Rationalization of the Mining Fiscal Regime","Other policy and legislative initiatives that will be pursued to support the expansion of fiscal space and to get on a sustainable revenue-and-spending path for the fiscal sector include ... (b) rationalization of the mining fiscal regime; and",""],[1,"67","11","Transparency and Accountability in Fiscal Incentives Administration","Other policy and legislative initiatives that will be pursued to support the expansion of fiscal space and to get on a sustainable revenue-and-spending path for the fiscal sector include ... (c) transparency and accountability in the administration and rationalization of fiscal incentives.",""],[1,"89","5","Rationalized Fiscal Incentives Act","Harmonize various incentive-giving laws such as those given by the BOI, PEZA, special economic zones, and other statutes through the Rationalized Fiscal Incentives Act;",""],[1,"89","8","Customs Modernization through Tariff and Customs Code Amendment","Pursue customs modernization by amending the Tariff and Customs Code of the Philippines, consistent with the prescribed standards and recommended practices of the revised Kyoto Convention;",""],[1,"89","9","Large-Scale Metallic Mining Revenue-Sharing Reform","Rationalize revenue-sharing arrangement for large-scale metallic mining operations;",""],[1,"336","12","Fiscal Incentives Reform Initiative","A Fiscal Incentives Reform (FIR) initiative that seeks to institute a strategic approach in the grant of tax incentives that promotes competitiveness and, at the same time, ensures cost-efficiency and fiscal sustainability.",""],[1,"336","14","Mining Fiscal Regime Framework","Refers to the adoption of a fiscal regime framework for the mining industry covering areas such as revenue sharing arrangement, incentives and royalties, as well as the allocation and utilization of mining revenues.",""],[1,"336","14","EITI Entry Support System","Moreover, the government wants to develop a system that will support its entry into the Extractive Industries Transparency Initiative (EITI), the internationally- accepted practice which makes the payment and collection of all mining- related fees and taxes paid by mining companies to national and local government units more transparent through standardized disclosures.",""]],"119":[[1,"6","7","Institutional Change and Innovation for Service Delivery","The government is determined to make the necessary institutional changes and innovations to deliver lasting results that are felt by the people, especially the poor.",""],[1,"48","3","E-Government Master Plan 2013-2016","The e-Government Master Plan 2013-2016 will serve as a blueprint for introducing innovations within government work processes, enhancing administrative productivity and allowing more citizen participation.",""]],"120":[[1,"70","6","Central Bank Regional and International Cooperation Participation","The BSP will continue to actively participate in regional and international cooperation programs to improve its capability to undertake economic surveillance and help generate quality outputs that would contribute to informed formulation of policies supportive of the regional integration and cooperation framework.",""],[1,"71","1","IMF Crisis-Fighting Fund Contribution","the BSP's US$1-billion commitment to the International Monetary Fund's (IMF) crisis-fighting fund pool",""],[1,"71","1","IMF New Arrangements to Borrow Contribution","its US$500-million pledge contribution to the IMF's expanded New Arrangements to Borrow (NAB) program",""],[1,"71","10","Participation in IMF Financial Safety Net Facilities","The pledge from the Philippines to the IMF's NAB program is on top of the country's $251.5-million contribution to the Financial Transactions Plan (FTP), another lending facility of the IMF.",""]],"121":[[1,"135","4","Microinsurance Product Development","Encourage development of new, relevant and innovative microinsurance products, especially those that will address multiple risks, including non- traditional ones such as index-based and parametric insurance products;",""],[1,"135","5","Microinsurance Advocacy Campaign","Continue advocacy campaign for microinsurance to reach out to the rest of the 23 million Filipinos who are living below the poverty line;",""]],"122":[[1,"87","1","Tourism Development Priority Program","Tourism development will be a priority program of the government.",""],[1,"87","2","Strategic Tourism Products Development and Support","Strategic tourism products will be developed and supported in the following top nine tourism cluster destinations to expand visitor's expenditure and length of stay: Central Visayas; Metro Manila and CALABARZON; Central Luzon; Palawan; Western Visayas; Davao Gulf and Coast; Cagayan de Oro, Island and Hinterland; Bicol; and Laoag-Vigan.",""],[1,"87","2","Tourism Product Diversification Initiative","These products include medical and retirement tourism; leisure and entertainment; meetings, incentives, conventions and exhibitions; cruise and nautical tourism; education tourism; and agri-tourism.",""],[1,"87","2","Business Traveler Tourism Promotion","Business travelers will be encouraged to tour the country while looking for investment opportunities.",""],[1,"95","7","ASEAN Tourism Market Collaboration","Greater collaboration with ASEAN member states will be undertaken to realize the potential of the ASEAN as a source market for tourism.",""],[1,"95","7","Tour Program Development Through Twinning and Dual Arrangements","Tour programs will be developed through twinning and dual",""],[1,"95","8","ASEAN Tourism Market Collaboration","Greater collaboration with ASEAN member states will be undertaken to realize the potential of the ASEAN as a source market for tourism.",""]],"123":[[1,"89","11","Labor Code Amendment for Industrial Modernization","Increase labor mobilization and gradually shift industries to technology-driven processes, among others, through the amendment of the Labor Code;",""],[1,"90","4","Mutually Agreed Work Arrangements Support","Mutually agreed-upon work arrangements, which are consistent with the promotion of employment and protection of basic rights of workers, as well as increased efficiency and streamlined operations, will be supported.",""],[1,"90","4","Two-Tiered Wage System","The two-tiered wage system, which seeks to balance interests of workers and employers, will be implemented.",""],[1,"90","5","Voluntary Codes of Good Practices for Industrial Labor Relations","The government will continue to push for the development of Voluntary Codes of Good Practices in industries to transform a traditionally litigious labor relations system to one that incorporates the tenets of social dialogue.",""],[1,"90","5","Single Entry Approach Program for Labor Dispute Mediation","The Single Entry Approach Program (SEnA), which is 30-day mandatory conciliation- mediation approach, will be promoted as a means to \"de-judicialize\" dispute settlement procedures.",""]],"124":[[1,"85","10","Supply Chain Improvement for Basic and Prime Commodities","Improve supply chains of basic and prime commodities",""],[1,"95","1","Basic Necessities and Prime Commodities Supply Assurance Programs","The government through the DTI will continue to implement various programs to ensure affordability and supply of basic necessities and prime commodities, especially during crisis.","DTI"],[1,"95","1","Supply Chain Bottleneck Review and Efficiency Improvement","The government and the private sector will work together in undertaking an in-depth review of the supply chain to determine major bottlenecks and identify effective points of interventions to make enhancements and eliminate inefficiencies.",""],[1,"95","1","Transport and Distribution Infrastructure Support Enhancement","The government will also strengthen infrastructure support and logistics mechanisms to improve efficiency in transport and distribution system, hence, reducing cost in bringing goods and services to the market.",""]],"125":[[1,"86","1","Integrated Coconut Industry and Poverty Reduction Roadmap","For the coconut sector, the Integrated Coconut Industry and Poverty Reduction Roadmap will be implemented.",""],[1,"123","1","Integrated Coconut Industry Poverty Reduction Roadmap","The Integrated Coconut Industry Poverty Reduction Roadmap is a program designed to alleviate poverty and develop the coconut industry.",""],[1,"123","2","Market Participation Measures for Coconut Farmers","Poverty reduction through market participation measures will be more applicable for coconut farmers who have secured land.",""],[1,"123","2","Social Protection for Coconut Farmers in Transition","social protection strategy will be geared towards attenuating the risks and costs that poor coconut farmers will bear during their transition from subsistence production to market integration.",""]],"126":[[1,"125","2","NFA Reorganization and Rice Import Permit Reform","The NFA Reorganization Act will further rationalize grains-sector trading.",""],[1,"125","3","National Food Authority Reorganization and Grains Trading Rationalization","The National Food Authority Reorganization Act will further rationalize grains-sector trading.",""]],"127":[[1,"116","25","Anti-Smuggling Campaign","Conduct and aggresive anti-smuggling campain",""],[1,"116","27","Legislative Action Promotion and Enhancement","Promote the passage and enhancement of key legislative actions",""],[1,"123","6","Anti-Smuggling Campaign and Oversight Mechanism","In order to address this issue, an aggressive campaign against smuggling, including an effective oversight mechanism, is needed.",""],[1,"124","1","Ongoing Review and Update of Laws and Policies","A review of laws and policies will be a continuing activity to ensure the responsiveness of such issuances to current developments in the sector.",""]],"128":[[1,"183","5","Voter Education Enhancement","· Enhance voter's education.",""],[1,"185","1","Voter Education and Electoral Information Campaign","The Commission on Elections (COMELEC) will continue to harness various media (e.g. print, voice and electronic, etc.) in educating the public about the electoral reforms and activities of the Commission, as well as its stand on various political issues.","Commission on Elections (COMELEC)"],[1,"185","1","Automated Election System Public Awareness and Demonstration Campaign","The COMELEC will also aim to increase understanding and appreciation of the benefits of the automated election system and provide alternative sources of information which may be accessed with greater ease.","Commission on Elections (COMELEC)"],[1,"185","1","Public Demonstrations on PCOS Machines","It will conduct public demonstrations on the Precinct Count Optical Scan (PCOS) machines for special interest groups, walk-ins, and the general public.","Commission on Elections (COMELEC)"],[1,"185","1","Overseas Filipino Voter Registration and Turnout Campaign","Furthermore, to increase voter registration and turnout for the next national elections, COMELEC will partner with CSOs in countries with high concentration of overseas Filipinos (OFs) in conducting sustained information dissemination campaigns, especially on the Overseas Voting Act of 2013 (RA 10590), to encourage OFs to register and cast their votes in the 2016 and future national elections.","Commission on Elections (COMELEC)"]],"129":[[1,"179","12","Commercial Dispute Resolution and Property Rights Enforcement","just and efficient resolution of commercial disputes, including contractual obligations and property rights;",""],[1,"197","6","Full Implementation of EO 78 on ADR in Public-Private Contracts","EO 78, which mandates the inclusion of ADR in contracts involving public- private partnerships (PPPs), build-operate and transfer (BOT) projects, and joint venture agreements between the government and private entities, will be fully implemented.",""],[1,"197","6","ADR Information Campaign and Promotion for Commercial Disputes","The DOJ-Office of ADR will proceed with information campaigns on the said policy and promote ADR in resolving commercial/contractual disputes outside the court system.","DOJ-Office of ADR"],[1,"197","6","Consistency of Legal Opinions on Government Contracts","The DOJ will also work on ensuring the consistency of legal opinions and advice on government contracts, and engage the SC in policy dialogues to resolve concerns on statutory interpretation and contract enforcement.","DOJ | SC"],[1,"197","6","Judicial Case Decongestion and Jurisprudence Consistency Measures","The judiciary, for its part, will address efficiency concerns on commercial dispute resolution through its efforts on case decongestion and consistency of jurisprudence.","judiciary"]],"130":[[1,"217","14","Quick Response Team for Indigenous Peoples Human Rights Violations","100 Quick Response Team for Indigenous Peoples Human Rights Violations capacitated and institutionalized in all Indigenous Peoples ethnographic regions",""],[1,"218","4","Indigenous Peoples Rights Support Measures","The government will also support indigenous peoples' (IPs) agenda by: (a) professionalizing the service bureaucracy; (b) strengthening processes towards full recognition of certificates of ancestral domain titles; (c) establishing mechanisms to protect IP rights; (d) complying with the International Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Racial Discrimination and the Convention of the Rights of the Child; and (e) ratifying International Labour Organization (ILO) Convention No. 169, or the Convention on Indigenous and Tribal Peoples.",""],[1,"218","5","Multi-sectoral and Multi-stakeholder Partnership Mechanism for Human Rights Enforcement","Conscious efforts to forge multi-sectoral and multi-stakeholder partnerships will be pursued to further strengthen mechanisms to end impunity, enforced disappearances, torture and other grave human rights violations.",""]],"131":[[1,"214","23","Bangsamoro Development Assistance Fund and Tripartite Implementation Monitoring Committee","Terms of Reference on Bangsamoro Development Assistance Fund and Tripartite Implementation Monitoring Committee agreed upon during the meetings of the Expert Working Groups composed of representatives",""],[1,"218","6","Halal Industry Development Support","Strong support will be provided to ARMM and the National Commission on Muslim Filipinos towards the development of the Halal industry","ARMM | National Commission on Muslim Filipinos"],[1,"218","6","Hajj Management System Institutionalization","institutionalization of the Hajj Management system",""],[1,"218","6","Islamic Finance Framework Development","establishment of a framework for Islamic finance",""],[1,"218","6","Shari'ah Courts System Strengthening","strengthening the Shari'ah Courts System",""],[1,"218","6","Land Use Policy Rationalization","The government will pursue efforts to rationalize land use policies",""]],"132":[[1,"212","5","Philippine Defense Reform and Transformation Programs","The Department of National Defense's (DND) Philippine Defense Reform and the Philippine Defense Transformation Programs and the PNP's Integrated Transformation Program Performance Governance System (ITP-PGS) are other initiatives meant to achieve the highest standards of personnel integrity and professional competence in the security sector.","Department of National Defense"],[1,"212","5","Integrated Transformation Program Performance Governance System","The Department of National Defense's (DND) Philippine Defense Reform and the Philippine Defense Transformation Programs and the PNP's Integrated Transformation Program Performance Governance System (ITP-PGS) are other initiatives meant to achieve the highest standards of personnel integrity and professional competence in the security sector.",""],[1,"222","1","Security Sector Reorganization and Retooling","Agencies under the security sector will undergo reorganization, retooling, and reorientation to keep up with the constantly changing policy and security strategy environment.",""],[1,"222","1","Continuing Human Rights and Cultural Sensitivity Training for Security Personnel","All officers, both commissioned and non-commissioned, as well as civilian employees will undergo continuing training on human rights, international law, and cultural sensitivity.",""],[1,"222","2","Security Forces Rationalization and Integration Reform","The government will continue its reforms as laid out in the DND's Philippine Defense Transformation Program and the PNP's ITP-PGS, to rationalize and integrate security forces (government and civilian/public and private) to address threats and challenges against peace.","DND | PNP"],[1,"222","2","Local Government Peace and Order Capacity Building","Capacity-building efforts of LGUs in managing peace and order concerns will be supported, alongside the broadening of the peace constituency by partnering with local and national civil society groups and the private sector.",""],[1,"222","2","Peace Constituency Expansion Partnership Initiative","Capacity-building efforts of LGUs in managing peace and order concerns will be supported, alongside the broadening of the peace constituency by partnering with local and national civil society groups and the private sector.",""]],"133":[[1,"222","5","Rights of IDPs Act","Rights of IDPs Act, providing protection for IDPs during and after armed conflicts, natural calamities, aggressive implementation of development projects, and other related matters;",""],[1,"222","6","Child Protection in Armed Conflict","Protection of children in situations of armed conflict, providing protection to children in situations of armed conflict as guaranteed under the Convention of the Rights of the Child, its Optional Protocol on the Involvement of Children in Armed Conflict and all other core human rights treaties.",""],[1,"226","14","Former Rebel Information System Development","A Former Rebel Information System (FRIS) is currently being developed as a means to monitor this specific indicator.",""],[1,"228","2","Gender-Responsive and Conflict-Sensitive Support Services for Women and Children","Gender-responsive and conflict-sensitive policies/ programs/ support services for women and children in conflict situations identified and mainstreamed in national government agencies and LGUs in PAMANA provinces",""]],"134":[[1,"227","14","Third-Party Monitoring System","Third party monitoring; (b) Web posting; (c) Project and community billboards; (d) Performance- based fund releases; and (d) Grievance Redress System",""],[1,"227","14","Web Posting for Project Information","Third party monitoring; (b) Web posting; (c) Project and community billboards; (d) Performance- based fund releases; and (d) Grievance Redress System",""],[1,"227","14","Project and Community Billboard Disclosure","Third party monitoring; (b) Web posting; (c) Project and community billboards; (d) Performance- based fund releases; and (d) Grievance Redress System",""],[1,"227","14","Performance-Based Fund Release Mechanism","Third party monitoring; (b) Web posting; (c) Project and community billboards; (d) Performance- based fund releases; and (d) Grievance Redress System",""],[1,"227","14","Grievance Redress System","Third party monitoring; (b) Web posting; (c) Project and community billboards; (d) Performance- based fund releases; and (d) Grievance Redress System",""]],"135":[[1,"243","10","Access to Innovative Financing Schemes for Climate Change Adaptation/Mitigation and Disaster Risk Reduction and Management","Improve access to innovative national and international financing schemes for CCA/M and DRRM",""],[1,"245","1","Operationalization of the People's Survival Fund","At the local level, there is a need to operationalize the PSF to provide additional financing source to support adaptation activities of LGUs and communities.",""],[1,"245","1","Climate Change Tagging Criteria Development","Priority activities to support the operationalization of PSF are formulation of climate change-tagging criteria, finalization and approval of the IRR of RA 10174, and preparation of the operational guidelines for the PSF.",""],[1,"245","1","Approval of PSF Implementing Rules and Operational Guidelines","Priority activities to support the operationalization of PSF are formulation of climate change-tagging criteria, finalization and approval of the IRR of RA 10174, and preparation of the operational guidelines for the PSF.",""],[1,"245","1","Revision of National Disaster Risk Reduction Fund Access Mechanism","On the other hand, there is a need to revisit the mechanism to access the NDRRMF to ensure that it will not only be used for relief assistance, rehabilitation and reconstruction activities but also for disaster preparedness and prevention measures.",""],[1,"245","2","Climate Adaptation and Disaster Risk Management Package","Among the priority activities for funding include adaptation measures, forecasting and early warning system, institutional strengthening, knowledge management and risk financing.",""],[1,"245","5","People's Survival Fund Operationalization","There is a need to operationalize the people's survival fund to provide additional financing source to support adaptation activities of LGUs and communities.",""],[1,"251","3","Carbon Credits and Ecosystem Services Financing Mechanism","To provide adequate and sustainable financing for ENR management, there is a need to institutionalize carbon credits and payments for ecosystems services and resource valuation techniques, such as user fees and economic rent for use of natural resources.",""],[1,"251","4","Carbon Credits and Ecosystem Services Payments Institutionalization","There is a need to institutionalize carbon credits and payments for ecosystems services and resource valuation techniques.",""]],"136":[[1,"238","1","Abandoned Mine Rehabilitation and Risk Assessment Programme","the government targets the full rehabilitation of Bagacay and completion of risk assessment of five abandoned mine sites by 2016.",""],[1,"248","14","Abandoned Mine Rehabilitation and Protection Programme","The 22 abandoned mines remain a priority for rehabilitation and protection.",""],[1,"251","1","Mine Rehabilitation Compliance and Funding Requirements","To facilitate the full rehabilitation of the mined-out areas, the government will strictly require mining companies of the following: (a) submission of Environmental Work Program, Environmental Protection and Enhancement Program, and Final Mine Rehabilitation and Decommissioning Program; (b) conduct of environmental monitoring and audit, including final mine rehabilitation, de-commissioning and multi-partite monitoring; and (c) contribution to the Contingent Liability and Rehabilitation Fund and payment of mine wastes and tailings fee.",""],[1,"318","6","Environmental Compliance Certification and Environmental Management Plan Implementation","A document issued by the DENR Secretary or the Regional Executive Director certifying that based on the representations of the proponent and the preparers, as reviewed and validated by the EIARC, the proposed project or undertaking will not cause a significant negative environmental impact; that the proponent has complied with all the requirements of the EIS System and that the proponent is committed to implement its approved Environmental Management Plan in the Environmental Impact Statement or mitigation measures in the Initial Environmental Examination.","DENR Secretary | Regional Executive Director | EIARC"]],"137":[[1,"237","3","Fast-Track Residential Patent Distribution","However, there is a need to fast-track the distribution of residential patent to achieve its 2016 target of 516,064 patents.",""],[1,"248","4","Sustainable Land Management Project Support in Land Degradation Hotspots","Adequate financial and institutional support is provided, particularly in the development of SLM projects within land degradation hotspots.",""],[1,"248","4","Harmonization of Land Administration and Management Policies","Land administration, distribution and management-related policies are harmonized.",""],[1,"250","5","Cadastral Survey Completion","Activities will include: (a) completing cadastral surveys in cities and municipalities;",""],[1,"250","5","Agricultural, Residential, and Ancestral Land Titling Acceleration","accelerating titling of agricultural, residential and ancestral lands in partnership with DAR, NCIP, Land Registration Authority, and LGUs;","DAR | NCIP | Land Registration Authority | LGUs"],[1,"250","5","Campaign Against Fake Land Titles","intensifying campaign against the proliferation of fake land titles;",""],[1,"250","5","Land Resources and Cadastral Information Computerization","computerization of land resources and cadastral information management;",""],[1,"250","5","Land Administration and Management Reform Integration","integrating the guiding principles of the Land Sector Development Framework in the implementation of land administration and management reforms.",""],[1,"258","1","Land Administration and Management Reform","This will reform the present land administration and management system by consolidating agencies into a single body responsible for survey, mapping, titling, registration, title transfer and public land management.",""],[1,"258","1","Interagency Committee on Land Management and Rural Development","The creation of the Interagency Committee on Institutional Arrangements for Land Management and Rural Development (Administrative Order 34, s. 2012) is a step forward in recognizing the need to improve institutional arrangements among agencies, particularly DAR whose redistribution function will be completed by 2014;",""],[1,"260","2","Interagency Coordination and Monitoring Committees for Plan Implementation","the two interagency committees under the NEDA Board-the National Land Use Committee (NLUC) and the Regional Development Committee (RDCOM)-will oversee the coordination of the sector deliverables.",""],[1,"284","13","National Land Use and Management Law","Enactment of law on national land use and management",""]],"138":[[1,"248","9","Support for CADT, CALT, and ADSDPP Issuance","Support initiatives that guide and facilitate the issuance of CADTs and CALTs and formulation of ADSDPPs are provided.",""],[1,"257","2","Security of Tenure in Upland and Coastal Areas","provision of security of tenure in upland and coastal areas;",""],[1,"257","2","Recognition of Indigenous Peoples' Ancestral Domain Rights","recognition of IPs' rights to their ancestral domain;",""],[1,"307","3","Ancestral Domain Sustainable Management and Development Plan","A plan that embodies the goals and objectives, policies and strategies of ICCs/ IPs for the sustainable management and development of their ancestral domain and all resources therein including the human and cultural resources such as their Indigenous Knowledge Systems and Practices (IKSPs).",""],[1,"311","6","Ancestral Domain Land Titling for Indigenous Communities","A title formally recognizing the rights of possession and Domain ownership of indigenous people and communities over their ancestral domains identified and delineated in accordance with this law; Land titles given to tribal communities in asserting their right on the protection and sustainable utilization of their ancestral domain areas.",""],[1,"311","8","Recognition of Ancestral Land Rights Title Issuance","A title formally recognizing the rights of indigenous people and communities over their ancestral lands identified and delineated in accordance with RA 8371.",""]],"139":[[1,"278","3","Digital Terrestrial Television Broadcasting Migration Plan","Digital Terrestrial Television Broadcasting Migration Plan, to prepare the Philippines' switchover from analogue to digital signaling broadcast system.",""],[1,"284","7","Strengthening of the National Telecommunications Commission as Independent ICT Regulator","Strengthening of National Telecommunications Commission as the independent regulator of the ICT sector",""],[1,"284","8","Converging Technologies Enabling Law","Enactment of law enabling an atmosphere for converging technologies brought about by enhancements in the ICT sector",""],[1,"287","11","Philippine Radio Frequency Management System","The Philippine Radio Frequency Management System will provide greater efficiency in facilitating increasing demand for radio frequencies and other wireless communications services.",""],[1,"288","1","Philippine ICT Statistics Portal Enhancement","the government will further enhance the Philippine ICT Statistics Portal, as well as other government websites in the energy subsector",""]],"140":[[1,"324","9","High Value Crops Development Program","these commodities are covered by the DA Agrikulturang Pinoy - High Value Crops Development Program.","DA"]],"141":[[1,"306","15","Parallel Learning System","A parallel learning system aimed to provide a viable alternative to the existing formal education instruction.",""],[1,"319","11","Certification Mechanism for Non-School-Based Learning","A certification mechanism for non-school based learning that is integrated into the country's educational system through the EO 330.",""]],"142":[[1,"319","6","National Biosafety Framework Establishment","An order establishing the National Biosafety Framework, which aims to strengthen the existing science-based determination of biosafety to ensure the safe and responsible use of modern biotechnology, enhance decision-making, and guide implementation of international obligations on biosafety.",""],[1,"323","8","Green ICT Sustainability Measures","An approach to ensuring environmental sustainability of ICTs in businesses and organizations.",""]],"143":[[1,"338","7","Governance Commission for Government-Owned and Controlled Corporations Implementation","The Governance Commission for Government- Owned and Controlled Corporations or the GCG was created for purposes of its implementation.",""]],"144":[[1,"338","15","Countryside and Barangay Business Enterprise Incentive Law","A law that aims to promote growth of countryside and barangay business enterprises by minimizing bureaucratic restrictions and granting incentives and other benefits.",""]],"145":[[1,"339","9","Indigenous Peoples Rights Protection Act","An act which recognizes, protects and promotes the rights of indigenous cultural communities/indigenous people, creating a national commission of indigenous people, establishing implementing mechanism, appropriating funds therefore, and for other purposes.",""]],"146":[[1,"340","12","Environmental Education and Public Awareness Legislation","An act to promote national awareness on the role of natural resources in economic growth and the importance of environmental conservation and ecological balance towards sustained national development.",""]]}});